window.LEVEL_DATA = window.LEVEL_DATA || {};
window.LEVEL_DATA["C2"] = {"st-01":{"intro":"Deneyimli bir sektör oyuncusuna girişimini akıcı, esprili ve kendinden emin bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"Give me the elevator pitch: what is it you're actually building?","tr":"Bana kısa tanıtımını yap: tam olarak ne inşa ediyorsunuz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The short version is that we've built an autonomous audiometer: a hearing test that, for all intents and purposes, runs itself.","tr":"Kısa versiyonu şu: otonom bir odyometre geliştirdik; yani pratikte kendi kendini yürüten bir işitme testi."},{"who":"Me","en":"The patient presses a button when they hear a tone, the AI adapts on the fly, and within ten minutes you have a full audiogram.","tr":"Hasta bir ton duyduğunda düğmeye basıyor, yapay zekâ anında uyum sağlıyor ve on dakika içinde elinizde eksiksiz bir odyogram oluyor."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Hearing tests are hardly a new idea, though.","tr":"Ama işitme testi pek de yeni bir fikir sayılmaz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Fair point, but the test was never really the problem; access is.","tr":"Haklısın, ama sorun hiçbir zaman testin kendisi değildi; sorun erişim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Something like one in five people lives with some degree of hearing loss, and the vast majority are never tested, simply because there aren't enough audiologists to go round.","tr":"Aşağı yukarı her beş kişiden biri bir dereceye kadar işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor ve büyük çoğunluk, sırf herkese yetecek kadar odyolog olmadığı için hiç test edilmiyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Outside the big cities, a months-long wait for an appointment is par for the course.","tr":"Büyük şehirlerin dışında randevu için aylarca beklemek olağan bir durum."},{"who":"Partner","en":"And I take it there's a market willing to pay for that?","tr":"Ve sanırım bunun için para ödemeye hazır bir pazar var?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Admittedly, five paying customers is a modest start, but it's proof that clinics will actually pay rather than just nod politely at a demo.","tr":"Kabul etmek gerekir ki beş ücretli müşteri mütevazı bir başlangıç, ama kliniklerin bir demoda kibarca başını sallamakla kalmayıp gerçekten para ödediğinin kanıtı."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're a team of six, three engineers, a doctor and two of us on the commercial side, so our bandwidth is, shall we say, finite.","tr":"Altı kişilik bir ekibiz; üç mühendis, bir doktor ve ticari tarafta iki kişi, yani kapasitemiz, nasıl desem, sınırlı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, what we lack in headcount we make up for in focus.","tr":"Yine de kişi sayısındaki eksikliğimizi odaklanmayla telafi ediyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Which brings me to why I wanted to talk: we'd make far more headway in Europe with a partner who already knows the terrain than we ever would on our own.","tr":"Bu da beni konuşmak isteme nedenime getiriyor: Avrupa'da sahayı zaten tanıyan bir ortakla, tek başımıza olabileceğimizden çok daha fazla yol alırız."}],"vocab":[{"en":"elevator pitch","tr":"çok kısa tanıtım konuşması","ex":"Give me the elevator pitch.","def":"a very short summary of a business, short enough for a lift ride"},{"en":"for all intents and purposes","tr":"pratikte, fiilen","ex":"The test, for all intents and purposes, runs itself.","def":"in every way that really matters"},{"en":"on the fly","tr":"anında, o anda","ex":"The AI adapts on the fly.","def":"while something is happening, without stopping"},{"en":"go round","tr":"herkese yetmek","ex":"There aren't enough audiologists to go round.","def":"to be enough for everyone who needs it"},{"en":"par for the course","tr":"olağan, beklenen durum","ex":"A months-long wait is par for the course.","def":"normal and expected, usually in a negative way"},{"en":"a modest start","tr":"mütevazı bir başlangıç","ex":"Five paying customers is a modest start.","def":"a small but real beginning"},{"en":"bandwidth","tr":"kapasite (zaman ve enerji)","ex":"Our bandwidth is, shall we say, finite.","def":"the time and energy a person or team has available"},{"en":"make up for","tr":"telafi etmek","ex":"What we lack in headcount we make up for in focus.","def":"to balance a weakness with a strength"},{"en":"make headway","tr":"yol almak, ilerleme kaydetmek","ex":"We'd make far more headway with a partner.","def":"to make progress, especially when it is difficult"},{"en":"know the terrain","tr":"sahayı tanımak","ex":"We need a partner who already knows the terrain.","def":"to understand a market or situation well"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging and understatement","tr":"Akıcı konuşanlar güçlü bir iddiayı yumuşatmak ya da ince bir ironi katmak için 'admittedly', 'shall we say', 'something like' gibi ifadeler kullanır. Bu, kendinden emin ama abartısız bir izlenim bırakır.","examples":["Admittedly, five paying customers is a modest start.","Our bandwidth is, shall we say, finite.","Something like one in five people lives with some degree of hearing loss."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the speaker, what is the real problem?","options":["The quality of existing hearing tests","Access to testing, because there are too few audiologists","The price of headphones"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of 'our bandwidth is, shall we say, finite'?","options":["Wry understatement about how stretched the team is","An angry complaint about the engineers","A formal technical description"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker say 'rather than just nod politely at a demo'?","options":["To criticise their own customers","To suggest demos are a waste of time","To show that interest has turned into real money"],"a":2},{"q":"How does the speaker respond to 'Hearing tests are hardly a new idea'?","options":["They get defensive and change the subject","They concede the point and reframe the problem","They ignore the comment"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the final line imply about the listener?","options":["The speaker wants them to invest money","The speaker wants to hire them as an engineer","The speaker sees them as a possible partner who knows the European market"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"The AI adapts on the ___.","a":"fly","hint":"anında"},{"s":"There aren't enough audiologists to go ___.","a":"round","hint":"herkese yetecek kadar"},{"s":"A months-long wait is par for the ___.","a":"course","hint":"olağan durum"},{"s":"We'd make far more ___ with a partner who knows the terrain.","a":"headway","hint":"ilerleme, yol"}],"order":[{"a":"The test was never really the problem."},{"a":"Five paying customers is a modest start."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kabul etmek gerekir ki beş müşteri mütevazı bir başlangıç.","en":"Admittedly, five customers is a modest start.","keys":["admittedly","modest start"]},{"tr":"Asıl sorun test değil, erişim.","en":"The real problem isn't the test; it's access.","keys":["isn't the test","access"]},{"tr":"Sahayı tanıyan bir ortakla çok daha fazla yol alırız.","en":"We'd make far more headway with a partner who knows the terrain.","keys":["headway","knows the terrain"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Potential partner","personaTr":"Olası iş ortağı","scene":"Berlin'deki bir sağlık teknolojisi konferansında, Almanya'da büyük bir klinik zinciri yöneten deneyimli biriyle kahve içiyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Give me the elevator pitch: what is it you're actually building?","aiTr":"Bana kısa tanıtımını yap: tam olarak ne inşa ediyorsunuz?","hint":"The short version is that we've built an autonomous audiometer, a hearing test that, for all intents and purposes, runs itself.","keys":["autonomous audiometer","runs itself","short version"]},{"ai":"Hearing tests are hardly a new idea, though, are they?","aiTr":"Ama işitme testleri pek yeni bir fikir değil, değil mi?","hint":"Fair point, but the test was never really the problem; access is, because there aren't enough audiologists to go round.","keys":["access","go round","fair point"]},{"ai":"And is anyone actually paying, or is it all pilots and goodwill at this stage?","aiTr":"Peki gerçekten para ödeyen var mı, yoksa bu aşamada her şey pilot projeler ve iyi niyetten mi ibaret?","hint":"Admittedly, five paying customers is a modest start, but it's proof that clinics will actually pay rather than just nod politely.","keys":["paying customers","modest start","proof"]},{"ai":"So where would someone like me fit in?","aiTr":"Peki benim gibi biri bu resmin neresinde?","hint":"We'd make far more headway in Europe with a partner who already knows the terrain than we ever would on our own.","keys":["headway","partner","terrain"]}]}},"ai-01":{"intro":"Cihazının mantığını, uzman bir doktora zarif ve akıcı bir dille, kendinden emin ama ölçülü anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Strip away the jargon and an audiometer answers a deceptively simple question: how quietly can a sound be played before this person stops hearing it?","tr":"Jargonu bir kenara bırakırsanız, odyometre aldatıcı derecede basit bir soruyu yanıtlar: bir ses ne kadar kısık çalındığında bu kişi onu duymayı bırakır?"},{"en":"Answering it properly has traditionally required an audiologist, a soundproofed booth and the best part of half an hour, which is precisely why so few people get tested.","tr":"Bu soruyu doğru yanıtlamak geleneksel olarak bir odyolog, ses yalıtımlı bir kabin ve neredeyse yarım saat gerektirmiştir; işte bu yüzden çok az insan test yaptırır."},{"en":"Our device does away with the first of those and most of the last.","tr":"Bizim cihazımız bunlardan ilkini tamamen, sonuncusunun da büyük kısmını ortadan kaldırıyor."},{"en":"The patient puts on the headphones, follows the prompts on screen and presses a button each time a tone registers.","tr":"Hasta kulaklıkları takar, ekrandaki yönergeleri izler ve bir tonu her algıladığında bir düğmeye basar."},{"en":"Behind that unassuming routine, the AI is weighing every response and deciding, in real time, which tone is most worth playing next.","tr":"Bu sıradan görünen rutinin arkasında yapay zekâ her yanıtı tartar ve sırada hangi tonun çalınmaya en değer olduğuna gerçek zamanlı olarak karar verir."},{"en":"The upshot is a test that converges on the patient's thresholds rather than plodding through a fixed protocol.","tr":"Sonuç, sabit bir protokolü ağır ağır izlemek yerine hastanın işitme eşiklerine hızla yaklaşan bir testtir."},{"en":"In under ten minutes, the device has produced an audiogram that a clinician can read at a glance, without an expert having had to sit in the room.","tr":"On dakikadan kısa bir sürede cihaz, bir klinisyenin bir bakışta okuyabileceği bir odyogram üretmiş olur; üstelik odada bir uzmanın oturmasına gerek kalmadan."},{"en":"None of this, I should stress, is about writing audiologists out of the story.","tr":"Şunu özellikle vurgulamalıyım: bunların hiçbiri odyologları hikâyeden çıkarmakla ilgili değil."},{"en":"If anything, it is about reserving their expertise for the patients who genuinely need it.","tr":"Aksine, mesele onların uzmanlığını gerçekten ihtiyaç duyan hastalara ayırmak."},{"en":"Equally deliberate was the decision to run the AI on the device rather than in the cloud.","tr":"Yapay zekâyı bulutta değil, cihazın üzerinde çalıştırma kararı da aynı derecede bilinçliydi."},{"en":"Patient data never leaves the room, and a clinic with temperamental Wi-Fi loses nothing in the process.","tr":"Hasta verileri odadan hiç çıkmaz ve Wi-Fi'ı nazlı bir klinik bu süreçte hiçbir şey kaybetmez."},{"en":"Software updates arrive roughly once a month, so the device you install today should be quietly sharper a year from now.","tr":"Yazılım güncellemeleri yaklaşık ayda bir gelir; böylece bugün kurduğunuz cihaz bir yıl sonra sessiz sedasız daha keskin olur."}],"vocab":[{"en":"strip away the jargon","tr":"jargonu bir kenara bırakmak","ex":"Strip away the jargon and the idea is simple.","def":"to remove technical language so the main idea is clear"},{"en":"deceptively simple","tr":"aldatıcı derecede basit","ex":"It answers a deceptively simple question.","def":"seeming simple but actually more complex"},{"en":"do away with","tr":"ortadan kaldırmak","ex":"Our device does away with the need for an expert in the room.","def":"to remove or get rid of something"},{"en":"unassuming","tr":"gösterişsiz, sıradan görünen","ex":"Behind that unassuming routine, the AI is working hard.","def":"modest and not attracting attention"},{"en":"the upshot","tr":"sonuç, netice","ex":"The upshot is a much shorter test.","def":"the final result of a process"},{"en":"converge on","tr":"...e yakınsamak, hızla yaklaşmak","ex":"The test converges on the patient's thresholds.","def":"to move towards one point from different directions"},{"en":"plod through","tr":"ağır ağır ilerlemek","ex":"Standard tests plod through a fixed protocol.","def":"to do something slowly and without imagination"},{"en":"at a glance","tr":"bir bakışta","ex":"A clinician can read the audiogram at a glance.","def":"immediately, with only a quick look"},{"en":"write someone out of the story","tr":"birini hikâyeden çıkarmak, devre dışı bırakmak","ex":"We are not writing audiologists out of the story.","def":"to remove someone from a role or situation"},{"en":"temperamental","tr":"nazlı, güvenilmez (cihaz)","ex":"The clinic's Wi-Fi is temperamental.","def":"not working reliably; often failing"}],"grammar":{"title":"Emphasis and hedging: I should stress, if anything, should","tr":"C2'de vurgu ve yumuşatmayı birlikte kullanırsın. 'I should stress' önemli bir noktayı öne çıkarır, 'if anything' beklenenin tersini nazikçe söyler, 'should be quietly sharper' iddiayı abartmadan yapar.","examples":["None of this, I should stress, is about writing audiologists out of the story.","If anything, it is about reserving their expertise for the patients who need it.","The device you install today should be quietly sharper a year from now."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'Our device does away with the first of those and most of the last' mean?","options":["It removes the need for a soundproofed booth","It removes the need for an audiologist and saves most of the time","It makes the test longer but cheaper"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the AI choose the next tone?","options":["It follows a fixed protocol","It lets the clinician decide","It weighs each response and picks the most useful tone"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the purpose of 'None of this, I should stress, ...'?","options":["To reassure audiologists that they are not being replaced","To criticise audiologists","To admit a weakness in the product"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'a clinic with temperamental Wi-Fi loses nothing' imply?","options":["Clinics need fast internet to use it","The company provides Wi-Fi","Wi-Fi problems slow the test down","The device works fully without the internet"],"a":3},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention that 'so few people get tested'?","options":["To blame patients for not caring","To explain the problem the device is designed to solve","To suggest the market is small"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Our device does ___ with the first of those.","a":"away","hint":"ortadan kaldırmak"},{"s":"The ___ is a test that converges on the patient's thresholds.","a":"upshot","hint":"sonuç"},{"s":"A clinician can read the audiogram at a ___.","a":"glance","hint":"bir bakışta"},{"s":"None of this, I should ___, is about replacing audiologists.","a":"stress","hint":"vurgulamak"}],"order":[{"a":"Patient data never leaves the room."},{"a":"The device produces an audiogram in under ten minutes."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bir klinisyen odyogramı bir bakışta okuyabilir.","en":"A clinician can read the audiogram at a glance.","keys":["audiogram","at a glance"]},{"tr":"Bu, odyologların yerini almakla ilgili değil.","en":"This isn't about replacing audiologists.","keys":["replacing audiologists"]},{"tr":"Hasta verileri odadan hiç çıkmaz.","en":"Patient data never leaves the room.","keys":["patient data","never leaves"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Curious doctor","personaTr":"Meraklı doktor","scene":"Bir fuarda kıdemli bir İngiliz odyoloji profesörü, cihazını kibar ama keskin bir şüphecilikle sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Forgive the scepticism, but 'autonomous' is a big word to put on a medical device.","aiTr":"Şüpheciliğimi bağışlayın ama 'otonom', tıbbi bir cihaz için büyük bir söz.","hint":"Fair enough, and what I mean is narrower than it sounds: the device runs the full test and produces an audiogram without an expert in the room.","keys":["without an expert","full test","audiogram"]},{"ai":"Fine, but what's actually going on under the hood while the patient sits there pressing a button?","aiTr":"Peki, hasta orada oturup düğmeye basarken kaputun altında aslında ne oluyor?","hint":"The AI weighs each response and decides in real time which tone is most worth playing next, so it converges on the thresholds instead of plodding through a fixed protocol.","keys":["real time","converges","fixed protocol"]},{"ai":"You can see why some of my colleagues might feel a little threatened by this.","aiTr":"Bazı meslektaşlarımın bundan neden biraz tehdit altında hissedebileceğini anlarsınız.","hint":"I can, but if anything it reserves their expertise for the patients who genuinely need it rather than for routine screening.","keys":["if anything","expertise","genuinely need"]},{"ai":"Last thing: our IT people will want to know where the data goes.","aiTr":"Son bir şey: BT ekibimiz verilerin nereye gittiğini bilmek isteyecek.","hint":"Reassuringly, nowhere: the AI runs on the device itself, so patient data never leaves the room and it works perfectly well offline.","keys":["on the device","never leaves","offline"]}]}},"co-01":{"intro":"Bir konferansta kendini esprili, akıcı ve ikna edici bir şekilde tanıtıyor, kısa bir sohbeti somut bir fırsata dönüştürüyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"I don't think we've crossed paths yet — I'm {name}.","tr":"Sanırım yollarımız henüz kesişmedi; ben {name}."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"Sarah, from a hospital group in the UK, and I confess I'm in desperate need of a coffee after that last panel.","tr":"Sarah, İngiltere'deki bir hastane grubundan; itiraf edeyim, o son panelden sonra bir kahveye fena hâlde ihtiyacım var."},{"who":"Me","en":"Then I'll keep it brief: I founded AIHEAR, a Turkish medtech company tackling a problem most people never hear about, quite literally.","tr":"O zaman kısa keseyim: çoğu insanın, kelimenin tam anlamıyla, hiç duymadığı bir sorunu çözmeye çalışan Türk medtech şirketi AIHEAR'ı kurdum."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"Go on, you've piqued my interest.","tr":"Devam edin, merakımı uyandırdınız."},{"who":"Me","en":"One in five people has some degree of hearing loss, yet most are never tested, simply because there aren't enough audiologists to go round.","tr":"Her beş kişiden birinde bir derece işitme kaybı var, ama çoğu hiç test edilmiyor; çünkü herkese yetecek kadar odyolog yok."},{"who":"Me","en":"So we've built an autonomous audiometer that runs the whole test without a specialist in the room.","tr":"Biz de odada bir uzman olmadan testin tamamını yapan otonom bir odyometre geliştirdik."},{"who":"Me","en":"The patient simply presses a button at each tone, the AI adapts on the fly, and the audiogram is ready in under ten minutes.","tr":"Hasta her seste sadece bir düğmeye basıyor, yapay zekâ anında uyum sağlıyor ve odyogram on dakikadan kısa sürede hazır oluyor."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"If that holds up, it would take a serious bite out of our waiting lists, which in some regions run to several months.","tr":"Bu gerçekten doğruysa, bazı bölgelerde birkaç ayı bulan bekleme listelerimizi ciddi biçimde kısaltır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our clinical data suggest it does hold up, though I'd rather show you the numbers than oversell them in a coffee queue.","tr":"Klinik verilerimiz bunun gerçekten tuttuğunu gösteriyor, ama rakamları bir kahve kuyruğunda abartmaktansa size göstermeyi tercih ederim."},{"who":"Me","en":"I won't hold you up any longer, but may I leave you my card, and perhaps we could pick this up after the next session?","tr":"Sizi daha fazla tutmayayım; kartımı bırakabilir miyim, belki bir sonraki oturumdan sonra konuya devam ederiz?"},{"who":"Sarah","en":"By all means, and do bring those numbers: I'm far more persuadable with data than with adjectives.","tr":"Elbette, o rakamları mutlaka getirin; çünkü beni sıfatlardan çok veriler ikna eder."}],"vocab":[{"en":"cross paths","tr":"yolları kesişmek","ex":"I don't think we've crossed paths before.","def":"to meet someone, often by chance"},{"en":"keep it brief","tr":"kısa kesmek","ex":"I'll keep it brief, since you need a coffee.","def":"to say something in as few words as possible"},{"en":"pique someone's interest","tr":"birinin merakını uyandırmak","ex":"You've piqued my interest.","def":"to make someone curious to know more"},{"en":"go round","tr":"herkese yetmek","ex":"There aren't enough audiologists to go round.","def":"to be enough for everyone who needs it"},{"en":"on the fly","tr":"anında, iş sürerken","ex":"The AI adapts the test on the fly.","def":"while something is happening, without stopping"},{"en":"hold up","tr":"geçerliliğini korumak, doğru çıkmak","ex":"Our clinical data suggest the claim holds up.","def":"to remain true when tested or examined"},{"en":"take a bite out of","tr":"önemli ölçüde azaltmak","ex":"It would take a serious bite out of our waiting lists.","def":"to reduce something by a significant amount"},{"en":"run to","tr":"...i bulmak, ...e varmak","ex":"Waiting lists run to several months.","def":"to reach a particular amount or length"},{"en":"oversell","tr":"abartmak, olduğundan fazla övmek","ex":"I'd rather show you the numbers than oversell them.","def":"to praise something more than it deserves"},{"en":"persuadable","tr":"ikna edilebilir","ex":"I'm more persuadable with data than with adjectives.","def":"able to be convinced"}],"grammar":{"title":"Understatement and soft persuasion","tr":"C2 düzeyinde ikna, abartıdan değil ölçülü ifadeden gelir: 'I'd rather show you than oversell', 'perhaps we could', 'if that holds up'. Bu yapılar güven veren ve kendinden emin bir ton yaratır.","examples":["I'd rather show you the numbers than oversell them.","Perhaps we could pick this up after the next session.","If that holds up, it would take a serious bite out of our waiting lists."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of Sarah's first line?","options":["Cold and formal","Light-hearted and self-deprecating","Impatient and rude","Nervous"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the founder's phrase 'a problem most people never hear about, quite literally' playing on?","options":["The founder's accent","The noise in the conference hall","The fact that the problem is hearing loss"],"a":2},{"q":"Why, according to the founder, are most people never tested?","options":["There aren't enough audiologists to go round","Tests are too expensive","People don't care about their hearing"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the founder imply by preferring to show the numbers rather than oversell them?","options":["They are unsure the device works","They trust the data to speak for itself","They have no data yet"],"a":1},{"q":"What does Sarah's final remark imply?","options":["She is losing interest","She dislikes the founder's style","Evidence will persuade her more than enthusiasm"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"I don't think we've crossed ___ yet.","a":"paths","hint":"yollar"},{"s":"Go on, you've ___ my interest.","a":"piqued","hint":"uyandırmak"},{"s":"The AI adapts on the ___.","a":"fly","hint":"anında"},{"s":"There aren't enough audiologists to go ___.","a":"round","hint":"herkese yetmek"}],"order":[{"a":"Then I'll keep it brief."},{"a":"The audiogram is ready in under ten minutes."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kısa keseyim.","en":"I'll keep it brief.","keys":["keep it brief"]},{"tr":"Merakımı uyandırdınız.","en":"You've piqued my interest.","keys":["piqued my interest"]},{"tr":"Rakamları abartmaktansa size göstermeyi tercih ederim.","en":"I'd rather show you the numbers than oversell them.","keys":["rather show you","oversell"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Operations director at a clinic chain","personaTr":"Bir klinik zincirinin operasyon direktörü","scene":"Kalabalık bir konferans arasında kısa bir fırsatın var; kendini esprili, öz ve ikna edici biçimde tanıt.","turns":[{"ai":"Emma, I run operations for a clinic chain in Ireland, and I'm told you're the person to talk to about hearing.","aiTr":"Emma; İrlanda'da bir klinik zincirinin operasyonlarını yönetiyorum ve işitme konusunda konuşulacak kişinin siz olduğunuzu duydum.","hint":"Guilty as charged. I'm {name}, and I founded AIHEAR, a Turkish medtech company tackling the shortage of audiologists.","keys":["founded","medtech","shortage","audiologists"]},{"ai":"Give me the thirty-second version.","aiTr":"Bana otuz saniyelik özetini verin.","hint":"One in five people has some hearing loss, yet most are never tested, so we've built an autonomous audiometer that needs no specialist in the room.","keys":["one in five","autonomous","no specialist","never tested"]},{"ai":"Bold claim. Does it actually hold up?","aiTr":"İddialı bir söz. Gerçekten tutuyor mu?","hint":"Our clinical data suggest it does, though I'd rather show you the numbers than oversell them in a coffee queue.","keys":["clinical data","rather show you","numbers"]},{"ai":"Fair enough, but I'm due at the next panel.","aiTr":"Makul, ama bir sonraki panelde olmam gerekiyor.","hint":"I won't hold you up, then. May I leave you my card, and perhaps we could pick this up afterwards?","keys":["card","pick this up","hold you up"]}]}},"ab-01":{"intro":"Berlin'de bir daireyi görüyorsun; ev sahibiyle depozito, sözleşme ve belgeler konusunda incelikli ve esprili bir şekilde pazarlık ediyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Landlord","en":"Do come in—I had the kitchen and bathroom gutted last spring, so you're very nearly the first person to see them in their new glory.","tr":"Buyurun girin; geçen bahar mutfağı ve banyoyu baştan sona söktürdüm, yani onları yeni halleriyle gören neredeyse ilk kişisiniz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Well, the photos certainly didn't do it justice; it's flooded with light in a way Berlin flats in winter rarely are.","tr":"Fotoğraflar kesinlikle hakkını vermemiş; kışın Berlin dairelerinde nadiren görülecek kadar ışıl ışıl."},{"who":"Me","en":"Before I fall head over heels for it, though, perhaps you could talk me through what the €1,200 actually covers.","tr":"Ama daireye sırılsıklam âşık olmadan önce, belki 1.200 avronun tam olarak neleri kapsadığını bana anlatırsınız."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"Heating and water are included, but the internet is very much your own affair—and German providers, I'm sorry to say, are not famed for their speed.","tr":"Isınma ve su dahil, ama internet tamamen sizin işiniz; üstelik söylemesi üzücü ama Alman sağlayıcılar hızlarıyla ün salmış değildir."},{"who":"Me","en":"So I gather; I've heard it can be quicker to register a company here than to get connected.","tr":"Öyle duydum; burada şirket kurmanın internete bağlanmaktan daha hızlı olabildiğini söylüyorlar."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"Quite—as for the deposit, it's the customary three months' rent, which brings us to €3,600.","tr":"Aynen öyle; depozitoya gelince, alışılageldiği gibi üç aylık kira, bu da bizi 3.600 avroya getiriyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's perfectly fair, though having just transplanted my whole life from Istanbul, I'd be grateful if we could spread it over three monthly instalments.","tr":"Gayet adil; yine de bütün hayatımı daha yeni İstanbul'dan buraya taşımışken, bunu üç aylık taksite yayabilirsek minnettar olurum."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"By all means—it's what most tenants do, and frankly, it's their right under German law anyway.","tr":"Elbette; kiracıların çoğu böyle yapıyor ve açıkçası bu, Alman hukukuna göre zaten onların hakkı."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"The one thing I won't budge on is the two-year minimum, but the flat is yours from 1 November, should you want it.","tr":"Taviz vermeyeceğim tek şey iki yıllık asgari süre; ama isterseniz daire 1 Kasım'dan itibaren sizin."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"Paperwork-wise, I'll need your passport and proof of income, though as you run your own company, your company documents will do just as well.","tr":"Evrak açısından pasaportunuza ve gelir belgenize ihtiyacım var; ama kendi şirketinizi yönettiğiniz için şirket belgeleriniz de aynı işi görür."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a relief, given that founders are notoriously the last people in the company to get a payslip.","tr":"Bu içimi rahatlattı; ne de olsa kurucuların şirkette maaş bordrosu alan son kişiler olduğu herkesçe bilinir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"do something justice","tr":"hakkını vermek","ex":"The photos didn't do the flat justice.","def":"to show how good something really is"},{"en":"flooded with light","tr":"ışıl ışıl, gün ışığıyla dolu","ex":"The living room is flooded with light.","def":"full of bright natural light"},{"en":"fall head over heels for","tr":"sırılsıklam âşık olmak, vurulmak","ex":"I fell head over heels for the flat.","def":"to fall completely in love with someone or something"},{"en":"your own affair","tr":"sizin kendi işiniz","ex":"The internet is your own affair.","def":"something only you are responsible for"},{"en":"so I gather","tr":"öyle duydum, öyle anlıyorum","ex":"Providers are slow here, so I gather.","def":"used to say you have heard or understood something"},{"en":"spread over","tr":"(ödemeyi) zamana yaymak","ex":"Could we spread the deposit over three months?","def":"to divide a payment across a period of time"},{"en":"by all means","tr":"elbette, tabii ki","ex":"By all means, pay it in instalments.","def":"a polite way of saying yes, certainly"},{"en":"budge on","tr":"taviz vermek, geri adım atmak","ex":"I won't budge on the two-year minimum.","def":"to change your position or opinion, even a little"},{"en":"should you want it","tr":"eğer isterseniz","ex":"The flat is yours, should you want it.","def":"a formal way of saying 'if you want it'"},{"en":"notoriously","tr":"(kötü anlamda) herkesçe bilindiği üzere","ex":"Founders are notoriously badly paid.","def":"in a way that is well known, usually for something bad"}],"grammar":{"title":"Inverted conditionals: 'should you want it'","tr":"'If you want it' yerine 'should you want it' demek koşulu daha kibar ve zarif kılar. Teklif yaparken ve resmi konuşmada sık kullanılır.","examples":["The flat is yours from 1 November, should you want it.","Should you need more time, just let me know.","Should the internet take weeks, you could use a mobile hotspot."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the landlord imply about German internet providers?","options":["They are cheap","They tend to be slow","They are included in most rents","They are hard to cancel"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of the speaker's remark about registering a company?","options":["Ironic and light-hearted","Angry","Formal and neutral"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the landlord add that instalments are 'their right under German law anyway'?","options":["To refuse the request","To suggest a higher rent","To show the request was hardly a favour"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the only point the landlord is firm about?","options":["The deposit","The move-in date","Pets","The two-year minimum"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the final remark suggest about the speaker?","options":["They pay themselves little or no regular salary","They earn a large salary","They dislike paperwork"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"The photos certainly didn't do it ___.","a":"justice","hint":"hakkını vermek"},{"s":"The one thing I won't ___ on is the two-year minimum.","a":"budge","hint":"taviz vermek"},{"s":"The flat is yours from 1 November, ___ you want it.","a":"should","hint":"eğer (resmi)"},{"s":"Founders are ___ the last people in the company to get a payslip.","a":"notoriously","hint":"herkesçe bilindiği üzere"}],"order":[{"a":"The internet is very much your own affair."},{"a":"It's what most tenants do anyway."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Depozitoyu üç aylık taksite yayabilirsek minnettar olurum.","en":"I'd be grateful if we could spread the deposit over three monthly instalments.","keys":["grateful","spread","instalments"]},{"tr":"Fotoğraflar dairenin hakkını hiç vermemiş.","en":"The photos didn't do the flat justice.","keys":["do the flat justice"]},{"tr":"Taviz vermeyeceğim tek şey iki yıllık asgari süre.","en":"The one thing I won't budge on is the two-year minimum.","keys":["won't budge","two-year minimum"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Landlord","personaTr":"Ev sahibi","scene":"Daire turu bitti. Ev sahibi Bayan Becker esprili ve doğrudan biri; son detayları konuşurken sen de aynı tonda cevap veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"So, has it passed inspection, or are you just being polite?","aiTr":"Eee, denetimi geçti mi, yoksa sadece kibarlık mı ediyorsunuz?","hint":"Genuinely, it's passed with flying colours—I haven't seen a flat this bright since I arrived.","keys":["flying colours","genuinely","bright"]},{"ai":"I'd better confess now that I draw the line at dogs, although I've nothing against cats. Does that rule you out?","aiTr":"Şimdiden itiraf edeyim, köpekte çizgiyi çekiyorum ama kedilere bir itirazım yok. Bu sizi eler mi?","hint":"Not remotely—I'm pet-free, and given my hours, any animal of mine would be shamefully neglected.","keys":["not remotely","pet-free","no pets"]},{"ai":"Is there anything nagging at you before you commit?","aiTr":"Karar vermeden önce aklınızı kurcalayan bir şey var mı?","hint":"Only the noise, if I'm honest—how lively does the street get once the sun goes down?","keys":["noise","lively","honest"]},{"ai":"The bedroom looks onto the courtyard, so it's blissfully quiet, but the bar on the corner does get rather boisterous on Fridays. Deal-breaker?","aiTr":"Yatak odası avluya bakıyor, o yüzden mis gibi sessiz; ama köşedeki bar cuma günleri epey şamatalı oluyor. Anlaşmayı bozar mı?","hint":"Hardly—one boisterous night a week at the front of the building is a price I'm more than willing to pay.","keys":["hardly","willing to pay","not a deal-breaker"]}]}},"ai-02":{"intro":"Kuruluş hikâyeni, ince ironi ve zarif bir anlatımla, bir yazar gibi anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"One in five people lives with some degree of hearing loss, which is north of a billion, if you like your numbers big.","tr":"Her beş kişiden biri bir derece işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor; büyük rakamları seviyorsanız, bu bir milyarın üzerinde demek."},{"en":"The figure that actually kept us up at night, though, was a much smaller one: the share of those people who are ever tested.","tr":"Yine de bizi asıl uykusuz bırakan rakam çok daha küçüktü: bu insanların içinde hiç test yaptıranların oranı."},{"en":"It isn't for want of technology; it's that there simply aren't enough audiologists to go round.","tr":"Mesele teknoloji eksikliği değil; herkese yetecek kadar odyolog yok, o kadar."},{"en":"Step outside a major city and a wait of several months for an appointment is less a scandal than a fact of life.","tr":"Büyük bir şehrin dışına çıktığınızda, bir randevu için aylarca beklemek bir skandaldan çok hayatın olağan bir gerçeği."},{"en":"Somewhere in all that, a rather impertinent question took hold.","tr":"Bütün bunların ortasında oldukça cüretkâr bir soru zihnimize yerleşti."},{"en":"What if the test didn't need an expert in the room at all?","tr":"Ya testin odada bir uzmana hiç ihtiyacı olmasaydı?"},{"en":"AIHEAR is, for better or worse, our attempt at an answer.","tr":"AIHEAR, iyisiyle kötüsüyle, bu soruya cevap verme girişimimiz."},{"en":"There are six of us: three engineers, a doctor and two on the business side, which is about as lean as medtech gets.","tr":"Altı kişiyiz: üç mühendis, bir doktor ve iş tarafında iki kişi; bu da bir medikal teknoloji ekibinin olabileceği en yalın hâl."},{"en":"The mission, stripped of pitch-deck gloss, is to make a hearing test as unremarkable to get hold of as a blood pressure check.","tr":"Sunum süslerinden arındırıldığında misyonumuz, işitme testine ulaşmayı tansiyon ölçtürmek kadar sıradan hâle getirmek."},{"en":"We happen to have started in Turkey, but the problem has never respected borders.","tr":"Türkiye'de başlamış olmamız bir rastlantı; sorun ise hiçbir zaman sınır tanımadı."},{"en":"By the same token, neither, we hope, will the solution.","tr":"Aynı şekilde, umarız çözüm de tanımayacak."}],"vocab":[{"en":"north of","tr":"...in üzerinde","ex":"Hearing loss affects north of a billion people.","def":"more than (informal)"},{"en":"keep someone up at night","tr":"birini uykusuz bırakmak","ex":"The figure that kept us up at night was a small one.","def":"to make someone worry a lot"},{"en":"for want of","tr":"...eksikliğinden","ex":"It isn't for want of technology.","def":"because of a lack of something"},{"en":"go round","tr":"herkese yetmek","ex":"There aren't enough audiologists to go round.","def":"to be enough for everyone (British English)"},{"en":"a fact of life","tr":"hayatın bir gerçeği","ex":"Long waits are a fact of life outside the cities.","def":"something unpleasant that people simply have to accept"},{"en":"impertinent","tr":"cüretkâr, küstahça","ex":"It was a rather impertinent question.","def":"slightly rude or bold, challenging what is normal"},{"en":"take hold","tr":"yerleşmek, kök salmak","ex":"Slowly, the idea took hold.","def":"to become strong and established"},{"en":"for better or worse","tr":"iyisiyle kötüsüyle","ex":"For better or worse, this is our answer.","def":"whether the result is good or bad"},{"en":"lean","tr":"yalın","ex":"Our team is about as lean as medtech gets.","def":"using few people or resources"},{"en":"stripped of pitch-deck gloss","tr":"sunum süslerinden arındırılmış","ex":"Stripped of pitch-deck gloss, our mission is simple.","def":"without the attractive marketing language"}],"grammar":{"title":"Understatement and ironic hedging","tr":"C2'de anlamı yumuşatmak ya da ironik bir ton katmak için ölçülü ifadeler kullanılır: 'rather impertinent', 'for better or worse', 'less a scandal than a fact of life'. Doğrudan iddia yerine dinleyicinin çıkarım yapmasına izin verir.","examples":["A rather impertinent question took hold.","AIHEAR is, for better or worse, our attempt at an answer.","A long wait is less a scandal than a fact of life."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of 'if you like your numbers big'?","options":["Slightly ironic","Angry","Apologetic"],"a":0},{"q":"Which number worried the founders most?","options":["The total number of people with hearing loss","The share of people who are ever tested","The price of a hearing test"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'less a scandal than a fact of life' suggest?","options":["Long waits are rare and shocking","Long waits only happen in big cities","Long waits are so common that people simply accept them"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker call the question 'rather impertinent'?","options":["It was rude to doctors","It challenged the assumption that an expert must be present","It was asked by a journalist"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'neither, we hope, will the solution' imply?","options":["The solution will only work in Turkey","They are unsure the product works","They hope to stay small","They intend the product to cross borders too"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"There simply aren't enough audiologists to go ___.","a":"round","hint":"herkese yetmek"},{"s":"It isn't for ___ of technology.","a":"want","hint":"eksiklik"},{"s":"AIHEAR is, for better or ___, our attempt at an answer.","a":"worse","hint":"iyisiyle kötüsüyle"},{"s":"Somewhere in all that, a rather impertinent question took ___.","a":"hold","hint":"yerleşmek"}],"order":[{"a":"The problem has never respected borders."},{"a":"What if the test didn't need an expert at all?"}],"translate":[{"tr":"Mesele teknoloji eksikliği değil.","en":"It isn't for want of technology.","keys":["for want of","technology"]},{"tr":"Sorun hiçbir zaman sınır tanımadı.","en":"The problem has never respected borders.","keys":["never respected borders"]},{"tr":"Altı kişilik yalın bir ekibiz.","en":"We are a lean team of six.","keys":["lean team","six"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Journalist","personaTr":"Gazeteci","scene":"Tanınmış bir yayından keskin zekâlı bir gazeteci, klişe olmayan bir kuruluş hikâyesi duymak istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Every founder has an origin story, so what's yours, minus the pitch-deck gloss?","aiTr":"Her kurucunun bir çıkış hikâyesi vardır; sizinki ne, sunum süslerini çıkarırsak?","hint":"Honestly, it was one figure that kept us up at night: how few of the billion-plus people with hearing loss are ever tested.","keys":["kept us up at night","ever tested","hearing loss"]},{"ai":"Isn't that just a question of money, though?","aiTr":"Ama bu sadece bir para meselesi değil mi?","hint":"Not really; it isn't for want of technology or funding so much as audiologists, and there simply aren't enough to go round.","keys":["for want of","audiologists","go round"]},{"ai":"And the idea itself, was there a eureka moment?","aiTr":"Peki fikrin kendisi; bir 'buldum!' anı oldu mu?","hint":"Less a eureka moment than a rather impertinent question: what if the test didn't need an expert in the room at all?","keys":["impertinent","what if","expert"]},{"ai":"A Turkish start-up with six people taking on a global problem: isn't that a little ambitious?","aiTr":"Altı kişilik bir Türk girişimi küresel bir sorunu üstleniyor; bu biraz fazla iddialı değil mi?","hint":"Perhaps, but the problem has never respected borders, and by the same token, we don't intend the solution to either.","keys":["respected borders","by the same token","solution"]}]}},"st-02":{"intro":"Küçük bir ekibi yönetmekten çıkardığın dersleri, ince bir öz eleştiri ve doğal bir akıcılıkla anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"In a team of six, every misunderstanding is expensive, because nobody has the bandwidth to clean up after anyone else.","tr":"Altı kişilik bir ekipte her yanlış anlaşılma pahalıya patlar, çünkü kimsenin başkasının arkasını toplayacak vakti yok."},{"en":"Hence the Monday stand-up, which is about the only meeting I'd defend to the hilt.","tr":"Pazartesi toplantısı da bu yüzden var; sonuna kadar savunacağım neredeyse tek toplantı o."},{"en":"Each of us runs through what we've delivered, what's next and what's in the way, and it's over before anyone's coffee has gone cold.","tr":"Her birimiz neyi teslim ettiğimizi, sırada ne olduğunu ve önümüzde ne engel olduğunu hızlıca anlatırız; kimsenin kahvesi soğumadan da biter."},{"en":"If there's one thing I've learned, it's that ambiguity is contagious: a fuzzy brief gets you fuzzy work.","tr":"Öğrendiğim bir şey varsa o da belirsizliğin bulaşıcı olduğu: muğlak bir talimat muğlak bir iş getirir."},{"en":"So 'could someone take a look at the report?' has given way to one name, one task and one date: the test report, by Friday.","tr":"Bu yüzden 'biri rapora bir bakabilir mi?' yerini tek bir isme, tek bir göreve ve tek bir tarihe bıraktı: test raporu, cumaya kadar."},{"en":"When things go sideways, which they inevitably do, the post-mortem is about the process, not the person.","tr":"İşler ters gittiğinde, ki kaçınılmaz olarak gider, değerlendirme kişiyle değil süreçle ilgilidir."},{"en":"The moment people start covering their backs, problems go underground, and by the time they resurface they've usually doubled in size.","tr":"İnsanlar kendilerini sağlama almaya başladığı anda sorunlar gizlenir ve yeniden ortaya çıktıklarında genellikle iki katına çıkmış olurlar."},{"en":"Feedback is frequent, positive and negative alike, and very much a two-way street.","tr":"Geri bildirim, olumlu olsun olumsuz olsun sıktır ve kesinlikle karşılıklıdır."},{"en":"That last part was driven home when one of our engineers told me, quite gently, that I had a habit of hijacking meetings.","tr":"Bu son kısım, mühendislerimizden biri bana oldukça nazik bir şekilde toplantıları ele geçirme alışkanlığım olduğunu söylediğinde iyice kafama dank etti."},{"en":"It wasn't what I wanted to hear, but she had a point, and I've been making a conscious effort to listen more than I talk ever since.","tr":"Duymak istediğim şey değildi ama haklılık payı vardı ve o günden beri konuştuğumdan daha çok dinlemek için bilinçli bir çaba gösteriyorum."},{"en":"That said, the real lesson is humbling: the people I've hired are far better at their jobs than I'd ever be, so my job is mostly to trust them and keep the path clear.","tr":"Yine de asıl ders insanı alçakgönüllü kılıyor: işe aldığım insanlar kendi işlerinde benim hiçbir zaman olamayacağım kadar iyi, bu yüzden benim işim çoğunlukla onlara güvenmek ve yollarını açık tutmak."}],"vocab":[{"en":"bandwidth","tr":"kapasite (zaman ve zihinsel enerji)","ex":"Nobody has the bandwidth to clean up after anyone else.","def":"the time and mental energy someone has available"},{"en":"defend to the hilt","tr":"sonuna kadar savunmak","ex":"It's the only meeting I'd defend to the hilt.","def":"to support something completely"},{"en":"fuzzy brief","tr":"muğlak talimat","ex":"A fuzzy brief gets you fuzzy work.","def":"instructions for a task that are unclear"},{"en":"give way to","tr":"yerini ...e bırakmak","ex":"Vague requests have given way to clear deadlines.","def":"to be replaced by something"},{"en":"go sideways","tr":"ters gitmek, rayından çıkmak","ex":"When things go sideways, we look at the process.","def":"(informal) to go wrong unexpectedly"},{"en":"post-mortem","tr":"olay sonrası değerlendirme","ex":"The post-mortem is about the process, not the person.","def":"a meeting to analyse what went wrong after a problem"},{"en":"cover your back","tr":"kendini sağlama almak","ex":"People start covering their backs when they fear blame.","def":"to protect yourself from being blamed"},{"en":"a two-way street","tr":"karşılıklı bir süreç","ex":"Feedback is very much a two-way street.","def":"something that both sides must contribute to"},{"en":"drive home","tr":"iyice kafasına dank ettirmek","ex":"That lesson was driven home by one of our engineers.","def":"to make someone understand something very clearly"},{"en":"hijack a meeting","tr":"toplantıyı ele geçirmek","ex":"I had a habit of hijacking meetings.","def":"to take control of a meeting so that it is all about you"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging and understatement","tr":"Akıcı konuşanlar fikirlerini abartmadan vurgulamak için küçük kelimelerle oynar: 'about the only meeting' (neredeyse tek toplantı), 'quite gently' (oldukça nazikçe), 'she had a point' (haklılık payı vardı). Bu, kendinden emin ama alçakgönüllü bir ton yaratır.","examples":["It's about the only meeting I'd defend to the hilt.","She told me, quite gently, that I had a habit of hijacking meetings.","It wasn't what I wanted to hear, but she had a point."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'ambiguity is contagious'?","options":["Unclear instructions lead to unclear work","Illness spreads quickly in small offices","Meetings should be cancelled"],"a":0},{"q":"Why is the Monday stand-up the one meeting the speaker would defend?","options":["It's the longest meeting of the week","Investors require it","It keeps everyone aligned without wasting anyone's time"],"a":2},{"q":"What does 'problems go underground' imply?","options":["Problems are solved faster","Problems get hidden and grow worse","Problems are passed to another team"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of 'It wasn't what I wanted to hear, but she had a point'?","options":["Bitter and resentful","Sarcastic","Candid and self-aware"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by saying the team are 'far better at their jobs than I'd ever be'?","options":["They regret hiring experts","They see humility and trust as central to leading the team","They plan to replace the team"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Nobody has the ___ to clean up after anyone else.","a":"bandwidth","hint":"kapasite (zaman/enerji)"},{"s":"When things go ___, the post-mortem is about the process.","a":"sideways","hint":"ters gitmek"},{"s":"Feedback is very much a two-way ___.","a":"street","hint":"karşılıklı süreç"},{"s":"She told me I had a habit of ___ meetings.","a":"hijacking","hint":"ele geçirmek"}],"order":[{"a":"The post-mortem is about the process not the person."},{"a":"Feedback is very much a two-way street."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kimsenin başkasının arkasını toplayacak vakti yok.","en":"Nobody has the bandwidth to clean up after anyone else.","keys":["bandwidth","clean up after"]},{"tr":"Duymak istediğim şey değildi ama haklılık payı vardı.","en":"It wasn't what I wanted to hear, but she had a point.","keys":["wanted to hear","had a point"]},{"tr":"Değerlendirme kişiyle değil süreçle ilgili.","en":"The post-mortem is about the process, not the person.","keys":["post-mortem","process","not the person"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"New engineer","personaTr":"Yeni işe başlayan mühendis","scene":"Deneyimli ve biraz şüpheci yeni mühendis, ekip kültürünün gerçekte nasıl işlediğini anlamak istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I'm still getting the lay of the land; what's the one thing I really shouldn't miss?","aiTr":"Hâlâ ortamı tanımaya çalışıyorum; asla kaçırmamam gereken tek şey ne?","hint":"The Monday stand-up: it's about the only meeting I'd defend to the hilt, and it's over before anyone's coffee has gone cold.","keys":["stand-up","defend","Monday"]},{"ai":"And how do you like tasks to be handed over?","aiTr":"Peki görevlerin nasıl devredilmesini seversin?","hint":"One name, one task, one date, because if there's one thing I've learned, it's that a fuzzy brief gets you fuzzy work.","keys":["one name","fuzzy","one date"]},{"ai":"What happens when something I own goes sideways?","aiTr":"Sorumlu olduğum bir şey ters giderse ne olur?","hint":"Tell me early; the post-mortem is about the process, not the person, so there's no need to cover your back.","keys":["post-mortem","process","cover your back"]},{"ai":"Fair enough, but is feedback here really a two-way street?","aiTr":"Anlaşıldı, ama burada geri bildirim gerçekten karşılıklı mı?","hint":"Very much so; one of our engineers once told me I had a habit of hijacking meetings, and she had a point.","keys":["two-way","hijacking","had a point"]}]}},"te-01":{"intro":"Şüpheci bir sağlık muhabirine, abartıya kaçmadan, ironi ve ince ayrımlarla yapay zekânın sağlıktaki gerçek değerini anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Every few months, someone announces that AI is about to make doctors obsolete, and every few months, the doctors, rather inconveniently, turn up for work.","tr":"Birkaç ayda bir biri yapay zekânın doktorları gereksiz kılmak üzere olduğunu ilan ediyor ve birkaç ayda bir doktorlar, bu iddiayı biraz da utandırırcasına, işe gelmeye devam ediyor."},{"en":"The more interesting story, I'd suggest, is a quieter one: machines absorbing the high-volume, low-judgment work that wears clinicians down.","tr":"Bence daha ilginç olan hikâye daha sessiz bir hikâye: Makinelerin, klinisyenleri yıpratan yüksek hacimli ve az muhakeme gerektiren işi üstlenmesi."},{"en":"A model can triage thousands of scans overnight without its attention flagging at three in the morning, which is more than can be said for any of us.","tr":"Bir model, sabahın üçünde dikkati dağılmadan bir gecede binlerce taramayı önceliklendirebilir; aynısını hiçbirimiz için söyleyemeyiz."},{"en":"That said, a model inherits every blind spot in its training data, and it does so with unnerving confidence.","tr":"Bununla birlikte bir model, eğitim verisindeki her kör noktayı devralır ve bunu tedirgin edici bir özgüvenle yapar."},{"en":"If a population is thinly represented in the data, the system's performance there tends to degrade quietly, with no alarm bells to warn anyone.","tr":"Bir nüfus grubu veride zayıf temsil ediliyorsa, sistemin o gruptaki performansı kimseyi uyaracak bir alarm çalmadan sessizce düşme eğiliminde olur."},{"en":"Hence the insistence, which I share wholeheartedly, that accountability for the final call rests with a clinician.","tr":"Son kararın sorumluluğunun bir klinisyende olması gerektiği konusundaki ısrar da buradan geliyor ve ben de bu görüşe yürekten katılıyorum."},{"en":"Where I think the real dividend lies, though, is not in sharper diagnosis but in wider access.","tr":"Ancak bence asıl kazanç daha keskin teşhiste değil, daha geniş erişimde yatıyor."},{"en":"Roughly one in five people has some degree of hearing loss, and yet the overwhelming majority are never tested, for the unglamorous reason that there simply aren't enough audiologists to go round.","tr":"Yaklaşık her beş kişiden birinde bir derece işitme kaybı var, ama ezici çoğunluğu hiç test edilmiyor; nedeni pek de çarpıcı değil: Herkese yetecek kadar odyolog yok."},{"en":"In smaller towns, the wait for an appointment is measured in months rather than weeks.","tr":"Küçük kasabalarda randevu beklemesi haftalarla değil, aylarla ölçülüyor."},{"en":"Our audiometer is a modest attempt to chip away at that: the patient presses a button, the AI adapts the test as it goes, and an audiogram emerges in under ten minutes.","tr":"Odyometremiz bu sorunu yavaş yavaş aşındırmaya yönelik mütevazı bir girişim: Hasta bir düğmeye basıyor, yapay zekâ testi ilerledikçe uyarlıyor ve on dakikadan kısa sürede bir odyogram ortaya çıkıyor."},{"en":"Because the model runs on the device itself, it works offline and patient data stays put, while updates go out roughly once a month.","tr":"Model cihazın kendi üzerinde çalıştığı için internetsiz çalışıyor ve hasta verileri yerinde kalıyor; güncellemeler ise yaklaşık ayda bir gönderiliyor."},{"en":"None of this sidelines the audiologist; if anything, it frees them to do the work that only they can do.","tr":"Bunların hiçbiri odyoloğu kenara itmiyor; aksine, yalnızca onların yapabileceği işe zaman ayırmalarını sağlıyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"obsolete","tr":"gereksiz, modası geçmiş","ex":"AI won't make doctors obsolete any time soon.","def":"no longer needed or used"},{"en":"wear someone down","tr":"birini yıpratmak","ex":"Repetitive screening wears clinicians down.","def":"to make someone tired or weak gradually"},{"en":"triage","tr":"önceliklendirmek, triyaj yapmak","ex":"The model can triage thousands of scans overnight.","def":"to sort cases by how urgently they need attention"},{"en":"blind spot","tr":"kör nokta","ex":"A model inherits every blind spot in its data.","def":"an area where someone or something lacks knowledge or awareness"},{"en":"unnerving","tr":"tedirgin edici","ex":"It makes mistakes with unnerving confidence.","def":"making you feel nervous or uneasy"},{"en":"the final call","tr":"son karar","ex":"The final call rests with a clinician.","def":"the last and deciding judgment"},{"en":"dividend","tr":"getiri, kazanç (mecazi)","ex":"The real dividend of AI is wider access.","def":"a benefit that results from an action"},{"en":"go round","tr":"herkese yetmek","ex":"There aren't enough audiologists to go round.","def":"to be enough for everyone"},{"en":"chip away at","tr":"yavaş yavaş azaltmak, aşındırmak","ex":"Our device chips away at the waiting lists.","def":"to reduce something gradually, little by little"},{"en":"stay put","tr":"yerinde kalmak","ex":"Patient data stays put on the device.","def":"to remain in the same place"}],"grammar":{"title":"Discourse markers for nuance","tr":"'That said' (bununla birlikte), 'Hence' (bu yüzden), 'if anything' (aksine, hatta) gibi bağlaçlar fikirler arasındaki ince ilişkiyi kurar. Konuşmayı akıcı ve ölçülü kılar.","examples":["That said, a model inherits every blind spot in its training data.","Hence the insistence that accountability rests with a clinician.","If anything, it frees them to do the work that only they can do."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of the opening sentence?","options":["Alarmed","Dryly ironic","Apologetic","Neutral and technical"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, what makes biased AI particularly dangerous?","options":["It is expensive to fix","It fails loudly","Its errors come with high confidence and no warning","It can't process scans"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by 'the unglamorous reason'?","options":["The cause of the problem is mundane, not technological","Audiologists are badly paid","Hearing tests are boring","The reason is kept secret"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention that the model runs on the device?","options":["To explain why it is cheap","To show it never needs updates","To prove it's faster than cloud AI","To highlight that it works offline and keeps data local"],"a":3},{"q":"What does 'a modest attempt to chip away at that' suggest about the speaker?","options":["They are overselling the device","They present the device as a partial solution, not a cure-all","They think the problem cannot be solved","They doubt their own product"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Every few months, someone announces that AI is about to make doctors ___.","a":"obsolete","hint":"gereksiz"},{"s":"A model inherits every blind ___ in its training data.","a":"spot","hint":"nokta (kör nokta)"},{"s":"There simply aren't enough audiologists to go ___.","a":"round","hint":"yetmek (go …)"},{"s":"Our audiometer is a modest attempt to chip ___ at that.","a":"away","hint":"yavaş yavaş azaltmak (chip … at)"}],"order":[{"a":"Accountability for the final call rests with a clinician."},{"a":"None of this sidelines the audiologist."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bununla birlikte bir model, eğitim verisindeki her kör noktayı devralır.","en":"That said, a model inherits every blind spot in its training data.","keys":["that said","blind spot"]},{"tr":"Randevu beklemesi haftalarla değil, aylarla ölçülüyor.","en":"The wait for an appointment is measured in months rather than weeks.","keys":["measured in months","rather than weeks"]},{"tr":"Hasta verileri yerinde kalıyor.","en":"Patient data stays put.","keys":["stays put"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Health journalist","personaTr":"Sağlık muhabiri","scene":"Abartılı iddialardan hoşlanmayan şüpheci bir sağlık muhabiri, yapay zekâ ve sağlık üzerine seninle röportaj yapıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"You must be tired of hearing that AI will make doctors obsolete. Is there anything to it?","aiTr":"Yapay zekânın doktorları gereksiz kılacağını duymaktan bıkmışsınızdır. Bunda bir gerçeklik payı var mı?","hint":"Not much, I'd suggest. The more interesting story is machines absorbing the high-volume work that wears clinicians down.","keys":["wears clinicians down","high-volume","I'd suggest"]},{"ai":"Critics say these systems simply bake in existing biases. Fair?","aiTr":"Eleştirmenler bu sistemlerin mevcut önyargıları kalıcı hale getirdiğini söylüyor. Haklılar mı?","hint":"Fair enough. A model inherits every blind spot in its training data, which is why the final call has to rest with a clinician.","keys":["blind spot","final call","clinician"]},{"ai":"So where's the real payoff, if not in diagnosis?","aiTr":"Teşhiste değilse asıl getiri nerede?","hint":"In access. One in five people has some hearing loss, yet most are never tested because there aren't enough audiologists to go round.","keys":["access","go round","one in five"]},{"ai":"And what about privacy? Where does all that patient data end up?","aiTr":"Peki ya mahremiyet? Bütün o hasta verileri nereye gidiyor?","hint":"Nowhere, in fact: the model runs on the device itself, so it works offline and patient data stays put.","keys":["stays put","on the device","offline"]}]}},"li-01":{"intro":"Havalimanında ve otelde, ana dili İngilizce olan biri gibi esprili, rahat ve son derece kibar konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Officer","en":"Morning, and what brings you here today?","tr":"Günaydın, bugün sizi buraya ne getirdi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"A medical technology conference, so I'm afraid it's all work and no play this time.","tr":"Bir medikal teknoloji konferansı; korkarım bu sefer hep iş var, eğlence yok."},{"who":"Officer","en":"And how long do you expect to be with us?","tr":"Peki ne kadar süre bizimle olmayı düşünüyorsunuz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Four days, with a return flight on Friday that I'd rather not miss.","tr":"Dört gün; cuma günü de kaçırmamayı tercih edeceğim bir dönüş uçuşum var."},{"who":"Officer","en":"Well, that all looks in order, so enjoy your stay, conference permitting.","tr":"Peki, her şey yolunda görünüyor; konferans izin verirse iyi konaklamalar."},{"who":"Me","en":"Evening, there ought to be a reservation under the name {name}, though after the day I've had, I wouldn't bet on it.","tr":"İyi akşamlar, {name} adına bir rezervasyon olması lazım, gerçi bugün yaşadıklarımdan sonra pek iddiaya girmezdim."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"No need to worry, it's right here, and if I might just see your passport, we'll have you sorted in no time.","tr":"Merak etmeyin, burada; pasaportunuzu bir görebilirsem işinizi hemencecik hallederiz."},{"who":"Me","en":"By all means, and while you're at it, I don't suppose breakfast is included?","tr":"Elbette; hazır elinizdeyken, kahvaltı dahil değildir herhalde?"},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"It is indeed, served from 7 until 10, which should give you ample time before your first session.","tr":"Dahil tabii, 7'den 10'a kadar servis ediliyor; bu da ilk oturumunuzdan önce size bolca zaman tanır."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"You're in 512 on the fifth floor, and your key card's good to go.","tr":"Beşinci kattaki 512'desiniz, anahtar kartınız da kullanıma hazır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Wonderful, and before I disappear upstairs, might I trouble you for the wifi password?","tr":"Harika; yukarı kaybolmadan önce wifi şifresini rica edebilir miyim?"}],"vocab":[{"en":"all work and no play","tr":"hep iş, hiç eğlence yok","ex":"I'm afraid it's all work and no play this trip.","def":"only working, with no time for fun"},{"en":"conference permitting","tr":"konferans izin verirse","ex":"Enjoy your stay, conference permitting.","def":"if the conference allows it (like 'weather permitting')"},{"en":"there ought to be","tr":"...olması gerekir","ex":"There ought to be a reservation under my name.","def":"there should be; used for something you expect"},{"en":"I wouldn't bet on it","tr":"pek iddiaya girmezdim","ex":"The flight might be on time, but I wouldn't bet on it.","def":"I doubt it; it may well not happen"},{"en":"have someone sorted","tr":"birinin işini halletmek","ex":"We'll have you sorted in no time.","def":"to solve or arrange something for someone"},{"en":"in no time","tr":"hemencecik, çabucak","ex":"Check-in was done in no time.","def":"very quickly"},{"en":"by all means","tr":"elbette, buyurun","ex":"By all means, here's my passport.","def":"certainly; of course you may"},{"en":"I don't suppose...?","tr":"...değildir herhalde?","ex":"I don't suppose breakfast is included?","def":"a very polite, indirect way to ask a question"},{"en":"ample time","tr":"bolca zaman","ex":"Breakfast gives you ample time before the first session.","def":"more than enough time"},{"en":"Might I trouble you for...?","tr":"...rica edebilir miyim?","ex":"Might I trouble you for the wifi password?","def":"an extremely polite way to ask for something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Tentative politeness: I don't suppose... / Might I...?","tr":"Ana dili İngilizce olanlar rica ederken çoğu zaman çekingen yapılar kullanır: 'I don't suppose...?', 'Might I...?', 'there ought to be'. Bu ifadeler talebi yumuşatır ve karşı tarafa 'hayır' deme alanı bırakır.","examples":["I don't suppose breakfast is included?","Might I trouble you for the wifi password?","There ought to be a reservation under my name."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does \"all work and no play\" tell the officer?","options":["The trip is purely for business","The speaker dislikes their job","The speaker plans to go sightseeing"],"a":0},{"q":"What is implied by \"a return flight on Friday that I'd rather not miss\"?","options":["The flight is already cancelled","The speaker is keen to get home on time","The speaker has no ticket"],"a":1},{"q":"How should \"conference permitting\" be understood?","options":["The officer needs to see a conference permit","The conference has been cancelled","The conference may leave little time for enjoyment"],"a":2},{"q":"What tone does the speaker take with \"I wouldn't bet on it\"?","options":["Angry and accusatory","Formal and cold","Anxious and panicked","Wry and self-deprecating"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the receptionist imply by mentioning \"your first session\"?","options":["Breakfast ends before the conference starts","There is enough time for breakfast before the conference","The speaker will have to skip breakfast"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"I'm afraid it's all work and no ___ this time.","a":"play","hint":"eğlence, oyun"},{"s":"There ought to be a reservation, though I wouldn't ___ on it.","a":"bet","hint":"iddiaya girmek"},{"s":"We'll have you sorted in no ___.","a":"time","hint":"(hemencecik) zaman"},{"s":"Might I ___ you for the wifi password?","a":"trouble","hint":"rahatsız etmek"}],"order":[{"a":"We'll have you sorted in no time."},{"a":"I'd rather not miss my return flight on Friday."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Korkarım bu sefer hep iş var, eğlence yok.","en":"I'm afraid it's all work and no play this time.","keys":["all work and no play"]},{"tr":"Kahvaltı dahil değildir herhalde?","en":"I don't suppose breakfast is included?","keys":["don't suppose","breakfast"]},{"tr":"Wifi şifresini rica edebilir miyim?","en":"Might I trouble you for the wifi password?","keys":["trouble you","wifi password"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hotel receptionist","personaTr":"Otel resepsiyonisti","scene":"Berlin'de yorucu bir günün ardından gece otele varıyorsun. Resepsiyonist esprili; sen de rahat ve kibar bir dille karşılık veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Good evening! You look like you've had quite a day. Checking in?","aiTr":"İyi akşamlar! Epey yoğun bir gün geçirmişe benziyorsunuz. Giriş mi yapacaksınız?","hint":"You could say that; there ought to be a reservation under the name {name}.","keys":["ought to be","reservation","under the name"]},{"ai":"Let me see... yes, there we are. If I might just see your passport?","aiTr":"Bir bakayım... evet, buldum. Pasaportunuzu bir görebilir miyim?","hint":"By all means, here you are; I don't suppose breakfast is included?","keys":["by all means","don't suppose","breakfast"]},{"ai":"It is, seven till ten. You're in 512, fifth floor. Anything else I can do for you this evening?","aiTr":"Dahil, yediden ona kadar. Beşinci kat, 512'desiniz. Bu akşam sizin için yapabileceğim başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"Might I trouble you for the wifi password? I've a presentation that still needs some polish.","keys":["trouble you","wifi password","presentation"]},{"ai":"It's on your key card. Shall I arrange a taxi for the morning, or are you braving public transport?","aiTr":"Anahtar kartınızda yazıyor. Sabah için taksi ayarlayayım mı, yoksa toplu taşımayı mı göze alıyorsunuz?","hint":"A taxi at 8 would be a godsend, thank you; I'd rather not arrive at the conference flustered.","keys":["taxi","godsend","conference"]}]}},"ab-02":{"intro":"Berlin'de bankada hesap açıyorsun; Alman bürokrasisine dair esprili ama kibar yorumlarla tüm detayları akıcı biçimde konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Clerk","en":"Good morning—what can we do for you?","tr":"Günaydın, sizin için ne yapabiliriz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I've recently moved to Berlin to open my company's European office, so I'm hoping to leave today with a personal account and, if the gods are kind, a business one too.","tr":"Şirketimin Avrupa ofisini açmak için kısa süre önce Berlin'e taşındım; bugün buradan kişisel bir hesapla ve şansım yaver giderse bir de ticari hesapla çıkmayı umuyorum."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"I'll do what I can, though I'm bound to ask first whether you've registered your address, since without that there's very little I'm able to do.","tr":"Elimden geleni yaparım, ama önce adresinizi kaydettirip kaydettirmediğinizi sormak zorundayım, çünkü o olmadan yapabileceğim çok az şey var."},{"who":"Me","en":"I braved the citizens' office last week, so I have the certificate here, along with my passport and residence permit.","tr":"Geçen hafta cesaretimi toplayıp Bürgeramt'a gittim; belge burada, pasaportum ve oturma iznimle birlikte."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Then the personal account is straightforward, and it's free of charge, provided at least €1,000 finds its way in each month.","tr":"O halde kişisel hesap kolay; her ay en az 1.000 avro hesaba girdiği sürece de ücretsiz."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Failing that, we'd charge a nominal €5 a month.","tr":"O olmazsa aylık sembolik bir 5 avro alırız."},{"who":"Me","en":"And the business account—is it merely a pricier version of the same thing, or is there more to it?","tr":"Peki ticari hesap aynı şeyin sadece daha pahalı bir versiyonu mu, yoksa işin içinde başka bir şey de var mı?"},{"who":"Clerk","en":"It's built for company transactions, which keeps them neatly walled off from your personal finances, and at €15 a month it does come at something of a premium.","tr":"Şirket işlemleri için tasarlanmış, bu da onları kişisel paranızdan düzgünce ayırıyor; aylık 15 avroyla da biraz daha pahalıya geliyor."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"The snag, I'm afraid, is that we can't open it until your company has been entered in the commercial register.","tr":"Korkarım pürüz şu: şirketiniz ticaret siciline kaydedilene kadar onu açamıyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm assured that's imminent, so I'll come back next week, German bureaucracy permitting.","tr":"Bunun an meselesi olduğu konusunda bana güvence verildi; Alman bürokrasisi izin verirse gelecek hafta tekrar gelirim."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"In the meantime, your debit card will arrive by post, and the PIN will follow under separate cover, purely as a precaution.","tr":"Bu arada banka kartınız postayla gelecek, şifreniz de tamamen önlem amacıyla ayrı bir zarfla ardından gelecek."},{"who":"Me","en":"Two letters for one card—I can see I'll be getting to know the postman rather well.","tr":"Bir kart için iki mektup; anlaşılan postacıyla epey yakından tanışacağım."}],"vocab":[{"en":"if the gods are kind","tr":"şansım yaver giderse","ex":"I'll leave with both accounts, if the gods are kind.","def":"if luck is on my side"},{"en":"be bound to","tr":"...mek zorunda olmak","ex":"I'm bound to ask about your address.","def":"to be required or obliged to do something"},{"en":"brave","tr":"cesaretle göğüs germek","ex":"I braved the citizens' office last week.","def":"to face something unpleasant with courage"},{"en":"find its way","tr":"yolunu bulmak, bir şekilde gelmek","ex":"At least €1,000 finds its way in each month.","def":"to arrive somewhere, often gradually"},{"en":"failing that","tr":"o olmazsa","ex":"Failing that, we'd charge a small fee.","def":"if that does not happen"},{"en":"nominal","tr":"sembolik","ex":"We charge a nominal fee of €5.","def":"very small compared with the real value"},{"en":"walled off","tr":"kesin çizgilerle ayrılmış","ex":"Company money is walled off from personal funds.","def":"completely separated from something else"},{"en":"at a premium","tr":"daha pahalıya, ek ücretle","ex":"It comes at something of a premium.","def":"at a higher price than usual"},{"en":"the snag","tr":"pürüz, sorun","ex":"The snag is the commercial register.","def":"a small problem or difficulty"},{"en":"under separate cover","tr":"ayrı zarfla","ex":"The PIN will follow under separate cover.","def":"in a different envelope or letter"}],"grammar":{"title":"Elegant conditions: provided, failing that, permitting","tr":"'If' yerine 'provided (that)', 'failing that' ve '… permitting' gibi kalıplar koşulu daha zarif ve ölçülü ifade eder. Resmi konuşmada ve hafif ironide sık kullanılır.","examples":["It's free of charge, provided at least €1,000 comes in each month.","Failing that, we'd charge €5 a month.","I'll be back next week, German bureaucracy permitting."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'if the gods are kind' suggest about the speaker's expectations?","options":["They doubt the business account will be easy","They expect no problems at all","They are very religious"],"a":0},{"q":"How does the clerk describe the €5 fee?","options":["Excessive","Nominal","Hidden"],"a":1},{"q":"What is 'the snag' with the business account?","options":["Its high price","The PIN","The company isn't in the commercial register yet"],"a":2},{"q":"What tone does 'German bureaucracy permitting' have?","options":["Openly hostile","Wryly sceptical","Completely neutral","Deeply anxious"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker's final remark imply?","options":["They expect plenty of post from German institutions","They dislike the postman","The card has been lost"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"I ___ the citizens' office last week.","a":"braved","hint":"cesaret edip gitmek"},{"s":"___ that, we'd charge a nominal €5 a month.","a":"Failing","hint":"o olmazsa"},{"s":"At €15 a month, it does come at something of a ___.","a":"premium","hint":"daha yüksek fiyat"},{"s":"The PIN will follow under separate ___.","a":"cover","hint":"zarf"}],"order":[{"a":"The snag is that we can't open it yet."},{"a":"I'll be getting to know the postman rather well."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Adresinizi kaydettirip kaydettirmediğinizi sormak zorundayım.","en":"I'm bound to ask whether you've registered your address.","keys":["bound to ask","registered your address"]},{"tr":"Her ay en az 1.000 avro gelmesi şartıyla hesap ücretsiz.","en":"The account is free, provided at least €1,000 comes in each month.","keys":["provided","comes in"]},{"tr":"Ticari hesap biraz daha pahalıya geliyor.","en":"The business account comes at something of a premium.","keys":["at something of a premium","business account"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Bank clerk","personaTr":"Banka memuru","scene":"Bankadasın. Memur esprili ve rahat biri; sen de ona aynı incelikli tonda cevap veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Good morning—personal or business, or are you one of those ambitious souls after both?","aiTr":"Günaydın; kişisel mi, ticari mi, yoksa ikisinin de peşinde olan o hırslı insanlardan biri misiniz?","hint":"Guilty as charged—I'd like both, though I gather the business account may have to wait.","keys":["guilty as charged","both","business account"]},{"ai":"It may, I'm afraid. In the meantime, I'll need proof that you've registered your address.","aiTr":"Maalesef bekleyebilir. Bu arada adresinizi kaydettirdiğinize dair bir belgeye ihtiyacım olacak.","hint":"Here's the certificate—I braved the citizens' office last week, and I've brought my passport and residence permit for good measure.","keys":["certificate","braved","residence permit"]},{"ai":"Splendid. Will you be a branch person or an app person?","aiTr":"Harika. Şubeci mi olacaksınız, uygulamacı mı?","hint":"Firmly an app person—my working hours and your opening hours are unlikely ever to overlap.","keys":["app person","opening hours","app"]},{"ai":"Then you'll receive a temporary password by text to log in, which you'll change at first use. Anything else I can do?","aiTr":"O halde giriş için kısa mesajla geçici bir şifre alacaksınız, ilk kullanımda onu değiştireceksiniz. Yapabileceğim başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"Nothing more for now, thank you—I'll be back next week, assuming the commercial register cooperates.","keys":["nothing more","be back","commercial register"]}]}},"ai-03":{"intro":"Prototipini, deneyimli bir yatırımcıya özgüvenli, esprili ve riskler konusunda açık sözlü bir dille sunuyorsun.","text":[{"en":"I'll keep the slides to a minimum, because the device makes the case rather better than I do.","tr":"Slaytları en aza indireceğim, çünkü cihaz derdini benden çok daha iyi anlatıyor."},{"en":"What you're looking at is an AI-assisted audiometer, designed to make hearing tests quicker and far more accessible without trading away any clinical accuracy.","tr":"Gördüğünüz şey, klinik doğruluktan hiç ödün vermeden işitme testlerini daha hızlı ve çok daha erişilebilir kılmak için tasarlanmış, yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre."},{"en":"It's our third iteration, and the first, I'm slightly embarrassed to admit, was a laptop and a pair of headphones held together by optimism.","tr":"Bu üçüncü sürümümüz; ilki ise, itiraf etmesi biraz utandırıcı ama, iyimserlikle bir arada tutulan bir dizüstü bilgisayar ve bir kulaklıktı."},{"en":"The core development is behind us, so the work now is less about invention than about removing every reason a cautious buyer might have to say no.","tr":"Temel geliştirme geride kaldı; dolayısıyla artık iş icattan çok, temkinli bir alıcının 'hayır' demesi için olabilecek her gerekçeyi ortadan kaldırmakla ilgili."},{"en":"To that end, we ran a blind study across two university hospitals, with 200 participants aged 18 to 75 tested by both the device and a trained audiologist.","tr":"Bu amaçla iki üniversite hastanesinde, 18-75 yaş arası 200 katılımcının hem cihazla hem de eğitimli bir odyologla test edildiği kör bir çalışma yürüttük."},{"en":"The two agreed in 94% of cases, and the handful of discrepancies were marginal enough that none of them altered a single diagnosis.","tr":"İkisi vakaların %94'ünde uyuştu; birkaç farklılık ise o kadar küçüktü ki hiçbiri tek bir tanıyı bile değiştirmedi."},{"en":"The results appeared in a medical journal last spring, which, for a company our size, carries more weight than any testimonial.","tr":"Sonuçlar geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlandı; bu da bizim ölçeğimizdeki bir şirket için herhangi bir müşteri referansından daha ağır basar."},{"en":"As a Class IIa device, we live or die by the CE mark, and we're working with a seasoned regulatory consultant to get it by the end of next year.","tr":"Sınıf IIa bir cihaz olarak varlığımız CE işaretine bağlı ve bunu gelecek yılın sonuna kadar almak için deneyimli bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışıyoruz."},{"en":"That said, I'd be doing you a disservice if I implied certification timelines were anything other than prone to slippage.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, sertifikasyon takvimlerinin kaymaya meyilli olmadığını ima edersem size haksızlık etmiş olurum."},{"en":"It is, frankly, the biggest risk in the plan, and we've treated it as such.","tr":"Açıkçası bu, plandaki en büyük risk ve ona da öyle davrandık."},{"en":"The €500,000 we're raising is sized to see us through certification and into the European market, with a sensible margin for the unexpected.","tr":"Topladığımız 500.000 €, beklenmedik durumlar için makul bir pay bırakarak bizi sertifikasyondan geçirip Avrupa pazarına taşıyacak şekilde hesaplandı."}],"vocab":[{"en":"make the case","tr":"gerekçeyi ortaya koymak, savunmak","ex":"The device makes the case better than I do.","def":"to give good reasons for something"},{"en":"trade away","tr":"...den ödün vermek","ex":"We didn't trade away any accuracy for speed.","def":"to give up something valuable in exchange for something else"},{"en":"behind us","tr":"geride kaldı","ex":"The core development is behind us.","def":"finished and in the past"},{"en":"to that end","tr":"bu amaçla","ex":"To that end, we ran a blind study.","def":"in order to achieve that aim"},{"en":"marginal","tr":"önemsiz derecede küçük","ex":"The discrepancies were marginal.","def":"very small and not important"},{"en":"carry weight","tr":"ağırlığı olmak, etkili olmak","ex":"A journal publication carries more weight than a testimonial.","def":"to be important and influence people"},{"en":"live or die by","tr":"varlığı tamamen ...e bağlı olmak","ex":"We live or die by the CE mark.","def":"to depend completely on something for success"},{"en":"seasoned","tr":"deneyimli, kurt","ex":"We work with a seasoned regulatory consultant.","def":"having a lot of experience"},{"en":"do someone a disservice","tr":"birine haksızlık etmek","ex":"I'd be doing you a disservice if I hid the risk.","def":"to harm someone, often by not being fully honest"},{"en":"prone to slippage","tr":"kaymaya meyilli","ex":"Certification timelines are prone to slippage.","def":"likely to be delayed"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging with candour: that said, I'd be doing you a disservice, frankly","tr":"C2'de riskleri kabul ederken güvenilir görünmek için ölçülü ama dürüst ifadeler kullanılır. 'That said' önceki olumlu tabloyu dengeler, 'I'd be doing you a disservice if...' nazik bir uyarıdır, 'frankly' açık sözlülüğü işaret eder.","examples":["That said, I'd be doing you a disservice if I implied the timeline was certain.","It is, frankly, the biggest risk in the plan.","The discrepancies were marginal enough that none of them altered a diagnosis."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of 'held together by optimism'?","options":["Anger","Self-deprecating humour","A formal apology"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, what is the main work now?","options":["Inventing the core technology","Building a cheaper laptop version","Removing every reason a cautious buyer might say no"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention that the study was published in a journal?","options":["It gives the results more credibility than a testimonial","Journals pay for studies","To show the team writes well"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'we live or die by the CE mark' imply?","options":["The CE mark is optional","Without the CE mark the business can't succeed in Europe","The CE mark is easy to get"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker openly admit the certification risk?","options":["To lower the valuation","Because the consultant insisted","To delay the deal","To build trust by being candid with the investor"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"The core development is ___ us.","a":"behind","hint":"geride"},{"s":"As a Class IIa device, we live or ___ by the CE mark.","a":"die","hint":"varlığımız ...e bağlı"},{"s":"We work with a ___ regulatory consultant.","a":"seasoned","hint":"deneyimli"},{"s":"Certification timelines are prone to ___.","a":"slippage","hint":"kayma"}],"order":[{"a":"The core development is behind us."},{"a":"It is frankly the biggest risk in the plan."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu, plandaki en büyük risk.","en":"This is the biggest risk in the plan.","keys":["biggest risk","plan"]},{"tr":"Deneyimli bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışıyoruz.","en":"We are working with a seasoned regulatory consultant.","keys":["regulatory consultant"]},{"tr":"Farklar o kadar küçüktü ki hiçbiri tanıyı değiştirmedi.","en":"The differences were so small that none of them changed the diagnosis.","keys":["none of them","diagnosis"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Investor","personaTr":"Yatırımcı","scene":"Londra'da çok sayıda sunum dinlemiş, alaycı ama adil bir yatırımcı prototipini görmek istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll be candid: I've sat through a dozen 'AI diagnostics' pitches this quarter, and most were a slide deck in search of a product.","aiTr":"Açık konuşacağım: bu çeyrekte bir düzine 'yapay zekâ teşhis' sunumu dinledim ve çoğu ürün arayan bir slayt destesiydi.","hint":"Which is exactly why I'd rather let the device make the case: this is our third iteration, and it's been through a blind clinical study.","keys":["make the case","third iteration","blind"]},{"ai":"Go on, then: how did it fare against a human audiologist?","aiTr":"Devam edin o zaman: bir insan odyologa karşı nasıl bir performans gösterdi?","hint":"The two agreed in 94% of cases, and the discrepancies were marginal enough that none altered a diagnosis.","keys":["94","marginal","diagnosis"]},{"ai":"Regulation is where I've watched good companies bleed out, so talk me through yours.","aiTr":"İyi şirketlerin mevzuat yüzünden kan kaybettiğini gördüm; sizinkini bana anlatın.","hint":"As a Class IIa device, we live or die by the CE mark; we're working with a seasoned consultant and targeting the end of next year, though I won't pretend that date is immune to slippage.","keys":["live or die","CE mark","slippage"]},{"ai":"And if I wrote the cheque, what does €500,000 actually get you?","aiTr":"Peki çeki yazsam, 500.000 € size aslında ne kazandırır?","hint":"It's sized to see us through certification and into the European market, with a sensible margin for the unexpected.","keys":["see us through","certification","European market"]}]}},"in-01":{"intro":"Deneyimli yatırımcılar karşısında, retorik açıdan ustalıklı ve doğal bir üç dakikalık sunum yapıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Good afternoon — I'm {name}, and I'd like to start with a figure that tends to stop people in their tracks.","tr":"İyi günler — ben {name}; insanları genellikle olduğu yerde durduran bir rakamla başlamak istiyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"One in five people on the planet lives with some degree of hearing loss — well over a billion of us — and most will go their entire lives without a single test.","tr":"Dünyada her beş kişiden biri bir dereceye kadar işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor — bu bir milyarı rahatlıkla aşan bir sayı — ve çoğu, tüm hayatı boyunca tek bir test bile yaptırmayacak."},{"who":"Me","en":"The bottleneck isn't awareness, and it certainly isn't demand; it's that there are nowhere near enough audiologists to go round.","tr":"Darboğaz farkındalık değil, talep ise hiç değil; sorun, herkese yetecek kadar odyoloğun olmaması."},{"who":"Me","en":"In a small town, the wait for an appointment is measured not in days but in months.","tr":"Küçük bir kasabada randevu için bekleme süresi günlerle değil, aylarla ölçülüyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"At AIHEAR, we've taken the expert out of the room without taking the expertise out of the test.","tr":"AIHEAR'da uzmanı odadan çıkardık, ama uzmanlığı testten çıkarmadık."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our autonomous, AI-assisted audiometer lets the patient put on headphones and simply press a button whenever they hear a tone, while the AI adapts the test in real time.","tr":"Otonom, yapay zekâ destekli odyometremizde hasta kulaklığı takıyor ve bir ses duyduğunda yalnızca düğmeye basıyor; yapay zekâ ise testi gerçek zamanlı olarak uyarlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Inside ten minutes, it delivers a full audiogram — and in a blind study at two university hospitals, it matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","tr":"On dakikanın altında eksiksiz bir odyogram çıkarıyor — ve iki üniversite hastanesinde yapılan kör bir çalışmada vakaların %94'ünde eğitimli bir odyologla aynı sonuca ulaştı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Commercially, the model is deliberately unglamorous: a device sale up front, followed by a monthly software fee that compounds quietly in the background.","tr":"Ticari açıdan model bilinçli olarak gösterişsiz: önce cihaz satışı, ardından arka planda sessizce katlanarak büyüyen aylık bir yazılım ücreti."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're on our third prototype, we have five paying customers, and the six of us cover engineering, medicine and business between us.","tr":"Üçüncü prototipimizdeyiz, beş ödeme yapan müşterimiz var ve altı kişi olarak mühendislik, tıp ve iş alanlarını birlikte kapsıyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're raising €500,000 to carry us through CE certification and into the European market.","tr":"Bizi CE sertifikasyonundan geçirip Avrupa pazarına taşıyacak 500.000 € topluyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Hearing care has never scaled one audiologist at a time, and, with the right partners, it no longer has to.","tr":"İşitme sağlığı hiçbir zaman tek tek odyologlarla ölçeklenemedi ve doğru ortaklarla artık buna gerek de yok."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd be delighted to take your questions.","tr":"Sorularınızı memnuniyetle yanıtlarım."}],"vocab":[{"en":"stop someone in their tracks","tr":"birini olduğu yerde durdurmak, şaşkına çevirmek","ex":"That figure tends to stop people in their tracks.","def":"to make someone suddenly stop and pay attention"},{"en":"go (your) entire life without","tr":"ömür boyu ...meden yaşamak","ex":"Most people go their entire lives without a single test.","def":"to never do or have something at any point in your life"},{"en":"bottleneck","tr":"darboğaz","ex":"The bottleneck isn't demand.","def":"the one point that slows down a whole process"},{"en":"nowhere near enough","tr":"yeterli olmanın çok uzağında","ex":"There are nowhere near enough audiologists.","def":"far less than is needed"},{"en":"to go round","tr":"herkese yetmek","ex":"There aren't enough audiologists to go round.","def":"to be enough for everyone"},{"en":"measured in months","tr":"aylarla ölçülmek","ex":"The wait is measured in months.","def":"lasting so long that you count it in months"},{"en":"up front","tr":"peşin, başta","ex":"Clinics pay for the device up front.","def":"at the beginning, before other payments"},{"en":"unglamorous","tr":"gösterişsiz","ex":"Our business model is deliberately unglamorous.","def":"not exciting, but solid and practical"},{"en":"compound","tr":"katlanarak büyümek","ex":"Recurring fees compound quietly in the background.","def":"to grow faster and faster over time"},{"en":"carry someone through","tr":"birini bir aşamadan geçirmek","ex":"The round will carry us through certification.","def":"to give enough support to reach the end of a stage"}],"grammar":{"title":"Emphatic contrast: not X but Y","tr":"'Not ... but ...' ve 'It isn't X; it's Y' yapıları, dinleyicinin beklentisini düzeltip asıl noktayı vurgular. Güçlü sunumlarda sık kullanılır.","examples":["The wait is measured not in days but in months.","The bottleneck isn't demand; it's the shortage of audiologists.","We've taken the expert out of the room, not the expertise out of the test."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the founder identify as the real bottleneck?","options":["Lack of awareness","Low demand","Too few audiologists"],"a":2},{"q":"What is implied by 'we've taken the expert out of the room without taking the expertise out of the test'?","options":["The device keeps clinical quality without a specialist present","Audiologists are no longer needed anywhere","The test is less accurate than before"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the founder call the business model 'deliberately unglamorous'?","options":["To admit it is not profitable","To present it as simple, solid and predictable","To suggest it will change soon"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the 94% figure meant to show?","options":["Customer satisfaction","Gross margin","Clinical reliability"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of the line about scaling hearing care?","options":["Defensive","Confident and quietly persuasive","Uncertain"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"The ___ isn't awareness, and it certainly isn't demand.","a":"bottleneck","hint":"darboğaz"},{"s":"There are nowhere near enough audiologists to go ___.","a":"round","hint":"herkese yetmek (go round)"},{"s":"The wait is measured not in days but in ___.","a":"months","hint":"aylar"},{"s":"We're raising €500,000 to carry us ___ CE certification.","a":"through","hint":"bir aşamadan geçirmek (carry through)"}],"order":[{"a":"Commercially the model is deliberately unglamorous."},{"a":"We're on our third prototype with five paying customers."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Darboğaz talep değil.","en":"The bottleneck isn't demand.","keys":["bottleneck","isn't demand"]},{"tr":"Bekleme süresi aylarla ölçülüyor.","en":"The wait is measured in months.","keys":["measured in months"]},{"tr":"Uzmanı odadan çıkardık.","en":"We've taken the expert out of the room.","keys":["taken the expert out","the room"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Lead partner at a European VC fund","personaTr":"Avrupalı bir VC fonunun yönetici ortağı","scene":"Sunumdan sonra deneyimli bir yatırımcı iddialarını zorluyor; kısa, zarif ve ikna edici cevaplar ver.","turns":[{"ai":"Lovely story, but autonomous diagnostics is a crowded field — what makes you think you'll be the ones to crack it?","aiTr":"Güzel hikâye, ama otonom teşhis kalabalık bir alan — bunu çözenin siz olacağınızı nereden çıkarıyorsunuz?","hint":"We've taken the expert out of the room without taking the expertise out of the test, and a blind study backs that up.","keys":["expert out of the room","blind study","expertise"]},{"ai":"Ninety-four percent sounds impressive, but what about the other six?","aiTr":"Yüzde doksan dört etkileyici görünüyor, ama ya kalan altı?","hint":"Those differed only slightly, and in none of them did the diagnosis change.","keys":["differed only slightly","diagnosis","none of them"]},{"ai":"Your model sounds rather pedestrian — where's the upside?","aiTr":"Modeliniz biraz sıradan görünüyor — büyüme potansiyeli nerede?","hint":"It's deliberately unglamorous: a device sale up front and a monthly fee that compounds as every new clinic signs on.","keys":["unglamorous","compounds","up front"]},{"ai":"And how far does half a million actually get you?","aiTr":"Peki yarım milyon sizi gerçekte ne kadar ileri götürür?","hint":"It carries us through CE certification and into the European market, which is exactly where growth takes off.","keys":["carries us through","CE certification","European market"]}]}},"st-03":{"intro":"Kusursuz bir cevabı olmayan bir kararı, ironi ve incelikli bir dille savunuyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Last month we had to make the kind of decision that doesn't so much have a right answer as a least-wrong one.","tr":"Geçen ay, doğru bir cevabı olmaktan çok 'en az yanlış' bir cevabı olan türden bir karar vermek zorunda kaldık."},{"en":"The choice was between building our own sales arm to sell directly to hospitals and handing distribution to a partner who already knew the market inside out.","tr":"Seçim, doğrudan hastanelere satmak için kendi satış kolumuzu kurmakla, dağıtımı pazarı avucunun içi gibi bilen bir ortağa devretmek arasındaydı."},{"en":"On paper, going direct was the obvious winner: full margin, a direct line to our customers and nobody else's priorities to contend with.","tr":"Kâğıt üzerinde doğrudan satış açık ara kazanandı: tam kâr marjı, müşterilerle doğrudan bağlantı ve uğraşmamız gereken başka kimsenin öncelikleri yok."},{"en":"In practice, it would have meant two business people trying to do the work of a twenty-strong sales team.","tr":"Pratikte ise bu, iki iş insanının yirmi kişilik bir satış ekibinin işini yapmaya çalışması anlamına gelirdi."},{"en":"The distributor's 20% commission stuck in my throat at first, I'll admit.","tr":"Kabul ediyorum, distribütörün yüzde 20 komisyonu ilk başta içime sinmedi."},{"en":"That said, it buys us relationships it would take years to build ourselves, and it's up for review after twelve months anyway.","tr":"Yine de bu, kendi başımıza kurmamızın yıllar alacağı ilişkileri bize kazandırıyor ve zaten on iki ay sonra yeniden gözden geçirilecek."},{"en":"We went back and forth for a fortnight, and to their credit, nobody on the team held back.","tr":"İki hafta boyunca bir o yana bir bu yana gidip geldik ve hakkını vermek gerekirse ekipte kimse fikrini saklamadı."},{"en":"The engineers made it clear they had no appetite for being dragged into sales calls, and frankly, I couldn't blame them.","tr":"Mühendisler satış görüşmelerine sürüklenmeye hiç hevesleri olmadığını açıkça belirttiler ve açıkçası onları suçlayamazdım."},{"en":"In the end, it came down to time: it's the one thing we can't raise more of, and a deeper-pocketed competitor would happily eat our lunch while we were still hiring.","tr":"Sonunda her şey zamana dayandı: fonunu bulup artıramayacağımız tek şey o ve biz hâlâ işe alım yaparken parası bol bir rakip pastamızı seve seve kapardı."},{"en":"It's hardly a perfect arrangement, but perfect wasn't on the menu.","tr":"Pek kusursuz bir düzenleme sayılmaz ama kusursuz zaten seçenekler arasında yoktu."},{"en":"Put another way, I'd rather keep 80% of something than 100% of nothing.","tr":"Başka bir deyişle, hiçbir şeyin yüzde 100'ündense bir şeyin yüzde 80'ini tutmayı tercih ederim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"on paper","tr":"kâğıt üzerinde, teoride","ex":"On paper, going direct was the obvious winner.","def":"in theory, but maybe not in reality"},{"en":"know something inside out","tr":"bir şeyi avucunun içi gibi bilmek","ex":"The partner knew the market inside out.","def":"to know something extremely well"},{"en":"contend with","tr":"uğraşmak zorunda kalmak","ex":"There were no other priorities to contend with.","def":"to have to deal with a difficulty"},{"en":"stick in your throat","tr":"içine sinmemek, kabullenmesi zor olmak","ex":"The commission stuck in my throat at first.","def":"to be hard to accept"},{"en":"go back and forth","tr":"bir o yana bir bu yana gidip gelmek","ex":"We went back and forth for a fortnight.","def":"to keep arguing both sides without deciding"},{"en":"to their credit","tr":"hakkını vermek gerekirse","ex":"To their credit, nobody on the team held back.","def":"used to praise someone for something they did"},{"en":"have no appetite for","tr":"...e hiç hevesi olmamak","ex":"The engineers had no appetite for sales calls.","def":"to have no wish to do something"},{"en":"come down to","tr":"...e dayanmak, sonuçta ...e bağlı olmak","ex":"In the end, it came down to time.","def":"to depend mainly on one thing"},{"en":"eat someone's lunch","tr":"birinin pastasını kapmak","ex":"A bigger competitor would happily eat our lunch.","def":"(informal) to beat a competitor and take their business"},{"en":"deep-pocketed","tr":"parası bol","ex":"A deeper-pocketed competitor could get there first.","def":"having a lot of money to spend"}],"grammar":{"title":"Conceding a point: I'll admit / That said / hardly","tr":"Akıcı konuşanlar karşı tarafın itirazını önce kabul edip sonra kendi görüşünü öne çıkarır: 'I'll admit' (kabul ediyorum), 'That said' (yine de), 'hardly' (pek değil). Bu, savunmacı değil, olgun bir ton verir.","examples":["The commission stuck in my throat at first, I'll admit.","That said, it buys us relationships it would take years to build.","It's hardly a perfect arrangement, but perfect wasn't on the menu."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why was going direct unrealistic in practice?","options":["Hospitals refused to buy directly","Two business people would have had to do the work of a large sales team","The engineers wanted to sell instead"],"a":1},{"q":"What makes the 20% commission easier to accept?","options":["It buys valuable relationships and is reviewed after twelve months","It's lower than the market average","The distributor pays it back later"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by 'it's the one thing we can't raise more of'?","options":["They've given up on raising investment","The team works too few hours","Unlike money, lost time can't be won back from investors"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of 'perfect wasn't on the menu'?","options":["Bitter and regretful","Pragmatic and slightly wry","Excited and optimistic"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'I'd rather keep 80% of something than 100% of nothing' suggest?","options":["They would prefer not to pay any commission","They think the distributor is overcharging","Giving up some margin is worth it to actually reach the market"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"On ___, going direct was the obvious winner.","a":"paper","hint":"kâğıt üzerinde"},{"s":"We went back and ___ for a fortnight.","a":"forth","hint":"gidip gelmek"},{"s":"In the end, it came ___ to time.","a":"down","hint":"...e dayanmak"},{"s":"A deeper-pocketed competitor would happily eat our ___.","a":"lunch","hint":"pastamızı kapmak"}],"order":[{"a":"The engineers had no appetite for sales calls."},{"a":"In the end it came down to time."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kâğıt üzerinde doğrudan satış açık ara kazanandı.","en":"On paper, going direct was the obvious winner.","keys":["on paper","going direct"]},{"tr":"Komisyon başta içime sinmedi, kabul ediyorum.","en":"The commission stuck in my throat at first, I'll admit.","keys":["stuck in my throat","I'll admit"]},{"tr":"Sonuçta her şey zamana dayandı.","en":"In the end, it all came down to time.","keys":["came down to time"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Co-founder","personaTr":"Kurucu ortak","scene":"Kurucu ortağın bilerek şeytanın avukatlığını yapıyor ve kararını her açıdan sınıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Play devil's advocate with me: why not just go direct and keep the whole margin?","aiTr":"Benimle şeytanın avukatlığını yap: neden doğrudan satıp tüm marjı kendimize saklamıyoruz?","hint":"On paper it's the obvious winner, but in practice it would mean two business people trying to do the work of a twenty-strong sales team.","keys":["on paper","in practice","sales team"]},{"ai":"Still, handing over 20% sticks in my throat.","aiTr":"Yine de yüzde 20'yi vermek içime sinmiyor.","hint":"I'll admit it stuck in mine too; that said, it buys us relationships it would take years to build, and it's up for review after twelve months.","keys":["that said","relationships","review"]},{"ai":"Couldn't the engineers pitch in on sales for a few months?","aiTr":"Mühendisler birkaç ay satışa el atamaz mı?","hint":"They've made it clear they have no appetite for sales calls, and frankly, I can't blame them.","keys":["no appetite","can't blame","sales calls"]},{"ai":"So, bottom line, what's the real reason?","aiTr":"Peki özetle, asıl sebep ne?","hint":"It comes down to time: it's the one thing we can't raise more of, and I'd rather keep 80% of something than 100% of nothing.","keys":["comes down to time","raise more of","of nothing"]}]}},"te-02":{"intro":"Deneyimli ve şüpheci bir CTO'ya, yapay zekâ kod asistanlarına ne kadar ve nasıl güvendiğinizi ölçülü, ironik ve teknik bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Two years ago, our three engineers wrote every line by hand, which in hindsight feels faintly quaint.","tr":"İki yıl önce üç mühendisimiz her satırı elle yazıyordu; geriye dönüp bakınca bu biraz eski moda geliyor."},{"en":"These days, an AI assistant produces most first drafts, and the craft has shifted from typing code to specifying intent and interrogating the result.","tr":"Bugünlerde ilk taslakların çoğunu bir yapay zekâ asistanı üretiyor; zanaat da kod yazmaktan, amacı tanımlamaya ve sonucu sorgulamaya kaydı."},{"en":"Give it a well-framed brief in plain English and it will hand back a plausible implementation before you've finished your coffee.","tr":"Ona sade İngilizceyle iyi kurgulanmış bir görev tanımı verin, daha kahvenizi bitirmeden size akla yatkın bir uygulama sunar."},{"en":"It's equally adept at untangling legacy code and flagging bugs that a bleary-eyed human would sail straight past.","tr":"Eski kodu çözmekte ve uykusuz bir insanın hiç fark etmeden geçip gideceği hataları işaretlemekte de aynı derecede usta."},{"en":"The net effect is that work which once took a week now tends to land in a day or two.","tr":"Net etki şu: Eskiden bir hafta süren iş artık genellikle bir iki günde tamamlanıyor."},{"en":"The catch, of course, is that the assistant is at its most dangerous precisely when it sounds most sure of itself.","tr":"İşin püf noktası elbette, asistanın tam da kendinden en emin göründüğü anda en tehlikeli olması."},{"en":"Its mistakes are rarely the clumsy kind; they're plausible, idiomatic and wrong in ways that only surface under load or at the edges.","tr":"Hataları nadiren kaba saba olur; akla yatkın, dile uygun ve ancak yük altında ya da uç durumlarda ortaya çıkan şekillerde yanlıştır."},{"en":"On a medical device, 'it seemed to work' is not a defense anyone wants to mount in front of a notified body.","tr":"Bir tıbbi cihazda 'çalışıyor gibiydi' kimsenin onaylanmış bir kuruluşun önünde öne sürmek isteyeceği bir savunma değil."},{"en":"So nothing reaches the device without human review, a full automated test suite and a paper trail that would satisfy the most pedantic auditor.","tr":"Bu yüzden hiçbir şey insan incelemesi, eksiksiz bir otomatik test paketi ve en kılı kırk yaran denetçiyi bile tatmin edecek bir belge izi olmadan cihaza ulaşmıyor."},{"en":"If that sounds like it erodes the time savings, it does, but only at the margins.","tr":"Bu, kazanılan zamanı aşındırıyor gibi geliyorsa, evet aşındırıyor, ama yalnızca çok küçük ölçüde."},{"en":"Weighed against what we'd pay for three more engineers, it's a trade-off I'd make again without a second thought.","tr":"Üç mühendis daha için ödeyeceğimiz parayla kıyaslandığında, bu ödünleşimi hiç düşünmeden yine yapardım."},{"en":"That said, I'd stop short of calling the tools a replacement for engineers; they're a lever, and a lever is only as good as the hand on it.","tr":"Yine de bu araçlara mühendislerin yerine geçen şey demem; onlar bir kaldıraç ve bir kaldıraç ancak onu tutan el kadar iyidir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"in hindsight","tr":"geriye dönüp bakınca","ex":"In hindsight, writing everything by hand was slow.","def":"when you think about the past with what you know now"},{"en":"quaint","tr":"eski moda, tuhaf biçimde sevimli","ex":"Writing every line by hand now feels quaint.","def":"attractively old-fashioned or unusual"},{"en":"interrogate","tr":"sorgulamak","ex":"Engineers have to interrogate every result.","def":"to examine something very closely and critically"},{"en":"adept at","tr":"...de usta, becerikli","ex":"The assistant is adept at untangling legacy code.","def":"skilled at something"},{"en":"sail straight past","tr":"fark etmeden geçip gitmek","ex":"A tired reviewer might sail straight past the bug.","def":"to pass something without noticing it"},{"en":"the catch","tr":"işin püf noktası, gizli dezavantaj","ex":"The catch is that it sounds confident when it's wrong.","def":"a hidden problem or disadvantage"},{"en":"surface","tr":"ortaya çıkmak","ex":"Some errors only surface under load.","def":"to become visible or known"},{"en":"pedantic","tr":"kılı kırk yaran, aşırı titiz","ex":"Our paper trail would satisfy the most pedantic auditor.","def":"too concerned with small details or rules"},{"en":"at the margins","tr":"çok küçük ölçüde","ex":"Reviews reduce our time savings only at the margins.","def":"only slightly, in small ways"},{"en":"stop short of","tr":"...e kadar gitmemek","ex":"I'd stop short of calling it a replacement for engineers.","def":"to almost do something but decide not to"}],"grammar":{"title":"Measured claims: hedging with precision","tr":"'tends to', 'at the margins', 'I'd stop short of…' gibi ifadeler iddianı abartmadan, tam olarak ne kadar emin olduğunu gösterir. Teknik dinleyiciler bu dürüstlüğü güven işareti olarak görür.","examples":["Work which once took a week now tends to land in a day or two.","It erodes the time savings, but only at the margins.","I'd stop short of calling the tools a replacement for engineers."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of 'in hindsight feels faintly quaint'?","options":["Bitter","Gently self-mocking","Angry","Sad and nostalgic"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, when is the assistant most dangerous?","options":["When it is slow","When it refuses to answer","When it sounds most confident","When the brief is in English"],"a":2},{"q":"What kind of mistakes does the assistant typically make?","options":["Plausible errors that only show up in edge cases or under load","Obvious syntax errors","Spelling mistakes in comments"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by saying 'it seemed to work' is not a defense anyone wants to mount?","options":["Notified bodies don't review software","The team often uses that excuse","Testing is optional for small startups","Regulators expect rigorous evidence, not impressions"],"a":3},{"q":"Why does the speaker call the tools 'a lever'?","options":["They replace engineers entirely","They amplify skilled engineers but depend on them","They are cheap to buy","They are hard to use"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"We wrote every line by hand, which in ___ feels faintly quaint.","a":"hindsight","hint":"geriye dönüp bakınca (in …)"},{"s":"It's equally ___ at untangling legacy code.","a":"adept","hint":"usta"},{"s":"If that sounds like it erodes the time savings, it does, but only at the ___.","a":"margins","hint":"çok küçük ölçüde (at the …)"},{"s":"I'd stop ___ of calling the tools a replacement for engineers.","a":"short","hint":"...e kadar gitmemek (stop … of)"}],"order":[{"a":"Nothing reaches the device without human review."},{"a":"A lever is only as good as the hand on it."}],"translate":[{"tr":"İşin püf noktası, asistanın kendinden en emin göründüğü anda en tehlikeli olması.","en":"The catch is that the assistant is at its most dangerous when it sounds most sure of itself.","keys":["the catch","most dangerous"]},{"tr":"Hataları nadiren kaba saba olur; akla yatkın ama yanlıştır.","en":"Its mistakes are rarely clumsy; they're plausible but wrong.","keys":["rarely clumsy","plausible"]},{"tr":"Bu ödünleşimi hiç düşünmeden yine yapardım.","en":"I'd make that trade-off again without a second thought.","keys":["trade-off","without a second thought"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Seasoned CTO","personaTr":"Deneyimli CTO (danışman)","scene":"Deneyimli ve şüpheci bir CTO, danışma kurulu toplantısında yapay zekâya bu kadar dayanmanın akıllıca olup olmadığını sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Be straight with me: aren't you just outsourcing your engineering to a chatbot?","aiTr":"Bana dürüst olun: Mühendisliğinizi bir sohbet robotuna devretmiyor musunuz?","hint":"Not quite. The assistant produces most first drafts, but the craft has shifted to specifying intent and interrogating the result.","keys":["first drafts","specifying intent","interrogating"]},{"ai":"In my experience, these tools are confidently wrong more often than people admit.","aiTr":"Deneyimime göre bu araçlar, insanların kabul ettiğinden daha sık, kendinden emin bir şekilde yanılıyor.","hint":"I couldn't agree more. The catch is that it's most dangerous when it sounds most sure of itself, and its mistakes tend to be plausible rather than clumsy.","keys":["the catch","plausible","most dangerous"]},{"ai":"So how do you keep that from ever reaching a medical device?","aiTr":"Peki bunun bir tıbbi cihaza ulaşmasını nasıl engelliyorsunuz?","hint":"Nothing reaches the device without human review, a full automated test suite and a paper trail that would satisfy the most pedantic auditor.","keys":["human review","test suite","paper trail"]},{"ai":"Doesn't all that process eat up the time you supposedly save?","aiTr":"Bütün bu süreç, güya kazandığınız zamanı yiyip bitirmiyor mu?","hint":"It does, but only at the margins, and weighed against the cost of three more engineers, I'd make that trade-off again without a second thought.","keys":["at the margins","trade-off","three more engineers"]}]}},"co-02":{"intro":"Kısa, zarif ve kendinden emin bir takip e-postasıyla konferanstaki sohbeti bir demo randevusuna dönüştürüyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Subject: Waiting lists, and a possible demo","tr":"Konu: Bekleme listeleri ve olası bir demo"},{"en":"Dear Sarah,","tr":"Sevgili Sarah,"},{"en":"Many thanks for your time at MedTech Europe yesterday; it was a genuine pleasure.","tr":"Dün MedTech Europe'ta ayırdığınız zaman için çok teşekkürler; gerçekten büyük bir zevkti."},{"en":"Your account of the waiting lists in your hospitals has stayed with me, not least because it is precisely the problem we set out to solve.","tr":"Hastanelerinizdeki bekleme listeleri hakkında anlattıklarınız aklımdan çıkmadı; özellikle de tam olarak çözmek için yola çıktığımız sorun bu olduğu için."},{"en":"As promised, I've attached a short overview of our autonomous audiometer, including the headline results from our clinical study.","tr":"Söz verdiğim gibi, klinik çalışmamızın öne çıkan sonuçlarını da içeren, otonom odyometremize dair kısa bir özet ekledim."},{"en":"That said, a device like ours is far better seen than described, so I'd welcome the chance to show it to you and your team in a brief online demo.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, bizimki gibi bir cihaz anlatılmaktan çok görülmeyi hak ediyor; bu yüzden onu size ve ekibinize kısa bir çevrimiçi demoyla gösterme fırsatını memnuniyetle karşılarım."},{"en":"Thirty minutes should be ample, with plenty of time left for your team's questions.","tr":"Otuz dakika fazlasıyla yeterli olur; ekibinizin soruları için de bolca zaman kalır."},{"en":"Next Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon would suit me, though I'm happy to work around your diary if neither is convenient.","tr":"Gelecek salı veya çarşamba öğleden sonra bana uyar; ikisi de size uygun değilse takviminize göre ayarlayabilirim."},{"en":"Should any questions arise in the meantime, I'm only an email away.","tr":"Bu arada aklınıza bir soru gelirse, bir e-posta uzaklığındayım."},{"en":"I look forward to picking up where we left off.","tr":"Kaldığımız yerden devam etmeyi dört gözle bekliyorum."},{"en":"Best wishes, {name}","tr":"En iyi dileklerimle, {name}"}],"vocab":[{"en":"stay with someone","tr":"birinin aklından çıkmamak","ex":"Your account of the waiting lists has stayed with me.","def":"to be remembered for a long time because it made an impression"},{"en":"not least because","tr":"özellikle de ... olduğu için","ex":"It stayed with me, not least because it's the problem we solve.","def":"partly, and importantly, because"},{"en":"set out to","tr":"...mek için yola çıkmak","ex":"It's precisely the problem we set out to solve.","def":"to start doing something with a clear aim"},{"en":"headline results","tr":"öne çıkan sonuçlar","ex":"The overview includes the headline results from our study.","def":"the most important findings, in short form"},{"en":"better seen than described","tr":"anlatılmaktansa görülmesi daha iyi","ex":"A device like ours is far better seen than described.","def":"easier to understand by watching it than by reading about it"},{"en":"welcome the chance to","tr":"...me fırsatını memnuniyetle karşılamak","ex":"I'd welcome the chance to show you the device.","def":"to be very happy to have an opportunity"},{"en":"ample","tr":"fazlasıyla yeterli","ex":"Thirty minutes should be ample.","def":"more than enough"},{"en":"work around someone's diary","tr":"birinin takvimine göre ayarlamak","ex":"I'm happy to work around your diary.","def":"to fit your plans to the times another person is free"},{"en":"be only an email away","tr":"bir e-posta uzaklıkta olmak, kolayca ulaşılabilir olmak","ex":"If anything comes up, I'm only an email away.","def":"to be very easy to contact"},{"en":"pick up where we left off","tr":"kaldığımız yerden devam etmek","ex":"I look forward to picking up where we left off.","def":"to continue something from the point where it stopped"}],"grammar":{"title":"Subtle emphasis: not least, precisely, far better","tr":"C2'de vurgu bağırarak değil, ince ifadelerle yapılır: 'not least because' (özellikle de … çünkü), 'precisely' (tam da), 'far better' (çok daha iyi). Bunlar e-postaya kibar ama kendinden emin bir ton verir.","examples":["It has stayed with me, not least because it is precisely the problem we set out to solve.","A device like ours is far better seen than described.","Thirty minutes should be ample."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'Your account of the waiting lists has stayed with me' suggest?","options":["The writer forgot most of the conversation","The conversation made a lasting impression on the writer","Sarah sent a written report"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the writer say the device is 'far better seen than described'?","options":["To justify asking for a live demo","To admit the overview is poor","To avoid sharing the study data"],"a":0},{"q":"What is attached to the email?","options":["A contract and a price list","A recording of the conference","A short overview, including headline clinical results"],"a":2},{"q":"How would you describe the tone of the email?","options":["Urgent and pushy","Casual and chatty","Stiff and bureaucratic","Polished, warm and unhurried"],"a":3},{"q":"What does 'I'm happy to work around your diary' imply?","options":["The writer will adapt to Sarah's availability","The writer wants to see Sarah's diary","Sarah must choose Tuesday"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"It has stayed with me, not ___ because it is precisely the problem we set out to solve.","a":"least","hint":"özellikle de"},{"s":"A device like ours is far better seen than ___.","a":"described","hint":"anlatılmak"},{"s":"I'm happy to work around your ___ if neither is convenient.","a":"diary","hint":"takvim, ajanda"},{"s":"Should any questions ___ in the meantime, I'm only an email away.","a":"arise","hint":"ortaya çıkmak"}],"order":[{"a":"I look forward to picking up where we left off."},{"a":"Thirty minutes should be ample."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sohbetimiz aklımdan çıkmadı.","en":"Our conversation has stayed with me.","keys":["stayed with me"]},{"tr":"Takviminize göre ayarlamaktan memnuniyet duyarım.","en":"I'm happy to work around your diary.","keys":["work around","diary"]},{"tr":"Bana her zaman e-postayla ulaşabilirsiniz.","en":"I'm only an email away.","keys":["only an email away"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Sarah (by email)","personaTr":"Sarah (e-posta ile)","scene":"Sarah ilgiyle yanıt veriyor; demo ayrıntılarını kısa, zarif ve net cümlelerle karara bağlıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Dear {name}, thank you for the overview. The headline results are impressive, and I'd certainly be interested in a demo.","aiTr":"Sevgili {name}, özet için teşekkürler. Öne çıkan sonuçlar etkileyici ve bir demoyla kesinlikle ilgilenirim.","hint":"That's very kind. Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon would suit me, though I'm happy to work around your diary.","keys":["work around","diary","Tuesday","Wednesday"]},{"ai":"Wednesday at 2 pm would be ideal. Who would you suggest we bring along?","aiTr":"Çarşamba 14:00 ideal olur. Kimi de getirmemizi önerirsiniz?","hint":"I'd suggest your clinic manager and one of your audiologists, since they'd be the ones using it day to day.","keys":["clinic manager","audiologists","day to day"]},{"ai":"And how long should we set aside?","aiTr":"Peki ne kadar zaman ayırmalıyız?","hint":"Thirty minutes should be ample, with plenty of time left for your team's questions.","keys":["thirty minutes","ample","questions"]},{"ai":"Perfect. Please send over an invitation when you have a moment.","aiTr":"Mükemmel. Fırsat bulduğunuzda bir davet gönderin lütfen.","hint":"Of course; I'll send a calendar invitation shortly, and should any questions arise before then, I'm only an email away.","keys":["calendar invitation","only an email away","should any questions arise"]}]}},"ab-03":{"intro":"Doktora belirtilerini son derece kesin ve incelikli bir dille anlatıyorsun; doktor dürüstçe tavsiye veriyor, sen de kendinle dalga geçerek karşılık veriyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Dr Hoffmann's practice, good morning.","tr":"Dr. Hoffmann'ın muayenehanesi, günaydın."},{"who":"Me","en":"Good morning—I've had a persistent ache in my lower back for the best part of three weeks, and I wondered whether the doctor might squeeze me in this week.","tr":"Günaydın; neredeyse üç haftadır belimde inatçı bir ağrı var, doktorun beni bu hafta araya sıkıştırıp sıkıştıramayacağını merak ettim."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Barring an emergency, Thursday at 9:30 is the earliest I can do, and you'll need to bring your health insurance card.","tr":"Acil bir durum olmadıkça verebileceğim en erken saat perşembe 9.30; sağlık sigortası kartınızı da getirmeniz gerekecek."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"So, what's brought you in?","tr":"Evet, sizi buraya ne getirdi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"In a nutshell, I've spent the past three weeks working twelve-hour days at my kitchen table, our office furniture being apparently lost somewhere between the warehouse and Berlin.","tr":"Kısacası son üç haftayı mutfak masasında günde on iki saat çalışarak geçirdim, çünkü ofis mobilyalarımız anlaşılan depoyla Berlin arasında bir yerde kayıp."},{"who":"Me","en":"It started as a vague stiffness, but by the evening it's a solid six out of ten, and long stretches of sitting make it noticeably worse.","tr":"Belli belirsiz bir tutulma olarak başladı, ama akşama doğru on üzerinden net bir altı oluyor ve uzun süre oturmak onu belirgin şekilde kötüleştiriyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"My sleep, if I'm honest, has gone to pieces as well—I'm wide awake by four, mentally drafting emails.","tr":"Dürüst olmak gerekirse uykum da darmadağın oldu; saat dörtte gözüm fal taşı gibi açık, kafamda e-posta taslakları yazıyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"Ibuprofen a few times a week dulls it for a few hours, but I'm conscious that I'm treating the symptom rather than the cause.","tr":"Haftada birkaç kez ibuprofen ağrıyı birkaç saatliğine köreltiyor, ama sorunun kaynağını değil belirtisini tedavi ettiğimin farkındayım."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"Well, the good news is that, tense as those muscles are, there's no indication whatsoever of nerve involvement.","tr":"İyi haber şu ki, o kaslar ne kadar gergin olsa da sinir tutulumuna dair hiçbir belirti yok."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"I'll give you a prescription for an anti-inflammatory gel, which any pharmacy will fill, though I'd be doing you a disservice if I let you think that was the cure.","tr":"Size iltihap giderici bir jel için reçete vereceğim, her eczane karşılar; ama bunun tedavi olduğunu düşünmenize izin verirsem size kötülük etmiş olurum."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"Get up every hour, walk for thirty minutes a day and banish screens from the bedroom after ten—and if it hasn't eased in two weeks, come back.","tr":"Her saat kalkın, günde otuz dakika yürüyün ve saat ondan sonra ekranları yatak odasından kovun; iki hafta içinde hafiflemezse tekrar gelin."},{"who":"Me","en":"Rather humblingly, that's almost word for word the routine I used to swear by before I moved.","tr":"Biraz utandırıcı ama bu, taşınmadan önce yeminle savunduğum rutinin neredeyse kelimesi kelimesine aynısı."}],"vocab":[{"en":"the best part of","tr":"neredeyse tamamı","ex":"I've had it for the best part of three weeks.","def":"most of a period of time"},{"en":"squeeze someone in","tr":"araya sıkıştırmak","ex":"Could the doctor squeeze me in this week?","def":"to find time for someone in a busy schedule"},{"en":"barring","tr":"...olmadıkça","ex":"Barring an emergency, Thursday is the earliest.","def":"unless something happens; except for"},{"en":"in a nutshell","tr":"kısacası","ex":"In a nutshell, I've been working too much.","def":"in a few words"},{"en":"go to pieces","tr":"darmadağın olmak","ex":"My sleep has gone to pieces.","def":"to become very bad or fall apart"},{"en":"treat the symptom rather than the cause","tr":"sorunun kaynağını değil belirtisini tedavi etmek","ex":"Painkillers treat the symptom rather than the cause.","def":"to deal with the effects of a problem, not its origin"},{"en":"no indication whatsoever","tr":"hiçbir belirti yok","ex":"There's no indication whatsoever of nerve damage.","def":"absolutely no sign of something"},{"en":"fill a prescription","tr":"reçeteyi karşılamak","ex":"Any pharmacy will fill the prescription.","def":"to give a patient the medicine written on a prescription"},{"en":"do someone a disservice","tr":"birine kötülük etmek","ex":"I'd be doing you a disservice if I didn't tell you.","def":"to harm someone, often by not being honest with them"},{"en":"swear by","tr":"bir şeye çok güvenmek","ex":"I used to swear by that routine.","def":"to believe strongly that something works well"}],"grammar":{"title":"Concessive clauses: tense as they are","tr":"'Although they are tense' yerine 'tense as they are' demek daha zarif ve vurgulu bir zıtlık kurar. Sıfat başa gelir, ardından 'as + özne + fiil' gelir.","examples":["Tense as those muscles are, there's no sign of nerve involvement.","Tired as I was, I couldn't get back to sleep.","Useful as ibuprofen is, it only treats the symptom."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is implied about the office furniture?","options":["It has been delivered","It seems to be stuck somewhere in transit","It was never ordered"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the speaker's attitude towards the ibuprofen?","options":["They know it only masks the problem","They think it's a cure","They refuse to take it"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the doctor mean by 'I'd be doing you a disservice'?","options":["The gel is expensive","The pharmacy may be closed","It would be misleading to present the gel as a cure"],"a":2},{"q":"What does 'mentally drafting emails' suggest?","options":["The speaker writes emails at night","Work worries keep the speaker awake","The speaker loves email"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of the speaker's final remark?","options":["Defensive irritation","Cheerful indifference","Open disbelief","Rueful self-awareness"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"I've had a persistent ache for the best ___ of three weeks.","a":"part","hint":"neredeyse tamamı"},{"s":"___ an emergency, Thursday at 9:30 is the earliest I can do.","a":"Barring","hint":"...olmadıkça"},{"s":"My sleep has gone to ___ as well.","a":"pieces","hint":"darmadağın olmak"},{"s":"Tense ___ those muscles are, there's no sign of nerve involvement.","a":"as","hint":"-e rağmen (ne kadar … olsa da)"}],"order":[{"a":"Any pharmacy will fill the prescription."},{"a":"I'm treating the symptom rather than the cause."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kısacası üç haftadır mutfak masasında çalışıyorum.","en":"In a nutshell, I've been working at my kitchen table for three weeks.","keys":["in a nutshell","kitchen table"]},{"tr":"Sinir tutulumuna dair hiçbir belirti yok.","en":"There's no indication whatsoever of nerve involvement.","keys":["no indication whatsoever","nerve"]},{"tr":"Taşınmadan önce bu rutine çok güvenirdim.","en":"I used to swear by this routine before I moved.","keys":["used to swear by","routine"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Doctor","personaTr":"Doktor","scene":"Dr. Hoffmann'ın muayene odasındasın. Doktor dikkatli ve doğrudan; belirtilerini olabildiğince kesin anlatıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Do sit down—so what's been troubling you?","aiTr":"Buyurun oturun; sizi rahatsız eden ne?","hint":"A persistent ache in my lower back for the best part of three weeks, and my sleep has gone to pieces too.","keys":["lower back","best part of three weeks","gone to pieces"]},{"ai":"Can you characterise the pain—sharp, burning, or more of a dull ache?","aiTr":"Ağrıyı tarif edebilir misiniz; keskin mi, yanıcı mı, yoksa daha çok hafif bir sızı mı?","hint":"Predominantly a dull ache, though it can creep up to a six out of ten after a long day at the desk.","keys":["dull ache","six out of ten","after a long day"]},{"ai":"And the sleep—is it getting to sleep that's the problem, or staying asleep?","aiTr":"Peki uyku; sorun uykuya dalmak mı, yoksa uykuda kalmak mı?","hint":"Staying asleep, without question—I'm wide awake by four with my mind already at work.","keys":["staying asleep","wide awake","by four"]},{"ai":"I'll write you a prescription for a gel, but I'd rather you changed your habits than relied on it. Fair?","aiTr":"Size bir jel için reçete yazacağım, ama ona güvenmektense alışkanlıklarınızı değiştirmenizi tercih ederim. Makul mü?","hint":"Entirely fair—I'll take the gel, but I take your point that the real cure lies in how I work.","keys":["entirely fair","take your point","how I work"]}]}},"in-02":{"intro":"İş modelini deneyimli bir yatırımcıya hem kesin hem ihtiyatlı, ustalıklı bir dille savunuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"However the conversation with an investor begins, it invariably circles back to one question: where, exactly, does the money come from?","tr":"Bir yatırımcıyla konuşma nasıl başlarsa başlasın, kaçınılmaz olarak tek bir soruya döner: Para tam olarak nereden geliyor?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Our answer has two parts, and the interesting part isn't the one people expect.","tr":"Cevabımız iki kısımdan oluşuyor ve ilginç olan kısım, insanların beklediği kısım değil."},{"who":"Me","en":"We sell each device for €4,000 against a production cost of around €1,500, which leaves a gross margin in the region of 60 percent.","tr":"Her cihazı yaklaşık 1.500 €'luk üretim maliyetine karşılık 4.000 €'ya satıyoruz; bu da yüzde 60 civarında bir brüt marj bırakıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Respectable, certainly, but hardware margins on their own have never made anyone's pulse race.","tr":"Saygın bir oran, kuşkusuz, ama donanım marjları tek başına hiç kimsenin nabzını hızlandırmamıştır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Where the model really earns its keep is the €99 a month that every clinic pays for the software.","tr":"Modelin asıl hakkını verdiği yer, her kliniğin yazılım için ödediği ayda 99 €."},{"who":"Me","en":"It's a modest sum, admittedly, yet it recurs, it compounds, and once a clinic has built its workflow around us, it has little reason to walk away.","tr":"Mütevazı bir meblağ, kabul; ama tekrarlanıyor, katlanarak büyüyor ve bir klinik iş akışını bizim etrafımızda kurduktan sonra ayrılmak için pek bir nedeni kalmıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Extrapolate to 1,000 clinics, and the subscriptions alone would come to roughly €1.2 million a year.","tr":"Bunu 1.000 kliniğe yansıtın, yalnızca abonelikler yılda yaklaşık 1,2 milyon €'ya ulaşır."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, with five paying customers today, I'm acutely aware that this is a projection, not a promise.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, bugün beş ödeme yapan müşterimiz varken bunun bir söz değil, bir projeksiyon olduğunun fazlasıyla farkındayım."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our costs are, unsurprisingly, dominated by salaries, certification and marketing — the last two being heavily front-loaded.","tr":"Maliyetlerimizde, şaşırtıcı olmayan şekilde, maaşlar, sertifikasyon ve pazarlama ağır basıyor — son ikisi büyük ölçüde en başta yoğunlaşıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Put differently, the years in which we spend most are precisely the years in which we build the recurring base we'll later live off.","tr":"Başka bir deyişle, en çok harcadığımız yıllar, ileride geçimimizi sağlayacak tekrarlayan gelir tabanını kurduğumuz yıllarla tam olarak aynı."},{"who":"Me","en":"On our current numbers, we expect to cross into profitability in year three — no sooner, and, barring regulatory surprises, no later.","tr":"Mevcut rakamlarımıza göre üçüncü yılda kâra geçmeyi bekliyoruz — daha erken değil ve düzenleyici bir sürpriz olmazsa daha geç de değil."}],"vocab":[{"en":"circle back to","tr":"...e geri dönmek","ex":"Every conversation circles back to revenue.","def":"to return to a topic discussed before"},{"en":"in the region of","tr":"civarında, yaklaşık","ex":"The margin is in the region of 60 percent.","def":"approximately"},{"en":"make someone's pulse race","tr":"birinin nabzını hızlandırmak, heyecanlandırmak","ex":"Hardware margins rarely make anyone's pulse race.","def":"to excite someone"},{"en":"earn its keep","tr":"hakkını vermek, maliyetini çıkarmak","ex":"The software fee is where the model earns its keep.","def":"to be worth the money or effort spent on it"},{"en":"walk away","tr":"bırakıp gitmek, vazgeçmek","ex":"A clinic has little reason to walk away.","def":"to leave or end a relationship"},{"en":"extrapolate","tr":"mevcut veriden ileriye yansıtmak","ex":"Extrapolate to 1,000 clinics, and the numbers look very different.","def":"to estimate future figures from current ones"},{"en":"acutely aware","tr":"fazlasıyla farkında","ex":"I'm acutely aware that this is a projection.","def":"very conscious of something"},{"en":"projection","tr":"projeksiyon, öngörü","ex":"This is a projection, not a promise.","def":"an estimate of future results"},{"en":"be dominated by","tr":"...nin ağırlığında olmak","ex":"Our costs are dominated by salaries.","def":"to be mostly made up of something"},{"en":"barring","tr":"...olmazsa, ...hariç","ex":"Barring regulatory surprises, we'll be profitable in year three.","def":"unless something happens"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging with precision: in the region of, barring, admittedly","tr":"C2 düzeyinde rakamları ve tahminleri hem kesin hem ihtiyatlı sunmak gerekir: 'in the region of' yaklaşıklığı, 'barring' bir koşulu, 'admittedly' bir kabulü zarifçe ifade eder.","examples":["The gross margin is in the region of 60 percent.","Barring regulatory surprises, we'll be profitable in year three.","It's a modest sum, admittedly, yet it recurs."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'the interesting part isn't the one people expect'?","options":["The device price is surprisingly high","The software fee matters more than the hardware sale","The company has a secret third revenue stream"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the speaker regard the 60% hardware margin?","options":["Respectable but not exciting","Exceptional and unique","Worryingly low"],"a":0},{"q":"Why would a clinic have 'little reason to walk away'?","options":["It signs a ten-year contract","It gets the software for free","Its workflow is built around the system"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of 'this is a projection, not a promise'?","options":["Defensive and evasive","Candid and measured","Overconfident"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'barring regulatory surprises, no later' imply?","options":["Certification delays are the main risk to the timeline","The company has already been certified","Regulators have promised quick approval"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"It invariably circles ___ to one question.","a":"back","hint":"geri dönmek (circle back)"},{"s":"That leaves a gross margin in the ___ of 60 percent.","a":"region","hint":"civarında (in the region of)"},{"s":"Where the model really earns its ___ is the monthly fee.","a":"keep","hint":"hakkını vermek (earn its keep)"},{"s":"___ regulatory surprises, we'll be profitable in year three.","a":"Barring","hint":"...olmazsa"}],"order":[{"a":"I'm acutely aware that this is a projection."},{"a":"The interesting part isn't the one people expect."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu bir söz değil, bir projeksiyon.","en":"This is a projection, not a promise.","keys":["projection","not a promise"]},{"tr":"Düzenleyici sürprizler olmazsa üçüncü yılda kâra geçeceğiz.","en":"Barring regulatory surprises, we'll turn profitable in year three.","keys":["barring","year three"]},{"tr":"Bir kliniğin ayrılmak için pek bir nedeni yok.","en":"A clinic has little reason to walk away.","keys":["little reason","walk away"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Partner at a health-tech VC fund","personaTr":"Sağlık teknolojisi odaklı bir VC fonunun ortağı","scene":"Deneyimli bir yatırımcı iş modelini sorgulayarak zayıf noktaları arıyor; ölçülü, net ve ikna edici ol.","turns":[{"ai":"Hardware is notoriously hard to scale — why shouldn't I simply pass on this?","aiTr":"Donanımı ölçeklemek bilindiği üzere zordur — neden bu fırsatı doğrudan geri çevirmeyeyim?","hint":"Because the hardware isn't where the model earns its keep; it's the €99 a month every clinic pays for the software.","keys":["earns its keep","99 a month","software"]},{"ai":"Ninety-nine euros is hardly going to move the needle.","aiTr":"Doksan dokuz euro pek bir fark yaratmaz.","hint":"It's a modest sum, admittedly, but at 1,000 clinics the subscriptions alone would come to roughly €1.2 million a year.","keys":["admittedly","1.2 million","subscriptions alone"]},{"ai":"And what's to stop clinics cancelling the moment budgets tighten?","aiTr":"Bütçeler daraldığı anda kliniklerin aboneliği iptal etmesini ne engelliyor?","hint":"Once a clinic has built its workflow around us, it has little reason to walk away.","keys":["workflow","walk away","little reason"]},{"ai":"Be honest with me — how confident are you in year-three profitability?","aiTr":"Bana dürüst olun — üçüncü yıl kârlılığından ne kadar eminsiniz?","hint":"Reasonably confident, though it's a projection, not a promise, and it holds barring regulatory surprises.","keys":["projection","barring","not a promise"]}]}},"ai-04":{"intro":"Yönetim kurulunda sertifikasyon sürecini, ölçülü ama güven veren, mevzuata hâkim bir dille savunuyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Regulators, understandably, take a dim view of uncertified medical devices, so the CE mark is less a milestone than a precondition for everything else.","tr":"Düzenleyiciler anlaşılır biçimde sertifikasız tıbbi cihazlara pek sıcak bakmıyor; bu yüzden CE işareti bir kilometre taşından çok, diğer her şeyin ön koşulu."},{"en":"As a Class IIa device under the MDR, our audiometer can't simply self-certify; a notified body has to sign off on both the product and the processes behind it.","tr":"MDR kapsamında Sınıf IIa bir cihaz olarak odyometremiz kendi kendini sertifikalandıramaz; hem ürünü hem de arkasındaki süreçleri onaylanmış bir kuruluşun onaylaması gerekir."},{"en":"That puts our clinical evidence squarely under the microscope.","tr":"Bu da klinik kanıtlarımızı doğrudan mercek altına koyuyor."},{"en":"Here, I'd venture to say, we're on reasonably firm ground: a blind comparison across two university hospitals, 200 participants aged 18 to 75, and 94% agreement with a trained audiologist.","tr":"Bu konuda, söylemeye cüret edersem, oldukça sağlam bir zemindeyiz: iki üniversite hastanesinde kör karşılaştırma, 18-75 yaş arası 200 katılımcı ve eğitimli bir odyologla %94 uyum."},{"en":"Admittedly, the remaining 6% diverged, but only marginally, and not once did the discrepancy alter a diagnosis.","tr":"Kabul etmek gerekir ki kalan %6'da sonuçlar ayrıştı, ama yalnızca çok az; ve bu farklar bir kez bile teşhisi değiştirmedi."},{"en":"Nor does it hurt that the findings were published in a medical journal last spring, since assessors tend to be wary of data that has never faced outside scrutiny.","tr":"Bulguların geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlanmış olmasının da zararı yok, çünkü değerlendiriciler dışarıdan hiç incelenmemiş verilere temkinli yaklaşır."},{"en":"The less glamorous part is the quality management system and the technical file, which, for all their tedium, are where certifications are quietly won or lost.","tr":"İşin daha az göz alıcı kısmı kalite yönetim sistemi ve teknik dosya; ne kadar sıkıcı olsalar da sertifikasyonlar sessiz sedasız orada kazanılır ya da kaybedilir."},{"en":"Our monthly software updates complicate matters further, because each release has to be validated, documented and traceable: agile development, but with a paper trail.","tr":"Aylık yazılım güncellemelerimiz işleri daha da karmaşıklaştırıyor, çünkü her sürümün doğrulanmış, belgelenmiş ve izlenebilir olması gerekiyor: çevik geliştirme, ama arkasında bir belge iziyle."},{"en":"We've retained a regulatory consultant who has steered several devices through this process, which, while no guarantee, does take some of the guesswork out of it.","tr":"Birkaç cihazı bu süreçten başarıyla geçirmiş bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışıyoruz; bu bir garanti olmasa da işin tahmine dayalı kısmını epey azaltıyor."},{"en":"The one variable we genuinely can't control is notified body capacity, and it would be naive to assume our timeline is immune to it.","tr":"Gerçekten kontrol edemediğimiz tek değişken onaylanmış kuruluşların kapasitesi ve takvimimizin bundan etkilenmeyeceğini varsaymak saflık olur."},{"en":"So while we're aiming for certification by the end of next year, I'd be loath to promise it to the month.","tr":"Yani sertifikasyonu gelecek yılın sonuna kadar almayı hedeflesek de bunu ayı ayına söz vermekten kaçınırım."},{"en":"That said, the very difficulty of the process cuts both ways: it slows us down, but by the same token, it keeps less rigorous competitors out.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, sürecin zorluğu iki tarafı keskin bir bıçak: Bizi yavaşlatıyor ama aynı şekilde daha az titiz rakipleri de dışarıda tutuyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"take a dim view of","tr":"hoş karşılamamak, olumsuz bakmak","ex":"Regulators take a dim view of uncertified devices.","def":"to disapprove of something"},{"en":"sign off on","tr":"resmî onay vermek","ex":"A notified body has to sign off on the device.","def":"to give official approval to something"},{"en":"under the microscope","tr":"mercek altında","ex":"Our clinical evidence is now under the microscope.","def":"being examined very closely"},{"en":"on firm ground","tr":"sağlam bir zeminde","ex":"With 94% agreement, we're on firm ground.","def":"in a position supported by strong facts"},{"en":"diverge","tr":"ayrışmak, farklılaşmak","ex":"The results diverged only marginally.","def":"to differ or go in different directions"},{"en":"paper trail","tr":"belge izi, kayıt zinciri","ex":"Every release leaves a clear paper trail.","def":"a series of documents that shows what was done and when"},{"en":"steer something through","tr":"bir şeyi bir süreçten başarıyla geçirmek","ex":"Our consultant has steered several devices through certification.","def":"to guide something successfully through a difficult process"},{"en":"take the guesswork out of","tr":"tahmine dayalı kısmı ortadan kaldırmak","ex":"Experience takes some of the guesswork out of the process.","def":"to make something more predictable"},{"en":"be loath to","tr":"...mekte isteksiz olmak","ex":"I'd be loath to promise an exact month.","def":"to be unwilling to do something"},{"en":"cut both ways","tr":"iki tarafı keskin bıçak olmak","ex":"Strict regulation cuts both ways.","def":"to have both good and bad effects"}],"grammar":{"title":"Nuanced hedging: confident but honest","tr":"'I'd venture to say', 'I'd be loath to', 'while no guarantee', 'it would be naive to assume' gibi ifadeler iddianı yumuşatır ama zayıflatmaz. Yatırımcı karşısında hem dürüst hem güvenilir görünmeni sağlar.","examples":["Here, I'd venture to say, we're on reasonably firm ground.","I'd be loath to promise it to the month.","It would be naive to assume our timeline is immune to it."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why can't the audiometer self-certify?","options":["Because it was developed in Turkey","Because it is a Class IIa device under the MDR","Because it uses AI","Because the study was too small"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest about the quality management system and the technical file?","options":["They are dull but often decisive","They are a formality that rarely matters","They have already been approved","They are the consultant's responsibility"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the tone of 'agile development, but with a paper trail'?","options":["Openly hostile","Deeply anxious","Wryly ironic","Purely technical"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by being 'loath to promise it to the month'?","options":["The target is unrealistic and will be dropped","The overall target stands, but the exact timing may shift","Certification is already complete","The consultant disagrees with the plan"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker say the difficulty of the process 'cuts both ways'?","options":["It costs money but attracts grants","It helps patients but frustrates doctors","It speeds up sales but raises prices","It delays the company but also keeps weaker competitors out"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Regulators take a ___ view of uncertified medical devices.","a":"dim","hint":"olumsuz (… view of)"},{"s":"A notified body has to sign ___ on both the product and the processes.","a":"off","hint":"onay vermek (sign … on)"},{"s":"Not once did the discrepancy ___ a diagnosis.","a":"alter","hint":"değiştirmek"},{"s":"I'd be ___ to promise it to the month.","a":"loath","hint":"isteksiz"}],"order":[{"a":"That puts our clinical evidence squarely under the microscope."},{"a":"Not once did the discrepancy alter a diagnosis."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu bir garanti olmasa da işin tahmine dayalı kısmını azaltıyor.","en":"While no guarantee, it takes some of the guesswork out of it.","keys":["no guarantee","guesswork"]},{"tr":"Takvimimizin bundan etkilenmeyeceğini varsaymak saflık olur.","en":"It would be naive to assume our timeline is immune to it.","keys":["naive to assume","immune"]},{"tr":"Sürecin zorluğu iki tarafı keskin bir bıçak.","en":"The difficulty of the process cuts both ways.","keys":["cuts both ways"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Lead investor","personaTr":"Lider yatırımcı (yönetim kurulu üyesi)","scene":"Yönetim kurulu toplantısında lider yatırımcı sertifikasyon takvimini sorguluyor ve seni zorluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Let's not sugar-coat it: how exposed are we if the notified body drags its feet?","aiTr":"Lafı dolandırmayalım: Onaylanmış kuruluş işi ağırdan alırsa ne kadar risk altındayız?","hint":"Fairly exposed, I'd venture to say. Notified body capacity is the one variable we can't control, so I'd be loath to promise the date to the month.","keys":["can't control","loath","capacity"]},{"ai":"Is the clinical evidence strong enough, or are we going to be sent back for more data?","aiTr":"Klinik kanıt yeterince güçlü mü, yoksa daha fazla veri için geri mi gönderileceğiz?","hint":"I think we're on reasonably firm ground: a blind comparison across two university hospitals, 94% agreement, and not once did a discrepancy alter a diagnosis.","keys":["firm ground","94","blind","diagnosis"]},{"ai":"The monthly updates worry me. Aren't we creating a compliance nightmare for ourselves?","aiTr":"Aylık güncellemeler beni endişelendiriyor. Kendimize bir uyum kabusu yaratmıyor muyuz?","hint":"It's more work, admittedly, but every release is validated, documented and traceable, so there's a clear paper trail.","keys":["paper trail","traceable","validated"]},{"ai":"Give me one good reason this whole ordeal is worth it.","aiTr":"Bütün bu çilenin neden buna değdiğine dair bana tek bir iyi sebep söyle.","hint":"The difficulty cuts both ways: it slows us down, but by the same token, it keeps less rigorous competitors out.","keys":["cuts both ways","competitors","by the same token"]}]}},"fu-01":{"intro":"Bir sağlık teknolojisi konferansındaki panelde, şüpheci bir doktorla yapay zekânın tıptaki yerini deneyimli bir panelistin incelikli ve dengeli diliyle tartışıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Dr. Weber","en":"I'll ask the question everyone in this room is too polite to ask: are we, the doctors, training our own replacements?","tr":"Bu salondaki herkesin sormaya çekindiği soruyu ben sorayım: biz doktorlar, kendi yerimize geçecek olanı mı yetiştiriyoruz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"It's a fair question, though I'd gently suggest it's the wrong one.","tr":"Haklı bir soru, ama nazikçe belirtmek isterim ki yanlış soru."},{"who":"Me","en":"The more useful question isn't whether AI replaces clinicians but how it can make them better at the parts of the job only they can do.","tr":"Daha faydalı soru, yapay zekânın klinisyenlerin yerini alıp almayacağı değil; onları işin yalnızca kendilerinin yapabildiği kısımlarında nasıl daha iyi kılabileceği."},{"who":"Me","en":"To be fair to the machines, they have undeniable strengths: they're fast, they're tirelessly consistent, and they don't lose concentration at the end of a twelve-hour shift.","tr":"Makinelere hakkını vermek gerekirse, inkâr edilemez güçlü yanları var: hızlılar, yorulmadan tutarlılar ve on iki saatlik bir vardiyanın sonunda dikkatleri dağılmıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"By the same token, they make mistakes, sometimes confidently, and they are only ever as good as the data they've been fed.","tr":"Aynı şekilde hata da yapıyorlar, bazen kendinden emin bir şekilde, ve her zaman ancak kendilerine verilen veri kadar iyiler."},{"who":"Me","en":"Train a model on a skewed dataset and it won't merely inherit those blind spots; it will scale them up, quietly and with impeccable confidence.","tr":"Bir modeli çarpık bir veri setiyle eğitirseniz, o kör noktaları devralmakla kalmaz; onları sessizce ve kusursuz bir özgüvenle büyütür."},{"who":"Me","en":"Which is precisely why responsibility can't be outsourced to an algorithm: someone has to own the decision, and that someone should have a name and a licence.","tr":"İşte tam da bu yüzden sorumluluk bir algoritmaya devredilemez: birinin kararın sahibi olması gerekir ve o kişinin bir adı ve bir lisansı olmalı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Trust, moreover, isn't something a patient extends to a probability score; it's something they extend to a person who can look them in the eye and explain.","tr":"Üstelik güven, bir hastanın bir olasılık skoruna duyduğu bir şey değildir; gözünün içine bakıp açıklama yapabilen bir insana duyduğu bir şeydir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our own audiometer is, I hope, a modest illustration: it runs a complete hearing test in under ten minutes, with no expert in the room.","tr":"Kendi odyometremiz, umarım, mütevazı bir örnek: odada uzman olmadan, eksiksiz bir işitme testini on dakikadan kısa sürede yapıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Far from making audiologists obsolete, it hands them back the hours they'd otherwise spend on routine tests, so they can devote themselves to the genuinely complex cases.","tr":"Odyologları gereksiz kılmak bir yana, rutin testlere harcayacakları saatleri onlara geri veriyor; böylece kendilerini gerçekten karmaşık vakalara adayabiliyorlar."},{"who":"Me","en":"So, if I may hedge my bets, AI is unlikely to replace doctors, although doctors who learn to work with it may well outpace those who don't.","tr":"Yani temkinli konuşmama izin verirseniz, yapay zekânın doktorların yerini alması pek olası değil; ama onunla çalışmayı öğrenen doktorlar, öğrenmeyenleri pekâlâ geride bırakabilir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"train one's replacement","tr":"kendi yerine geçecek olanı yetiştirmek","ex":"Are doctors training their own replacements?","def":"to teach the person or thing that will take your job"},{"en":"by the same token","tr":"aynı şekilde, aynı mantıkla","ex":"By the same token, AI can make confident mistakes.","def":"for the same reason; in a similar way"},{"en":"inherit","tr":"devralmak","ex":"A model inherits the blind spots in its data.","def":"to receive qualities or problems from something that came before"},{"en":"impeccable","tr":"kusursuz","ex":"It can be wrong with impeccable confidence.","def":"perfect, without any faults"},{"en":"outsource","tr":"dışarıya devretmek","ex":"Responsibility can't be outsourced to an algorithm.","def":"to give a task to an outside company or system"},{"en":"own the decision","tr":"kararın sahibi olmak","ex":"A clinician has to own the decision.","def":"to accept full personal responsibility for a choice"},{"en":"obsolete","tr":"işlevsiz, modası geçmiş","ex":"AI won't make audiologists obsolete.","def":"no longer needed or used"},{"en":"devote oneself to","tr":"kendini ...e adamak","ex":"Audiologists can devote themselves to complex cases.","def":"to give all your time and energy to something"},{"en":"hedge one's bets","tr":"temkinli davranmak, riski bölmek","ex":"If I may hedge my bets, the answer is probably no.","def":"to avoid committing fully to one position"},{"en":"outpace","tr":"geride bırakmak","ex":"Doctors who use AI may outpace those who don't.","def":"to go faster or do better than someone else"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging and concession in debate","tr":"Usta konuşmacılar görüşlerini yumuşatarak daha ikna edici olur: 'I'd gently suggest', 'is unlikely to', 'may well', 'if I may hedge my bets'. 'To be fair to…' ve 'By the same token' ise karşı tarafın haklı olduğu noktayı kabul edip dengeli bir argüman kurar.","examples":["I'd gently suggest it's the wrong question.","AI is unlikely to replace doctors, although doctors who work with it may well outpace those who don't.","By the same token, they make mistakes, sometimes confidently."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the speaker first respond to Dr. Weber's question?","options":["By rejecting it angrily","By accepting it as fair but reframing it","By avoiding it completely","By agreeing that doctors will be replaced"],"a":1},{"q":"What danger of skewed data does the speaker highlight?","options":["The model scales up its blind spots, confidently and quietly","The model refuses to work","The test takes more than ten minutes"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker say the responsible person 'should have a name and a licence'?","options":["Because software companies need licences","Because patients like to know names","Because a specific, qualified person must be accountable"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of 'with impeccable confidence'?","options":["Admiring","Neutral","Fearful","Ironic"],"a":3},{"q":"What does 'if I may hedge my bets' suggest about the speaker?","options":["They are avoiding an overconfident prediction","They are about to place a bet","They doubt their own device"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Are we, the doctors, training our own ___?","a":"replacements","hint":"yerimize geçecek olanlar"},{"s":"By the same ___, they make mistakes.","a":"token","hint":"aynı şekilde (deyim)"},{"s":"Responsibility can't be ___ to an algorithm.","a":"outsourced","hint":"dışarıya devredilmek"},{"s":"Far from making audiologists ___, it hands them back their hours.","a":"obsolete","hint":"gereksiz, işlevsiz"}],"order":[{"a":"Someone has to own the decision."},{"a":"Trust is something patients extend to a person."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Nazikçe belirtmek isterim ki bu yanlış soru.","en":"I'd gently suggest it's the wrong question.","keys":["gently suggest","wrong question"]},{"tr":"Sorumluluk bir algoritmaya devredilemez.","en":"Responsibility can't be outsourced to an algorithm.","keys":["responsibility","outsourced","algorithm"]},{"tr":"Yapay zekânın doktorların yerini alması pek olası değil.","en":"AI is unlikely to replace doctors.","keys":["unlikely to replace"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Skeptical doctor on the panel","personaTr":"Paneldeki şüpheci doktor","scene":"Panelde keskin zekâlı ve şüpheci bir doktor seni köşeye sıkıştırmaya çalışıyor. Esprili ama ölçülü, ikna edici yanıtlar veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Forgive the bluntness, but isn't 'augmenting clinicians' just a euphemism investors find easier to swallow?","aiTr":"Açık sözlülüğümü bağışlayın ama 'klinisyenleri güçlendirmek', yatırımcıların daha kolay yuttuğu bir örtmece değil mi?","hint":"I'd gently push back: the real question isn't whether AI replaces clinicians, but how it makes them better at what only they can do.","keys":["push back","replaces clinicians","only they can do"]},{"ai":"And yet the algorithm never tires, never has an off day, and doesn't ask for a pay rise.","aiTr":"Yine de algoritma hiç yorulmuyor, kötü günü olmuyor ve zam istemiyor.","hint":"True, but by the same token it makes mistakes, sometimes confidently, and it's only ever as good as the data it's been fed.","keys":["by the same token","makes mistakes","data"]},{"ai":"Then who carries the can when it gets a diagnosis wrong?","aiTr":"Peki bir teşhisi yanlış koyduğunda faturayı kim ödeyecek?","hint":"A clinician, always; responsibility can't be outsourced to an algorithm, and someone with a name and a licence has to own the decision.","keys":["outsourced","own the decision","responsibility"]},{"ai":"Convince me your device isn't simply the thin end of the wedge.","aiTr":"Cihazınızın daha büyük bir değişimin ilk adımı olmadığına beni ikna edin.","hint":"Far from making audiologists obsolete, it takes over the routine tests so they can devote themselves to the genuinely complex cases.","keys":["obsolete","routine tests","complex cases"]}]}},"st-04":{"intro":"Sert bir açılış yapan deneyimli bir distribütörle, ince ironi ve kendinden emin bir dille anlaşmayı şekillendiriyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"I'll cut to the chase: we work on 25%, and frankly, that's already generous for a product nobody in Germany has heard of yet.","tr":"Sadede geleyim: yüzde 25 ile çalışıyoruz ve açıkçası, Almanya'da henüz kimsenin duymadığı bir ürün için bu zaten cömert bir oran."},{"who":"Me","en":"I appreciate the candour, and I'll return the favour: at 25%, the unit economics simply don't stack up for us.","tr":"Açık sözlülüğünüz için teşekkürler, ben de aynısını yapayım: yüzde 25'te birim ekonomisi bizim için kesinlikle tutmuyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Each unit carries real hardware costs, and beyond 15% we'd be buying growth at the expense of the R&D that keeps us ahead.","tr":"Her cihazın ciddi bir donanım maliyeti var ve yüzde 15'in ötesinde, bizi önde tutan Ar-Ge'den feragat ederek büyüme satın almış oluruz."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Fifteen wouldn't even cover our launch marketing, never mind building a sales channel from the ground up.","tr":"On beş, sıfırdan bir satış kanalı kurmak şöyle dursun, lansman pazarlamamızı bile karşılamaz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Then perhaps the answer is to split the difference: 20% for year one, with a proper review at the twelve-month mark.","tr":"O zaman belki de çözüm farkı paylaşmak: ilk yıl yüzde 20, on ikinci ayda da esaslı bir değerlendirme."},{"who":"Me","en":"If the volumes are there, you'll find us more than reasonable when we revisit the terms.","tr":"Satış hacmi gelirse, şartları yeniden ele aldığımızda bizi fazlasıyla makul bulacaksınız."},{"who":"Partner","en":"I could work with that, on the understanding that Germany is ours exclusively.","tr":"Almanya'nın yalnızca bize ait olması şartıyla bununla çalışabilirim."},{"who":"Me","en":"In principle, yes, though I'd want exclusivity to be earned rather than simply granted, so it would hinge on a minimum sales target.","tr":"Prensipte evet, ama münhasırlığın öylece verilmesini değil hak edilmesini isterim; yani bu bir minimum satış hedefine bağlı olur."},{"who":"Me","en":"Handing over a market like Germany on the strength of a handshake would be, shall we say, a bold move for a company our size.","tr":"Almanya gibi bir pazarı sadece bir el sıkışmaya dayanarak devretmek, bizim büyüklüğümüzde bir şirket için, nasıl desem, cesur bir hamle olurdu."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Point taken; let's get the lawyers to paper it and aim to sign next week.","tr":"Anlaşıldı; avukatlara yazıya döktürelim ve gelecek hafta imzalamayı hedefleyelim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Sounds good, and for what it's worth, I think this is a deal both sides can genuinely live with.","tr":"Kulağa iyi geliyor ve bence, ne kadar önemi varsa, bu iki tarafın da gönül rahatlığıyla kabul edebileceği bir anlaşma."}],"vocab":[{"en":"cut to the chase","tr":"sadede gelmek","ex":"I'll cut to the chase.","def":"to get to the point immediately"},{"en":"return the favour","tr":"aynı şekilde karşılık vermek","ex":"I appreciate the candour, and I'll return the favour.","def":"to do the same kind thing for someone that they did for you"},{"en":"unit economics","tr":"birim ekonomisi","ex":"At 25%, the unit economics don't work.","def":"the revenue and cost of selling one single unit"},{"en":"stack up","tr":"mantıklı olmak, tutmak","ex":"The numbers simply don't stack up.","def":"(of numbers or arguments) to make sense"},{"en":"never mind","tr":"...şöyle dursun","ex":"It wouldn't cover marketing, never mind a sales channel.","def":"used to say the second thing is even less possible"},{"en":"split the difference","tr":"farkı paylaşmak, ortada buluşmak","ex":"Perhaps we should split the difference at 20%.","def":"to agree on an amount halfway between two offers"},{"en":"on the understanding that","tr":"...şartıyla","ex":"I could work with that, on the understanding that Germany is ours.","def":"on the condition that"},{"en":"hinge on","tr":"tamamen ...e bağlı olmak","ex":"Exclusivity would hinge on a minimum sales target.","def":"to depend completely on something"},{"en":"on the strength of","tr":"...e dayanarak","ex":"We can't hand over Germany on the strength of a handshake.","def":"because of or based on something"},{"en":"paper a deal","tr":"anlaşmayı yazıya dökmek","ex":"Let's get the lawyers to paper it.","def":"(informal) to turn an agreement into formal documents"}],"grammar":{"title":"Softening and understatement","tr":"Sert bir 'hayır' demek yerine ince ifadelerle sınır çizilir: 'shall we say' ironik bir yumuşatma katar, 'perhaps' öneriyi dayatmadan sunar, 'for what it's worth' kendi görüşünü alçakgönüllüce ekler.","examples":["It would be, shall we say, a bold move for a company our size.","Then perhaps the answer is to split the difference.","For what it's worth, I think this is a deal both sides can live with."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the distributor justify asking for 25%?","options":["The product is still unknown in Germany","Their lawyers are expensive","The device is too heavy to ship"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'the unit economics don't stack up'?","options":["The device is too cheap to make","At that commission, each sale wouldn't make enough financial sense","The distributor's maths is wrong"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of 'a bold move for a company our size'?","options":["Openly aggressive","Enthusiastic","Ironic understatement meaning it would be unwise"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by wanting exclusivity 'earned rather than simply granted'?","options":["Exclusivity is out of the question","The distributor must prove itself through sales first","The distributor should pay an upfront fee"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the overall tone of the negotiation?","options":["Tense, with both sides close to walking away","Polite but distant","Frank and firm, but constructive on both sides"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"I'll cut to the ___.","a":"chase","hint":"sadede gelmek"},{"s":"At 25%, the unit economics don't ___ up.","a":"stack","hint":"tutmak, mantıklı olmak"},{"s":"Perhaps the answer is to split the ___.","a":"difference","hint":"fark"},{"s":"Exclusivity would ___ on a minimum sales target.","a":"hinge","hint":"bağlı olmak"}],"order":[{"a":"Let's get the lawyers to paper it."},{"a":"Perhaps the answer is to split the difference."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sadede geleyim: yüzde 25 ile çalışıyoruz.","en":"I'll cut to the chase: we work on 25%.","keys":["cut to the chase","we work on"]},{"tr":"Münhasırlık bir minimum satış hedefine bağlı olur.","en":"Exclusivity would hinge on a minimum sales target.","keys":["hinge on","minimum sales target"]},{"tr":"Bu, iki tarafın da gerçekten kabul edebileceği bir anlaşma.","en":"This is a deal both sides can genuinely live with.","keys":["both sides","live with"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Distributor","personaTr":"Distribütör","scene":"Sert bir açılış yapmaktan çekinmeyen deneyimli bir Hollandalı distribütörle Almanya anlaşmasını pazarlık ediyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll cut to the chase: we work on 25%, and that's generous for a product nobody here has heard of.","aiTr":"Sadede geleyim: yüzde 25 ile çalışıyoruz ve burada kimsenin duymadığı bir ürün için bu cömert bile.","hint":"I appreciate the candour, and I'll return the favour: at 25%, the unit economics simply don't stack up for us.","keys":["return the favour","unit economics","stack up"]},{"ai":"Fifteen wouldn't even cover our launch marketing, never mind a sales channel.","aiTr":"On beş, satış kanalı şöyle dursun, lansman pazarlamamızı bile karşılamaz.","hint":"Then perhaps the answer is to split the difference: 20% for year one, with a proper review at the twelve-month mark.","keys":["split the difference","year one","review"]},{"ai":"I could work with that, on the understanding that Germany is ours exclusively.","aiTr":"Almanya'nın yalnızca bize ait olması şartıyla bununla çalışabilirim.","hint":"In principle, yes, though exclusivity would have to be earned, so it would hinge on a minimum sales target.","keys":["in principle","hinge on","earned"]},{"ai":"You don't think a handshake and a bit of trust would do?","aiTr":"Bir el sıkışma ve biraz güvenin yeteceğini düşünmüyor musunuz?","hint":"Handing over a market like Germany on the strength of a handshake would be, shall we say, a bold move for a company our size.","keys":["on the strength of","bold move","shall we say"]}]}},"te-03":{"intro":"Sahada ortaya çıkan zor bir hatayı ve çıkardığınız dersi ustaca, hafif bir ironiyle anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Last week we were confronted with the kind of bug every hardware team dreads: one that only shows up in the field.","tr":"Geçen hafta her donanım ekibinin korktuğu türden bir hatayla karşılaştık: yalnızca sahada ortaya çıkan bir hata."},{"who":"Me","en":"A handful of clinics were seeing high-frequency hearing loss in patients who, by every other measure, had perfectly normal hearing.","tr":"Birkaç klinik, başka her açıdan işitmesi tamamen normal olan hastalarda yüksek frekanslarda işitme kaybı görüyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"Tellingly, the very same units were behaving impeccably everywhere else.","tr":"Dikkat çekici olan, aynı cihazların başka her yerde kusursuz çalışmasıydı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our knee-jerk reaction was to blame the headphones, yet swapping them out changed precisely nothing.","tr":"İlk refleksimiz suçu kulaklıklara atmak oldu, ama onları değiştirmek kesinlikle hiçbir şeyi değiştirmedi."},{"who":"Me","en":"So we did what, in hindsight, we ought to have done from the outset: we stopped theorising and pulled the logs from every device.","tr":"Böylece, geriye dönüp bakınca en başta yapmamız gereken şeyi yaptık: teori üretmeyi bıraktık ve her cihazın kayıtlarını çektik."},{"who":"Me","en":"Set side by side, the affected and unaffected clinics told a remarkably clear story.","tr":"Yan yana konduğunda, sorun yaşayan ve yaşamayan klinikler son derece net bir hikâye anlatıyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"Every anomalous result had come from a room cooled by an ageing air-conditioning unit.","tr":"Her anormal sonuç, eskimiş bir klimayla soğutulan bir odadan gelmişti."},{"who":"Me","en":"These units, it transpired, emit a faint high-pitched whine at precisely the frequencies we test, so the device was diligently recording a hearing loss that was, quite literally, the room's and not the patient's.","tr":"Meğer bu klimalar tam da test ettiğimiz frekanslarda hafif, tiz bir vızıltı çıkarıyormuş; yani cihaz, kelimenin tam anlamıyla hastaya değil odaya ait bir işitme kaybını özenle kaydediyormuş."},{"who":"Me","en":"The remedy was almost embarrassingly modest: a brief ambient-noise check before each test, which warns the user if the room is too loud to give a trustworthy result.","tr":"Çözüm neredeyse utandıracak kadar mütevazıydı: her testten önce yapılan ve oda güvenilir bir sonuç için fazla gürültülüyse kullanıcıyı uyaran kısa bir ortam gürültüsü kontrolü."},{"who":"Me","en":"It went out with the next monthly update, and results have been consistent across every site since.","tr":"Düzeltme bir sonraki aylık güncellemeyle gönderildi ve o günden beri sonuçlar tüm merkezlerde tutarlı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, the fix is not really the point.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, asıl mesele düzeltmenin kendisi değil."},{"who":"Me","en":"What lingers is a rather humbling lesson: a confident hunch, however seasoned the engineer, is no match for half an hour spent with the data.","tr":"Akılda kalan, insanı oldukça alçakgönüllü kılan bir ders: mühendis ne kadar deneyimli olursa olsun, kendinden emin bir önsezi verilerle geçirilen yarım saatin yerini tutmaz."}],"vocab":[{"en":"show up in the field","tr":"sahada (gerçek kullanımda) ortaya çıkmak","ex":"It was a bug that only showed up in the field.","def":"to appear only when a product is used by real customers"},{"en":"tellingly","tr":"dikkat çekici biçimde, manidar şekilde","ex":"Tellingly, the same units worked perfectly elsewhere.","def":"in a way that reveals something important"},{"en":"knee-jerk reaction","tr":"düşünmeden verilen ilk tepki","ex":"Our knee-jerk reaction was to blame the headphones.","def":"a quick reaction without careful thought"},{"en":"in hindsight","tr":"geriye dönüp bakınca","ex":"In hindsight, we should have checked the data first.","def":"when you look back at a past event with what you know now"},{"en":"from the outset","tr":"en başından","ex":"We ought to have pulled the logs from the outset.","def":"from the very beginning"},{"en":"anomalous","tr":"anormal, olağan dışı","ex":"Every anomalous result came from the same kind of room.","def":"different from what is normal or expected"},{"en":"it transpired that","tr":"meğer, ...olduğu ortaya çıktı","ex":"It transpired that the units emit a faint whine.","def":"it became known that (formal)"},{"en":"almost embarrassingly","tr":"neredeyse utandıracak kadar","ex":"The remedy was almost embarrassingly simple.","def":"so much that it feels slightly awkward to admit"},{"en":"that said","tr":"bununla birlikte","ex":"That said, the fix is not really the point.","def":"used to add a point that contrasts with what came before"},{"en":"be no match for","tr":"...ile boy ölçüşememek","ex":"A confident hunch is no match for the data.","def":"to be much weaker or less effective than something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Ought to have / should have + past participle","tr":"'ought to have / should have + V3' geçmişte yapılması gerekip yapılmayan şeyleri anlatır; özeleştiriyi ölçülü ve zarif bir dille ifade eder. 'Ought to' biraz daha resmîdir.","examples":["We did what we ought to have done from the outset.","In hindsight, we should have pulled the logs first.","We ought not to have blamed the headphones so quickly."]},"questions":[{"q":"What makes this kind of bug especially frustrating for a hardware team?","options":["It only appears in real-world use, not in the lab","It affects every device equally","It was reported by investors"],"a":0},{"q":"What is implied by 'we ought to have done from the outset'?","options":["The clinics delayed the investigation","The team had no access to the logs earlier","The team regrets not looking at the data sooner"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of 'a hearing loss that was, quite literally, the room's and not the patient's'?","options":["Angry and defensive","Wry and ironic","Anxious and apologetic"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker call the remedy 'almost embarrassingly modest'?","options":["Because it was expensive to build","Because customers complained about it","Because a very simple fix solved a problem that had baffled the team"],"a":2},{"q":"What does 'That said, the fix is not really the point' signal?","options":["The speaker is moving on to a broader lesson","The fix did not work","The speaker disagrees with the engineers"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Our ___ reaction was to blame the headphones.","a":"knee-jerk","hint":"düşünmeden verilen (tepki)"},{"s":"In ___, we ought to have pulled the logs from the outset.","a":"hindsight","hint":"geriye dönüp bakınca"},{"s":"These units, it ___, emit a faint high-pitched whine.","a":"transpired","hint":"ortaya çıktı (meğer)"},{"s":"A confident hunch is no ___ for half an hour with the data.","a":"match","hint":"denk, rakip"}],"order":[{"a":"Tellingly the same units behaved impeccably everywhere else."},{"a":"We stopped theorising and pulled the logs from every device."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Geriye dönüp bakınca, verilere en başından bakmalıydık.","en":"In hindsight, we ought to have looked at the data from the outset.","keys":["in hindsight","ought to have","from the outset"]},{"tr":"Bununla birlikte, asıl mesele düzeltme değil.","en":"That said, the fix is not really the point.","keys":["that said","not really the point"]},{"tr":"İlk refleksimiz suçu kulaklıklara atmak oldu.","en":"Our knee-jerk reaction was to blame the headphones.","keys":["knee-jerk reaction","blame the headphones"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Head of audiology at a hospital","personaTr":"Bir hastanenin odyoloji bölüm başkanı","scene":"Bir hastanenin odyoloji bölüm başkanı olayı sorguluyor; güven kaybını önlemek için açık ve ölçülü konuşmalısın.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll be candid — when a device starts diagnosing hearing loss in people with perfectly good hearing, my confidence takes a knock. What on earth happened?","aiTr":"Açık konuşacağım — bir cihaz işitmesi gayet iyi olan insanlarda işitme kaybı teşhis etmeye başlayınca güvenim sarsılıyor. Ne oldu böyle?","hint":"That's entirely fair. It transpired that ageing air conditioners emit a faint whine at precisely the frequencies we test, so the device was recording the room rather than the patient.","keys":["it transpired","air conditioners","whine","the room"]},{"ai":"Surely that should have been caught during validation?","aiTr":"Bunun doğrulama aşamasında yakalanması gerekmez miydi?","hint":"In hindsight, yes, it ought to have been; our validation rooms were simply too quiet to reveal it.","keys":["in hindsight","ought to have","too quiet"]},{"ai":"So what's stopping it from happening again?","aiTr":"Peki bunun tekrar olmasını ne engelliyor?","hint":"Every test now begins with a brief ambient-noise check, and if the room is too loud to give a trustworthy result, the user is warned before anything is recorded.","keys":["ambient-noise check","warned","too loud"]},{"ai":"And beyond the fix itself, has this changed how your team works?","aiTr":"Düzeltmenin ötesinde, bu olay ekibinizin çalışma şeklini değiştirdi mi?","hint":"It has; we now treat every confident hunch with suspicion until the data backs it up.","keys":["hunch","data backs it up","suspicion"]}]}},"sc-01":{"intro":"Çalışmanı deneyimli bir araştırmacı gibi anlatıyorsun: ölçülü iddialar, ince ironi ve dikkatli yumuşatmalar.","text":[{"en":"Everything rested on one deceptively simple question: does our device reach the same conclusions as a trained audiologist?","tr":"Her şey göründüğünden çok daha zor tek bir soruya dayanıyordu: cihazımız eğitimli bir odyologla aynı sonuçlara ulaşıyor mu?"},{"en":"To answer it in a way regulators would accept, we designed a clinical study in partnership with two university hospitals.","tr":"Bu soruyu düzenleyici kurumların kabul edeceği şekilde yanıtlamak için iki üniversite hastanesiyle ortaklaşa bir klinik çalışma tasarladık."},{"en":"We set ourselves a fairly demanding bar, hypothesising that the two methods would agree in at least 90 percent of cases.","tr":"Kendimize oldukça yüksek bir çıta koyduk ve iki yöntemin vakaların en az yüzde 90'ında uyuşacağını varsaydık."},{"en":"Two hundred participants aged 18 to 75 were recruited, each of whom was tested twice on the same day, once by the device and once by an audiologist.","tr":"18-75 yaş arası iki yüz katılımcı alındı; her biri aynı gün iki kez, bir kez cihazla, bir kez de bir odyolog tarafından test edildi."},{"en":"The audiologists were kept blind to the device's output, so whatever bias they might have brought into the room could not have flattered our results.","tr":"Odyologlar cihazın çıktısından habersiz tutuldu; böylece odaya getirmiş olabilecekleri herhangi bir yanlılık sonuçlarımızı olduğundan iyi gösteremezdi."},{"en":"In the event, agreement reached 94 percent, a figure that left us rather more relieved than we cared to admit at the time.","tr":"Sonuçta uyum yüzde 94'e ulaştı; bu rakam bizi o zamanlar itiraf etmek istediğimizden çok daha fazla rahatlattı."},{"en":"The remaining 6 percent showed only marginal discrepancies, none of which would have altered the diagnosis.","tr":"Kalan yüzde 6'da yalnızca çok küçük farklar vardı ve hiçbiri teşhisi değiştirecek nitelikte değildi."},{"en":"That said, we have been careful not to overstate the case, since a sample of adults aged 18 to 75 says little about children or the very elderly.","tr":"Bununla birlikte durumu abartmamaya özen gösterdik, çünkü 18-75 yaş arası yetişkinlerden oluşan bir örneklem çocuklar ya da çok yaşlılar hakkında pek bir şey söylemez."},{"en":"Publication in a medical journal last spring lent the findings a credibility that no amount of marketing could have bought.","tr":"Geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlanması, bulgulara hiçbir pazarlama bütçesinin satın alamayacağı bir güvenilirlik kazandırdı."},{"en":"The study has since become the cornerstone of our certification file and, arguably, the most persuasive page in our pitch deck.","tr":"Çalışma o zamandan beri sertifikasyon dosyamızın temel taşı ve belki de sunum dosyamızın en ikna edici sayfası haline geldi."}],"vocab":[{"en":"deceptively simple","tr":"göründüğünden zor, aldatıcı derecede basit","ex":"It was a deceptively simple question.","def":"appearing easy but actually difficult"},{"en":"set a demanding bar","tr":"yüksek bir çıta koymak","ex":"We set ourselves a fairly demanding bar.","def":"to choose a high standard to reach"},{"en":"keep someone blind to","tr":"birini ...den habersiz tutmak","ex":"The audiologists were kept blind to the device's output.","def":"to deliberately not let someone know certain information"},{"en":"flatter the results","tr":"sonuçları olduğundan iyi göstermek","ex":"Bias could easily flatter the results.","def":"to make results look better than they really are"},{"en":"in the event","tr":"sonuçta, iş olduğunda","ex":"In the event, agreement reached 94 percent.","def":"as things actually happened"},{"en":"more than we cared to admit","tr":"itiraf etmek istediğimizden daha fazla","ex":"We were more nervous than we cared to admit.","def":"to a greater degree than we wanted others to know"},{"en":"overstate the case","tr":"durumu abartmak","ex":"We have been careful not to overstate the case.","def":"to claim more than the evidence really shows"},{"en":"lend credibility to","tr":"...e güvenilirlik kazandırmak","ex":"Publication lent the findings real credibility.","def":"to make something more believable"},{"en":"cornerstone","tr":"temel taşı","ex":"The study is the cornerstone of our certification file.","def":"the most important part on which everything else depends"},{"en":"arguably","tr":"tartışmaya açık olsa da, belki de","ex":"It is arguably the most persuasive page in our deck.","def":"used to say something can reasonably be claimed, though others may disagree"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging and understatement in scientific writing","tr":"İleri düzey bilimsel dilde iddialar ölçülü tutulur: 'fairly', 'rather', 'arguably', 'says little about' gibi ifadeler, abartmadan güven verir. Yumuşatma, zayıflık değil, dürüstlük işaretidir.","examples":["We set ourselves a fairly demanding bar.","It left us rather more relieved than we cared to admit.","It is, arguably, the most persuasive page in our deck."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the writer call the central question \"deceptively simple\"?","options":["It was easy to answer","It sounded simple but was hard to prove","Nobody understood it"],"a":1},{"q":"What was the purpose of keeping the audiologists blind?","options":["To stop bias from making the results look better","To reduce costs","To shorten the tests"],"a":0},{"q":"What does \"rather more relieved than we cared to admit\" reveal?","options":["The team was disappointed with 94 percent","The team had expected 100 percent","The team had privately worried about the outcome"],"a":2},{"q":"Why is the writer careful not to overstate the case?","options":["The journal asked them to","The results were below target","Investors were sceptical","The sample covered only adults aged 18 to 75"],"a":3},{"q":"What is the tone of the final sentence?","options":["Boastful and exaggerated","Confident but carefully hedged","Bitter and ironic"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Everything rested on one ___ simple question.","a":"deceptively","hint":"aldatıcı derecede"},{"s":"We have been careful not to ___ the case.","a":"overstate","hint":"abartmak"},{"s":"Publication ___ the findings a credibility that no marketing could have bought.","a":"lent","hint":"kazandırdı"},{"s":"The study has become the ___ of our certification file.","a":"cornerstone","hint":"temel taşı"}],"order":[{"a":"The study has become the cornerstone of our certification file."},{"a":"We set ourselves a fairly demanding bar."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Durumu abartmamaya özen gösterdik.","en":"We have been careful not to overstate the case.","keys":["careful","overstate the case"]},{"tr":"Odyologlar cihazın çıktısından habersiz tutuldu.","en":"The audiologists were kept blind to the device's output.","keys":["kept blind","output"]},{"tr":"Belki de sunum dosyamızın en ikna edici sayfası bu.","en":"It is arguably the most persuasive page in our pitch deck.","keys":["arguably","most persuasive"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Senior clinical researcher","personaTr":"Kıdemli klinik araştırmacı","scene":"Bir panelde deneyimli bir araştırmacı çalışmanızı sert ama nazik sorularla sınıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Agreement studies are often accused of flattering the device under test. Why should I trust yours?","aiTr":"Uyum çalışmaları sık sık test edilen cihazı olduğundan iyi göstermekle suçlanır. Sizinkine neden güveneyim?","hint":"That's a fair challenge; the audiologists were kept blind to the device's output, so their judgement couldn't have been nudged in our favour.","keys":["kept blind","in our favour","fair challenge"]},{"ai":"Ninety-four percent sounds almost too good. Was the threshold set after the fact?","aiTr":"Yüzde doksan dört neredeyse fazla iyi görünüyor. Eşik sonradan mı belirlendi?","hint":"Not at all; we set the 90 percent bar before recruiting a single participant, and the result cleared it with room to spare.","keys":["before recruiting","90 percent","room to spare"]},{"ai":"And the discordant six percent: anything clinically worrying there?","aiTr":"Peki uyuşmayan yüzde altı: klinik açıdan endişe verici bir şey var mı?","hint":"Reassuringly little; the discrepancies were marginal, and none of them would have altered the diagnosis.","keys":["marginal","altered the diagnosis","reassuringly"]},{"ai":"Where would you be the first to admit the evidence is thin?","aiTr":"Kanıtların zayıf olduğunu ilk kabul edeceğiniz nokta neresi?","hint":"I'd readily concede that a sample of adults aged 18 to 75 tells us little about children or the very elderly.","keys":["concede","18 to 75","children"]}]}},"ab-04":{"intro":"Komşun Lena ve iş arkadaşın Tom'la ince espriler, ironi ve zarif ifadelerle dolu, tamamen doğal bir sohbet ediyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Lena","en":"You must be the new arrival on the third floor—I'm Lena, the one whose footsteps you've no doubt been cursing.","tr":"Üçüncü kata yeni gelen sen olmalısın; ben Lena, ayak seslerine şüphesiz söylenip durduğun kişi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Not at all, though I'm relieved to put a face to them—I'm {name}, and I suspect my moving boxes did rather more damage to your sleep.","tr":"Hiç de değil, ama sahibini görmek içimi rahatlattı; ben {name}, ve sanırım asıl benim taşınma kutularım senin uykuna çok daha fazla zarar verdi."},{"who":"Lena","en":"Water under the bridge—besides, after the week we've had, a bit of sunshine makes up for almost anything, even this biting cold.","tr":"Geçmiş geçmişte kaldı; hem geçirdiğimiz haftadan sonra biraz güneş neredeyse her şeyi telafi ediyor, bu iliklere işleyen soğuğu bile."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd begun to suspect the sun was a rumour put about by the tourist board.","tr":"Güneşin turizm bürosunun yaydığı bir söylenti olduğundan şüphelenmeye başlamıştım."},{"who":"Lena","en":"So what possessed you to swap the Bosphorus for the Spree?","tr":"Peki hangi akla hizmet Boğaz'ı Spree'ye değiştirdin?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm opening the European office of my health-tech startup, a prospect I find exhilarating and terrifying in roughly equal measure.","tr":"Sağlık teknolojisi girişimimin Avrupa ofisini açıyorum; bu, aşağı yukarı eşit ölçüde heyecan verici ve korkutucu bulduğum bir şey."},{"who":"Me","en":"The city's greenery has won me over completely, though I learned the hard way, staring into an empty fridge, that Sunday is sacred here.","tr":"Şehrin yeşilliği gönlümü tamamen kazandı, ama boş bir buzdolabına bakarken burada pazarın kutsal olduğunu acı tecrübeyle öğrendim."},{"who":"Lena","en":"Then let me make amends on Berlin's behalf: we're having a barbecue in the courtyard on Sunday, quite possibly the last before winter closes in.","tr":"O zaman Berlin adına gönlünü almama izin ver: pazar günü avluda mangal yapıyoruz, büyük ihtimalle kış bastırmadan önceki sonuncusu."},{"who":"Tom","en":"So, did Berlin live up to its fearsome reputation at the weekend?","tr":"Eee, Berlin hafta sonu o korkutucu şöhretini hak etti mi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"On the contrary—my neighbours dragged me to a barbecue and were so welcoming that the famous Berlin frostiness has yet to make an appearance.","tr":"Tam tersine; komşularım beni bir mangala sürükledi ve o kadar sıcak karşıladılar ki meşhur Berlin soğukluğu henüz ortaya çıkmadı."},{"who":"Tom","en":"Give it time, but the trick is that once they let you in, you're in for life—and on that note, drinks on Friday after work?","tr":"Zamanla görürsün, ama işin sırrı şu: seni bir kez içeri aldılar mı, ömür boyu içeridesin; hazır lafı gelmişken, cuma iş çıkışı içkiye ne dersin?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I wouldn't miss it, provided the first round is on me.","tr":"Kaçırmam, yeter ki ilk içkiler benden olsun."}],"vocab":[{"en":"no doubt","tr":"şüphesiz, muhtemelen","ex":"You've no doubt heard my footsteps.","def":"certainly; very probably"},{"en":"water under the bridge","tr":"geçmiş geçmişte kaldı","ex":"The noise last week? That's water under the bridge.","def":"something in the past that no longer matters"},{"en":"make up for","tr":"telafi etmek","ex":"A bit of sunshine makes up for almost anything.","def":"to compensate for something bad"},{"en":"biting cold","tr":"iliklere işleyen soğuk","ex":"Even the biting cold couldn't spoil the day.","def":"very sharp, unpleasant cold"},{"en":"what possessed you","tr":"hangi akla hizmet, ne diye","ex":"What possessed you to move to Berlin in winter?","def":"used to ask why someone did something surprising"},{"en":"in equal measure","tr":"eşit ölçüde","ex":"It's exhilarating and terrifying in equal measure.","def":"to the same degree"},{"en":"make amends","tr":"gönül almak, telafi etmek","ex":"Let me make amends on Berlin's behalf.","def":"to do something good to show you are sorry"},{"en":"live up to","tr":"(beklentiyi) karşılamak, hak etmek","ex":"Did Berlin live up to its reputation?","def":"to be as good or bad as people expected"},{"en":"has yet to","tr":"henüz ...-medi","ex":"The famous frostiness has yet to appear.","def":"has not happened so far"},{"en":"be on me","tr":"benden olsun (hesap)","ex":"The first round is on me.","def":"I will pay for it"}],"grammar":{"title":"Softening and hedging: rather, roughly, quite possibly, has yet to","tr":"C2 düzeyinde konuşmacılar iddiaları yumuşatmak ya da ironi katmak için 'rather', 'roughly', 'quite possibly', 'has yet to' gibi ifadeler kullanır. Bu, cümleye kibar ve esprili bir ton verir.","examples":["My moving boxes did rather more damage to your sleep.","I find it exhilarating and terrifying in roughly equal measure.","It's quite possibly the last barbecue before winter.","The famous Berlin frostiness has yet to make an appearance."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'swap the Bosphorus for the Spree' refer to?","options":["Moving from Istanbul to Berlin","Changing jobs","Taking a boat trip"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the tone of 'a rumour put about by the tourist board'?","options":["Bitter","Dry and humorous","Anxious","Formal"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'Sunday is sacred here' imply?","options":["Everyone goes to church","Sunday is only for tourists","Almost everything is closed on Sundays"],"a":2},{"q":"What does Tom imply with 'once they let you in, you're in for life'?","options":["Berliners are slow to open up but very loyal","Berliners always lock their doors","Tom wants to move in with the speaker"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker's last line convey?","options":["Reluctance","Eager acceptance with a generous gesture","A polite refusal"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Water under the ___.","a":"bridge","hint":"köprü (geçmiş geçmişte kaldı)"},{"s":"What ___ you to swap the Bosphorus for the Spree?","a":"possessed","hint":"hangi akla hizmet"},{"s":"Let me make ___ on Berlin's behalf.","a":"amends","hint":"gönül almak"},{"s":"The famous Berlin frostiness has ___ to make an appearance.","a":"yet","hint":"henüz"}],"order":[{"a":"A bit of sunshine makes up for almost anything."},{"a":"The first round is on me."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Biraz güneş neredeyse her şeyi telafi ediyor, bu iliklere işleyen soğuğu bile.","en":"A bit of sunshine makes up for almost anything, even this biting cold.","keys":["makes up for","biting cold"]},{"tr":"Bunu aşağı yukarı eşit ölçüde heyecan verici ve korkutucu buluyorum.","en":"I find it exhilarating and terrifying in roughly equal measure.","keys":["exhilarating","equal measure"]},{"tr":"Berlin adına gönlünü almama izin ver.","en":"Let me make amends on Berlin's behalf.","keys":["make amends","on Berlin's behalf"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Neighbour (Lena)","personaTr":"Komşu (Lena)","scene":"Cumartesi sabahı merdivende üst kattaki komşun Lena ile karşılaşıyorsun. Lena hazırcevap; sen de aynı incelikte karşılık veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"You must be the new arrival—I'm Lena, the owner of the footsteps you've no doubt been cursing.","aiTr":"Yeni gelen sen olmalısın; ben Lena, şüphesiz söylenip durduğun ayak seslerinin sahibi.","hint":"Not in the slightest—I'm {name}, and if anything, I owe you an apology for all my moving boxes.","keys":["owe you an apology","moving boxes","not in the slightest"]},{"ai":"Water under the bridge. So what possessed you to swap the Bosphorus for the Spree?","aiTr":"Geçmiş geçmişte kaldı. Peki hangi akla hizmet Boğaz'ı Spree'ye değiştirdin?","hint":"Ambition, mostly—I'm opening the European office of my health-tech startup, which I find thrilling and terrifying in equal measure.","keys":["European office","equal measure","startup"]},{"ai":"And how's Berlin treating you—any culture shocks yet?","aiTr":"Peki Berlin sana nasıl davranıyor; şimdiden bir kültür şoku yaşadın mı?","hint":"The greenery has won me over, but I learned the hard way that Sunday is sacred here and the shops stay firmly shut.","keys":["won me over","Sunday","learned the hard way"]},{"ai":"Then let me make amends: we're having a barbecue in the courtyard on Sunday, weather permitting. Will you join us?","aiTr":"O zaman gönlünü alayım: hava izin verirse pazar günü avluda mangal yapıyoruz. Bize katılır mısın?","hint":"I'd be delighted, and I'll bring some baklava, if only to prove that Istanbul does desserts rather well.","keys":["delighted","baklava","join"]}]}},"co-03":{"intro":"Ortağının fiyatı yarıya indirme fikrine ince bir diplomasiyle, yumuşatıcı ifadeler ve hafif ironiyle karşı çıkıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"Let me play devil's advocate for a moment: what if we simply halved the price to 2,000 euros and let volume do the rest?","tr":"Bir an şeytanın avukatlığını yapayım: fiyatı 2.000 euroya, yani yarıya indirsek ve gerisini satış hacmine bıraksak?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I can see the appeal, and I'd be the last person to argue that our sales cycle is short enough.","tr":"Cazip yanını görüyorum; satış döngümüzün yeterince kısa olduğunu savunacak son kişi de benim."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, at 1,500 euros a unit, we'd be trading a healthy 60 percent margin for a rather precarious 25, which feels like a steep price to pay for speed.","tr":"Yine de cihaz başına 1.500 euroluk maliyetle, sağlıklı bir yüzde 60 marjı oldukça kırılgan bir yüzde 25'e değişmiş oluruz; hız için ödenecek ağır bir bedel gibi geliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"And once you've taught the market that the device is worth 2,000 euros, it's notoriously hard to persuade anyone it's worth twice that.","tr":"Üstelik piyasaya cihazın 2.000 euro ettiğini bir kez öğrettin mi, kimseyi bunun iki katı ettiğine ikna edememek bilinen bir gerçektir."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Granted, but I keep hearing the same thing from clinics, namely that it's simply too expensive.","tr":"Kabul, ama kliniklerden sürekli aynı şeyi duyuyorum: cihaz düpedüz çok pahalı."},{"who":"Me","en":"I don't doubt that's what they say, though I'd gently suggest it isn't quite what they mean.","tr":"Bunu söylediklerinden şüphem yok, ama kastettikleri şeyin tam olarak bu olmadığını nazikçe belirtmek isterim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Nobody balks at a price they can see paying for itself; what they're balking at, I suspect, is a cost whose return is invisible to them.","tr":"Kimse kendini amorti ettiğini gördüğü bir fiyattan çekinmez; bence çekindikleri şey, getirisini göremedikleri bir maliyet."},{"who":"Me","en":"By the same token, if we made the monthly savings impossible to ignore, the 4,000-euro price tag would more or less justify itself.","tr":"Aynı mantıkla, aylık tasarrufu göz ardı edilemez hale getirirsek 4.000 euroluk fiyat etiketi kendini aşağı yukarı kendiliğinden haklı çıkarır."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Fair enough, but that's easier said than done, so what exactly do you have in mind?","tr":"Peki, ama söylemesi kolay; tam olarak aklında ne var?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Something almost embarrassingly simple: a calculator showing that a clinic running 100 tests a month saves 1,500 euros.","tr":"Neredeyse utandıracak kadar basit bir şey: ayda 100 test yapan bir kliniğin 1.500 euro tasarruf ettiğini gösteren bir hesaplayıcı."},{"who":"Partner","en":"All right, I'll hold off on the price for two months and we'll see whether the numbers bear you out.","tr":"Peki, fiyat konusunu iki ay bekletiyorum; bakalım rakamlar seni haklı çıkaracak mı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That seems more than fair, and thank you for entertaining a dissenting view.","tr":"Bu fazlasıyla adil, farklı bir görüşü dikkate aldığın için de teşekkür ederim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"play devil's advocate","tr":"şeytanın avukatlığını yapmak","ex":"Let me play devil's advocate for a moment.","def":"to argue for an idea you may not believe, in order to test it"},{"en":"I'd be the last person to...","tr":"...yapacak son kişi benim","ex":"I'd be the last person to say our sales are fast enough.","def":"I would never... (used to show you partly agree)"},{"en":"a steep price to pay","tr":"ağır bir bedel","ex":"Losing half our margin is a steep price to pay for speed.","def":"a high cost, not only in money"},{"en":"notoriously","tr":"bilindiği üzere, kötü şöhretiyle","ex":"Prices are notoriously hard to raise once they fall.","def":"in a way that is well known, usually for something bad or difficult"},{"en":"balk at","tr":"...den çekinmek, ...e yanaşmamak","ex":"Clinics balk at costs they can't justify.","def":"to be unwilling to accept something, such as a price"},{"en":"pay for itself","tr":"kendini amorti etmek","ex":"The device pays for itself within months.","def":"to save or earn as much money as it costs"},{"en":"by the same token","tr":"aynı mantıkla","ex":"By the same token, clear savings would justify the price.","def":"for the same reason; in the same way"},{"en":"easier said than done","tr":"söylemesi kolay, yapması zor","ex":"Showing the value is easier said than done.","def":"simple to suggest but hard to actually do"},{"en":"bear someone out","tr":"birini haklı çıkarmak","ex":"Let's see whether the numbers bear you out.","def":"to show that what someone said is true"},{"en":"entertain a dissenting view","tr":"farklı bir görüşü dikkate almak","ex":"Thank you for entertaining a dissenting view.","def":"to seriously consider an opinion that disagrees with yours"}],"grammar":{"title":"Nuanced hedging: softening disagreement","tr":"C2 düzeyinde itiraz çoğu zaman doğrudan 'hayır' demek yerine yumuşatıcılarla yapılır: I'd gently suggest, I suspect, not quite, rather. Bu ifadeler karşı tarafın yüzünü korurken görüşünü net bırakır.","examples":["I'd gently suggest it isn't quite what they mean.","What they're balking at, I suspect, is a cost whose return is invisible.","We'd be trading a healthy margin for a rather precarious one."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the partner present the idea as playing devil's advocate?","options":["To signal that they are testing an idea, not insisting on it","To show that they are angry","To end the discussion quickly"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker mean by \"a steep price to pay for speed\"?","options":["Fast delivery costs a lot","The device is overpriced","Faster sales would cost too much margin"],"a":2},{"q":"Why, in the speaker's view, would halving the price be hard to undo?","options":["Regulators would object","The market would get used to the lower price","Customers would sign long contracts"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the speaker implying with \"it isn't quite what they mean\"?","options":["Clinics are being dishonest","Clinics want a cheaper model","Clinics have not read the brochure","Clinics are reacting to an unclear return, not the price itself"],"a":3},{"q":"How would you describe the tone of the final exchange?","options":["Grudging and tense","Cooperative, with the decision left to the data","Ironic and dismissive"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Let me play devil's ___ for a moment.","a":"advocate","hint":"avukat"},{"s":"Nobody ___ at a price they can see paying for itself.","a":"balks","hint":"çekinir"},{"s":"By the same ___, clear savings would justify the price.","a":"token","hint":"(aynı) mantıkla"},{"s":"We'll see whether the numbers bear you ___.","a":"out","hint":"haklı çıkarmak"}],"order":[{"a":"I'd gently suggest it isn't quite what they mean."},{"a":"That's easier said than done."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bir an şeytanın avukatlığını yapayım.","en":"Let me play devil's advocate for a moment.","keys":["devil's advocate"]},{"tr":"Söylemesi kolay, yapması zor.","en":"That's easier said than done.","keys":["easier said than done"]},{"tr":"Farklı bir görüşü dikkate aldığın için teşekkürler.","en":"Thank you for entertaining a dissenting view.","keys":["entertaining","dissenting view"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Business partner","personaTr":"İş ortağı","scene":"Ortağın SaaS şirketlerini örnek göstererek donanımı bedava vermeyi savunuyor. Sen ince bir diplomasiyle itiraz edip kararı verilere bırakmayı öneriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Hear me out: what if the hardware were free and we lived entirely off subscriptions, the way every SaaS company does?","aiTr":"Beni bir dinle: donanım ücretsiz olsa ve her SaaS şirketi gibi tamamen aboneliklerden geçinsek?","hint":"It's an intriguing idea, though I'd point out that SaaS companies don't pay 1,500 euros to build each customer's hardware.","keys":["intriguing","I'd point out","hardware"]},{"ai":"Surely the subscriptions would claw that back within a year or two?","aiTr":"Abonelikler bunu bir iki yıl içinde geri kazandırmaz mı?","hint":"Possibly, but at 99 euros a month it would take well over a year per unit, and in the meantime we'd be bankrolling our own customers.","keys":["possibly","in the meantime","bankrolling"]},{"ai":"So you'd rather keep a price that clinics keep telling us is too high?","aiTr":"Yani kliniklerin sürekli çok yüksek dediği bir fiyatı korumayı mı tercih edersin?","hint":"Not necessarily; I'd simply rather we made the savings impossible to ignore before concluding that the price is the problem.","keys":["not necessarily","impossible to ignore","price is the problem"]},{"ai":"All right, I'm not entirely persuaded, but I'm listening. What do you propose?","aiTr":"Peki, tam olarak ikna olmadım ama dinliyorum. Ne öneriyorsun?","hint":"Let's pilot both models with a handful of clinics for two months and let the data settle it.","keys":["pilot","two months","let the data"]}]}},"in-03":{"intro":"Deneyimli bir yatırımcıyla değerleme pazarlığını zarif, ölçülü ve ikna edici bir dille yürütüyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Investor","en":"We've liked what we've seen, so let me cut to the chase: €500,000 for a quarter of the company.","tr":"Gördüklerimizi beğendik, o yüzden lafı dolandırmayayım: şirketin dörtte biri için 500.000 euro."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a generous vote of confidence, and I don't want to sound ungrateful, but it implies a two-million post-money valuation, which frankly leaves a fair amount on the table.","tr":"Bu cömert bir güven oyu ve nankör görünmek istemem ama bu, yatırım sonrası iki milyonluk bir değerleme anlamına geliyor ki açıkçası masada epey değer bırakıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're not pitching a slide deck here; we're pitching a third-generation device that five clinics already pay for every month.","tr":"Burada bir sunum dosyası satmıyoruz; beş kliniğin şimdiden her ay ödeme yaptığı üçüncü nesil bir cihazı anlatıyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Add to that a peer-reviewed study showing 94 percent agreement with trained audiologists, and the technical risk looks rather smaller than your offer assumes.","tr":"Buna eğitimli odyologlarla yüzde 94 uyum gösteren hakemli bir çalışmayı da ekleyin; teknik risk, teklifinizin varsaydığından epey küçük görünüyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our clinical validation, incidentally, was funded by a €250,000 European grant rather than by anyone's equity.","tr":"Bu arada klinik doğrulamamız kimsenin hissesiyle değil, 250.000 euroluk bir Avrupa hibesiyle finanse edildi."},{"who":"Investor","en":"I don't dispute any of that, but you're still pre-CE mark, and regulators are not known for keeping to founders' timelines.","tr":"Bunların hiçbirine itirazım yok ama hâlâ CE işareti öncesindesiniz ve düzenleyiciler kurucuların takvimlerine uymalarıyla pek tanınmaz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Point taken, which is precisely why this round exists: to see certification through and get us into Europe on the front foot.","tr":"Haklısınız; bu tur zaten tam da bu yüzden var: sertifikasyonu sonuna kadar götürmek ve Avrupa'ya güçlü bir başlangıçla girmek."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, I'm not going to pretend the risk is zero, so let's meet in the middle at €2.5 million post-money for 20 percent.","tr":"Bununla birlikte riskin sıfır olduğunu iddia edecek değilim; o yüzden yüzde 20 için yatırım sonrası 2,5 milyonda ortada buluşalım."},{"who":"Investor","en":"I could probably sell that to my partners, on the condition that we take a board seat.","tr":"Yönetim kurulunda bir koltuk almamız koşuluyla bunu muhtemelen ortaklarıma kabul ettirebilirim."},{"who":"Me","en":"By all means, and frankly I'd rather have you in the room arguing with me than writing a cheque and disappearing.","tr":"Elbette; açıkçası çeki yazıp ortadan kaybolmanızdansa odada benimle tartışmanızı tercih ederim."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Fair enough; we'll have a term sheet with you by Friday.","tr":"Makul; cumaya kadar ön anlaşma metni elinizde olur."}],"vocab":[{"en":"cut to the chase","tr":"lafı dolandırmadan sadede gelmek","ex":"Let me cut to the chase: we're offering €500,000.","def":"to get straight to the most important point"},{"en":"vote of confidence","tr":"güven oyu","ex":"The offer is a generous vote of confidence.","def":"an action that shows you trust someone's ability"},{"en":"leave something on the table","tr":"masada (alınabilecek) değer bırakmak","ex":"A two-million valuation leaves money on the table.","def":"to accept less than you could have got in a deal"},{"en":"add to that","tr":"buna bir de ... ekleyin","ex":"Add to that our clinical data, and the risk looks smaller.","def":"used to introduce one more point that strengthens an argument"},{"en":"point taken","tr":"haklısınız, anlaşıldı","ex":"Point taken, the timeline could slip.","def":"used to accept that someone has made a fair argument"},{"en":"see something through","tr":"bir şeyi sonuna kadar götürmek","ex":"This round will let us see certification through.","def":"to continue with a difficult task until it is finished"},{"en":"on the front foot","tr":"güçlü ve inisiyatif sahibi bir konumda","ex":"We want to enter Europe on the front foot.","def":"in a strong, confident position, acting before others do"},{"en":"meet in the middle","tr":"ortada buluşmak","ex":"Let's meet in the middle at 2.5 million.","def":"to agree on a compromise between two positions"},{"en":"sell something to someone","tr":"birini bir şeye ikna etmek","ex":"I could probably sell that to my partners.","def":"to persuade someone to accept an idea or plan"},{"en":"by all means","tr":"elbette, buyurun","ex":"By all means, take a board seat.","def":"a polite and strong way of saying yes"}],"grammar":{"title":"Softening a firm position","tr":"Kesin bir itirazı kibar kılmak için yumuşatıcılar kullanılır: 'I don't want to sound…, but', 'rather', 'probably', 'frankly'. Mesaj net kalır ama ton kırıcı olmaz.","examples":["I don't want to sound ungrateful, but it leaves a fair amount on the table.","The technical risk looks rather smaller than your offer assumes.","I could probably sell that to my partners."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the founder imply by saying 'we're not pitching a slide deck'?","options":["The founder forgot the presentation","The company is past the idea stage and has real traction","The investor should not look at the slides"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the tone of the investor's remark about regulators and founders' timelines?","options":["Dryly ironic","Angry","Apologetic","Enthusiastic"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the founder mention the European grant?","options":["To show they don't need investors","To ask for a bigger grant","To show the clinical work was funded without giving away equity"],"a":2},{"q":"What final terms are agreed?","options":["€2 million post-money for 25 percent","€3 million post-money for 20 percent, with no board seat","€2.5 million post-money for 20 percent, plus a board seat"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the founder's comment about 'writing a cheque and disappearing' suggest?","options":["They want an investor engaged enough to challenge them","They want a passive investor who stays out of the way","They are worried the investor won't pay"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Let me cut to the ___: €500,000 for a quarter of the company.","a":"chase","hint":"sadede gelmek"},{"s":"Frankly, it leaves a fair amount on the ___.","a":"table","hint":"masa"},{"s":"This round exists to see certification ___.","a":"through","hint":"sonuna kadar götürmek"},{"s":"Let's meet in the ___ at €2.5 million post-money.","a":"middle","hint":"orta"}],"order":[{"a":"I could probably sell that to my partners."},{"a":"Regulators are not known for keeping to founders' timelines."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Nankör görünmek istemem ama bu, masada para bırakıyor.","en":"I don't want to sound ungrateful, but this leaves money on the table.","keys":["sound ungrateful","on the table"]},{"tr":"Riskin sıfır olduğunu iddia edecek değilim.","en":"I'm not going to pretend the risk is zero.","keys":["pretend","risk is zero"]},{"tr":"Ortada buluşalım.","en":"Let's meet in the middle.","keys":["meet in the middle"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Senior partner at a VC fund","personaTr":"Bir VC fonunun kıdemli ortağı","scene":"Kıdemli bir ortak doğrudan rakam veriyor; değerlemeyi zarafetle ama net bir şekilde yukarı çekiyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll cut to the chase: €500,000 for a quarter of the company. Can you live with that?","aiTr":"Sadede geleyim: şirketin dörtte biri için 500.000 euro. Buna razı olabilir misiniz?","hint":"It's a generous vote of confidence, but a two-million post-money valuation leaves a fair amount on the table.","keys":["vote of confidence","on the table","two-million"]},{"ai":"Go on, then. What am I missing?","aiTr":"Buyurun o zaman. Neyi gözden kaçırıyorum?","hint":"We're not pitching a slide deck: five clinics already pay for the device, and a peer-reviewed study shows 94 percent agreement with audiologists.","keys":["slide deck","five clinics","peer-reviewed","94 percent"]},{"ai":"Be that as it may, you're still pre-CE mark, and regulators rarely keep to founders' timelines.","aiTr":"Öyle olsa bile hâlâ CE işareti öncesindesiniz ve düzenleyiciler kurucuların takvimine nadiren uyar.","hint":"Point taken, which is precisely why this round exists: to see certification through and get us into Europe.","keys":["point taken","see certification through","precisely"]},{"ai":"So where does that leave us?","aiTr":"Peki bu bizi nereye getiriyor?","hint":"I won't pretend the risk is zero, so let's meet in the middle: €2.5 million post-money for 20 percent, with a board seat for you.","keys":["meet in the middle","2.5 million","20 percent","board seat"]}]}},"ai-05":{"intro":"Her satıcının aynı vaatleri verdiğini düşünen deneyimli ve şüpheci bir satın alma direktörünü, ölçülü ve esprili bir dille ikna ediyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Buyer","en":"I'll spare you the small talk: every vendor who walks through that door tells me their device will pay for itself.","tr":"Lafı uzatmayacağım: O kapıdan giren her satıcı bana cihazının kendini amorti edeceğini söylüyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd be surprised if they didn't, so let me try to earn the claim rather than simply assert it.","tr":"Söylemeselerdi şaşırırdım; o yüzden bu iddiayı öylece ileri sürmek yerine hak ettiğimi göstermeye çalışayım."},{"who":"Me","en":"The unit is €4,000, with a software subscription of €99 a month per clinic, which, admittedly, puts us well above a conventional audiometer on paper.","tr":"Cihaz 4.000 euro, buna klinik başına ayda 99 euroluk yazılım aboneliği ekleniyor; kabul etmek gerekir ki bu, bizi kâğıt üzerinde klasik bir odyometrenin epey üstüne koyuyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Where the comparison starts to tilt, though, is staffing: the test runs in under ten minutes with no audiologist in the room.","tr":"Ancak karşılaştırmanın lehimize dönmeye başladığı yer personel: Test, odada odyolog olmadan on dakikadan kısa sürede tamamlanıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"In other words, your specialists stop spending their days on routine screenings and get back to the cases that genuinely warrant their expertise.","tr":"Başka bir deyişle uzmanlarınız günlerini rutin taramalarla geçirmeyi bırakıp gerçekten uzmanlık gerektiren vakalara dönüyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"That's all very well, but our data protection officer will have my head if patient data ends up on some server abroad.","tr":"Bunlar güzel de hasta verileri yurt dışında bir sunucuya düşerse veri koruma görevlimiz kellemi alır."},{"who":"Me","en":"Then you can set their mind at rest: the AI runs entirely on the device, so nothing needs to leave your network, and it works offline to boot.","tr":"O zaman içini rahatlatabilirsiniz: Yapay zekâ tamamen cihaz üzerinde çalışıyor, yani hiçbir şeyin ağınızdan çıkması gerekmiyor; üstelik internetsiz de çalışıyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"And when it inevitably breaks down at the worst possible moment?","tr":"Peki kaçınılmaz olarak en kötü anda bozulduğunda?"},{"who":"Me","en":"You'd be covered by a two-year warranty, and in our experience most issues are resolved remotely with a software update before anyone has to call a technician.","tr":"İki yıllık garanti kapsamında olursunuz ve deneyimimize göre çoğu sorun, kimse teknisyen çağırmak zorunda kalmadan bir yazılım güncellemesiyle uzaktan çözülüyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"Even so, I'd want to see it hold up in our own clinics before putting my name to anything.","tr":"Yine de herhangi bir şeye imza atmadan önce cihazın kendi kliniklerimizde ayakta kaldığını görmek isterim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Which is precisely why we offer a free one-month trial: installation takes about an hour, and we train your staff the same day.","tr":"Tam da bu yüzden bir aylık ücretsiz deneme sunuyoruz: Kurulum yaklaşık bir saat sürüyor ve personelinizi aynı gün eğitiyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"If it doesn't earn its keep in that month, by all means send it back, no hard feelings.","tr":"O ay içinde masrafına değmezse lütfen geri gönderin, hiç gönül koymayız."}],"vocab":[{"en":"spare someone the small talk","tr":"lafı uzatmamak, sohbeti atlamak","ex":"Let me spare you the small talk and get to the price.","def":"to skip polite conversation and get to the point"},{"en":"pay for itself","tr":"kendini amorti etmek","ex":"Every vendor says their device will pay for itself.","def":"to save or earn as much money as it cost"},{"en":"tilt","tr":"(denge) bir tarafa kaymak","ex":"The comparison starts to tilt in our favor when you look at staffing.","def":"to start to favor one side"},{"en":"warrant","tr":"gerektirmek, hak etmek","ex":"Only complex cases warrant a specialist's time.","def":"to make something necessary or deserved"},{"en":"have someone's head","tr":"birinin kellesini almak","ex":"Our data protection officer will have my head.","def":"(informal) to punish or blame someone severely"},{"en":"set someone's mind at rest","tr":"birinin içini rahatlatmak","ex":"This should set your mind at rest.","def":"to stop someone from worrying"},{"en":"to boot","tr":"üstelik, cabası","ex":"It's fast, and it works offline to boot.","def":"as well; in addition"},{"en":"hold up","tr":"dayanmak, sağlam çıkmak","ex":"I want to see it hold up in our own clinics.","def":"to remain strong or valid when tested"},{"en":"earn its keep","tr":"masrafına değmek, hakkını vermek","ex":"If it doesn't earn its keep, send it back.","def":"to be worth the money spent on it"},{"en":"no hard feelings","tr":"gönül koymak yok","ex":"If you decide against it, no hard feelings.","def":"used to say you won't be upset or offended"}],"grammar":{"title":"Conceding a point without losing ground","tr":"'Admittedly', 'in our experience', 'I'd be surprised if…' gibi ifadelerle karşı tarafın haklı olduğu noktayı kabul eder, yine de kendi argümanını güçlü tutarsın. Şüpheci alıcılar karşısında güven kazandırır.","examples":["I'd be surprised if they didn't.","Admittedly, it puts us well above a conventional audiometer on paper.","In our experience, most issues are resolved remotely."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of the buyer's opening line?","options":["Warm and enthusiastic","Wearily skeptical","Openly hostile","Confused"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the founder mean by 'earn the claim rather than simply assert it'?","options":["Back it up with concrete reasons","Repeat it more confidently","Lower the price","Avoid making any claims"],"a":0},{"q":"According to the founder, where does the device's real value lie?","options":["Its low purchase price","Its design","Freeing specialists from routine screenings","Its cloud storage"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the buyer imply with 'when it inevitably breaks down at the worst possible moment'?","options":["The device has already failed in their hospital","They don't need a warranty","They want a discount","Experience tells them all equipment fails eventually, so support matters"],"a":3},{"q":"What attitude does the founder's final line convey?","options":["Desperation to close the deal","Quiet confidence in the product","Indifference to the sale","Irritation with the buyer"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Every vendor tells me their device will pay for ___.","a":"itself","hint":"kendini (amorti etmek)"},{"s":"Your specialists get back to the cases that genuinely ___ their expertise.","a":"warrant","hint":"gerektirmek"},{"s":"Then you can set their mind at ___.","a":"rest","hint":"rahat (içini rahatlatmak)"},{"s":"If it doesn't earn its ___ in that month, send it back.","a":"keep","hint":"masrafına değmek (earn its …)"}],"order":[{"a":"I'd want to see it hold up in our clinics."},{"a":"Nothing needs to leave your network."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kabul etmek gerekir ki kâğıt üzerinde klasik bir odyometrenin epey üstündeyiz.","en":"Admittedly, on paper we're well above a conventional audiometer.","keys":["admittedly","on paper","well above"]},{"tr":"Üstelik internetsiz de çalışıyor.","en":"It works offline to boot.","keys":["offline","to boot"]},{"tr":"Masrafına değmezse geri gönderin.","en":"If it doesn't earn its keep, send it back.","keys":["earn its keep","send it back"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Procurement director","personaTr":"Satın alma direktörü","scene":"Deneyimli ve şüpheci bir satın alma direktörü her satıcının aynı vaatleri verdiğini düşünüyor; onu somut gerekçelerle ikna etmelisin.","turns":[{"ai":"Every vendor tells me their kit pays for itself. Why should I believe you're any different?","aiTr":"Her satıcı bana ekipmanının kendini amorti ettiğini söylüyor. Sizin farklı olduğunuza neden inanayım?","hint":"Fair enough, so let me earn the claim: the test runs in under ten minutes with no audiologist in the room, which frees your specialists for the cases that genuinely warrant their expertise.","keys":["no audiologist","under ten minutes","warrant","specialists"]},{"ai":"Our data protection officer will have my head if patient data leaves the building.","aiTr":"Hasta verileri binadan çıkarsa veri koruma görevlimiz kellemi alır.","hint":"Then you can set their mind at rest: the AI runs entirely on the device, so nothing needs to leave your network, and it works offline to boot.","keys":["on the device","mind at rest","offline","leave your network"]},{"ai":"And when it breaks down at the worst possible moment, as these things do?","aiTr":"Peki bu tür cihazların hep yaptığı gibi en kötü anda bozulduğunda?","hint":"You'd be covered by a two-year warranty, and in our experience most issues are resolved remotely with a software update.","keys":["two-year warranty","remotely","software update"]},{"ai":"I'm not putting my name to anything until I've seen it in our own clinics.","aiTr":"Kendi kliniklerimizde görmeden hiçbir şeye imza atmam.","hint":"Nor would I expect you to, which is precisely why we offer a free one-month trial; if it doesn't earn its keep, send it back.","keys":["trial","earn its keep","send it back"]}]}},"te-04":{"intro":"Kritik bir mimari tercihi ustalıkla tartışıyor, karşı argümanları kabul edip kararını net biçimde savunuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Engineer","en":"Before we freeze the hardware spec, there's one architectural question we can't keep kicking down the road: does the model live on the device or in the cloud?","tr":"Donanım spesifikasyonunu dondurmadan önce, daha fazla erteleyemeyeceğimiz bir mimari soru var: model cihazda mı yaşayacak, bulutta mı?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Make the strongest case you can for the cloud, and then let's see whether it survives contact with our customers.","tr":"Bulut için yapabileceğin en güçlü savunmayı yap, sonra da bunun müşterilerimizle karşılaşınca ayakta kalıp kalmadığına bakalım."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"In the cloud we could run a far heavier model and iterate on it as often as we liked, without ever touching a unit in the field.","tr":"Bulutta çok daha ağır bir model çalıştırabilir ve sahadaki tek bir cihaza bile dokunmadan onu istediğimiz sıklıkta geliştirebilirdik."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"The rub, of course, is that every single test would then be hostage to the clinic's internet connection, which in a small-town practice is anything but guaranteed.","tr":"İşin sıkıntılı yanı tabii ki her bir testin kliniğin internet bağlantısına mahkûm olması; küçük bir kasaba muayenehanesinde bu hiç de garanti değil."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"And that's before we get to the hospitals whose data policies flatly forbid patient information from leaving the building.","tr":"Üstelik daha, veri politikaları hasta bilgisinin binadan çıkmasını kesinlikle yasaklayan hastanelere gelmedik bile."},{"who":"Me","en":"Whereas keeping it on the device buys us what, exactly?","tr":"Peki modeli cihazda tutmak bize tam olarak ne kazandırıyor?"},{"who":"Engineer","en":"Privacy by design and a test that works offline — at the cost of a heftier bill of materials and a model we'd have to trim to fit.","tr":"Tasarımdan gelen gizlilik ve çevrimdışı çalışan bir test — bunun bedeli de daha yüklü bir malzeme maliyeti ve sığması için küçültmemiz gereken bir model."},{"who":"Me","en":"Frankly, I've yet to sit down with a hospital IT team that didn't raise privacy within the first five minutes.","tr":"Açıkçası, ilk beş dakika içinde gizliliği gündeme getirmeyen bir hastane bilgi işlem ekibiyle henüz hiç oturmadım."},{"who":"Me","en":"Admittedly, it dents the margin, but a somewhat higher unit cost strikes me as a small price for taking one of the most common objections off the table.","tr":"Kabul ediyorum, kâr marjını biraz zedeliyor, ama en sık duyduğumuz itirazlardan birini ortadan kaldırmak için biraz daha yüksek bir birim maliyeti bana küçük bir bedel gibi geliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"So let's keep the model on the device and ship updates monthly, whenever a unit happens to be connected.","tr":"O halde modeli cihazda tutalım ve güncellemeleri, cihaz ne zaman bağlanırsa, ayda bir gönderelim."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"Fair enough — it's a genuine trade-off, but I'd much rather justify a higher unit cost than explain a data breach to a hospital board.","tr":"Makul — bu gerçek bir ödünleşim, ama bir hastane yönetim kuruluna veri ihlali açıklamaktansa daha yüksek bir birim maliyetini savunmayı çok daha fazla tercih ederim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"kick something down the road","tr":"bir şeyi sürekli ertelemek","ex":"We can't keep kicking this decision down the road.","def":"to keep delaying dealing with a problem"},{"en":"survive contact with","tr":"...ile karşılaşınca ayakta kalmak","ex":"Let's see whether the plan survives contact with our customers.","def":"to still work when tested in reality"},{"en":"the rub","tr":"işin sıkıntılı noktası","ex":"The rub is that every test depends on the internet.","def":"the main difficulty (slightly literary)"},{"en":"be hostage to","tr":"...ye mahkûm olmak, ...nin insafına kalmak","ex":"Every test would be hostage to the connection.","def":"to be controlled by something you cannot control"},{"en":"anything but","tr":"hiç de ... değil","ex":"A stable connection is anything but guaranteed.","def":"not at all"},{"en":"privacy by design","tr":"tasarımdan gelen gizlilik","ex":"On-device AI gives us privacy by design.","def":"privacy built into a product from the start"},{"en":"bill of materials","tr":"malzeme listesi (ve maliyeti)","ex":"A heftier bill of materials raises our unit cost.","def":"the list and cost of all the parts needed to build a product"},{"en":"I've yet to","tr":"henüz hiç ...medim","ex":"I've yet to meet an IT team that didn't raise privacy.","def":"used to say something has not happened so far"},{"en":"dent the margin","tr":"kâr marjını zedelemek","ex":"Admittedly, it dents the margin.","def":"to reduce profit a little"},{"en":"take something off the table","tr":"bir şeyi gündemden çıkarmak, ortadan kaldırmak","ex":"It takes a common objection off the table.","def":"to remove something as an issue"}],"grammar":{"title":"Conceding a point: Admittedly…, but…","tr":"İkna ederken önce karşı tarafın haklı olduğu noktayı kabul edip ('Admittedly', 'Fair enough', 'Granted') ardından asıl argümanınızı 'but' ile sunmak sizi hem dürüst hem güçlü gösterir.","examples":["Admittedly, it dents the margin, but the price is worth it.","Fair enough, it's a genuine trade-off, but privacy comes first.","Granted, the cloud is more powerful, but our customers want privacy."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the engineer insist on deciding now?","options":["The hardware spec is about to be frozen","An investor demanded it","The cloud provider raised its prices"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'see whether it survives contact with our customers' imply?","options":["The founder has already chosen the cloud","Any option must hold up against real customer concerns","Customers have rejected the device"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'I've yet to sit down with a hospital IT team that didn't raise privacy' suggest?","options":["The founder has never met a hospital IT team","IT teams rarely care about privacy","Privacy comes up in virtually every hospital meeting"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of the founder's comment on the margin?","options":["Dismissive and careless","Candid but firm","Anxious and uncertain"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the engineer's final position?","options":["Accepts the decision, preferring a higher cost to a privacy failure","Still pushes for the cloud","Wants to delay the decision"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"There's one question we can't keep kicking down the ___.","a":"road","hint":"yol (ertelemek)"},{"s":"Every test would be ___ to the clinic's internet connection.","a":"hostage","hint":"mahkûm, rehin"},{"s":"I've ___ to sit down with a hospital IT team that didn't raise privacy.","a":"yet","hint":"henüz"},{"s":"It takes one of the most common objections off the ___.","a":"table","hint":"masa (gündem)"}],"order":[{"a":"A stable connection is anything but guaranteed."},{"a":"Let's keep the model on the device and ship updates monthly."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kabul ediyorum, kâr marjını zedeliyor.","en":"Admittedly, it dents the margin.","keys":["admittedly","dents the margin"]},{"tr":"Bu, en sık duyduğumuz itirazlardan birini ortadan kaldırıyor.","en":"It takes one of the most common objections off the table.","keys":["objections","off the table"]},{"tr":"Tasarımdan gelen gizlilik sunuyoruz.","en":"We offer privacy by design.","keys":["privacy by design"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hospital chief information officer","personaTr":"Hastanenin bilgi işlem direktörü (CIO)","scene":"Bir üniversite hastanesinin bilgi işlem direktörü mimari tercihinizi sorguluyor ve kolay ikna olmuyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Every vendor tells me their system is secure, so forgive me if I'm sceptical — where does our patients' data actually go?","aiTr":"Her tedarikçi bana sisteminin güvenli olduğunu söylüyor, şüpheciliğimi mazur görün — hastalarımızın verisi aslında nereye gidiyor?","hint":"Healthy scepticism; the honest answer is nowhere, because the model runs entirely on the device, so privacy is built in by design.","keys":["on the device","by design","nowhere"]},{"ai":"Surely running it locally means you're compromising on accuracy?","aiTr":"Yerelde çalıştırmak doğruluktan taviz verdiğiniz anlamına gelmiyor mu?","hint":"We did have to trim the model to fit, admittedly, but it still matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases in our clinical study.","keys":["admittedly","94","trim the model"]},{"ai":"And when the connection in a rural clinic drops out halfway through a test?","aiTr":"Peki kırsaldaki bir klinikte test yarıdayken bağlantı koparsa?","hint":"The test simply carries on, because it works offline and is never hostage to the connection.","keys":["works offline","hostage","carries on"]},{"ai":"How do you keep the model from falling behind, then?","aiTr":"O zaman modelin geride kalmasını nasıl önlüyorsunuz?","hint":"We ship an update once a month whenever a unit happens to be connected, so it never falls far behind.","keys":["once a month","ship an update","connected"]}]}},"li-02":{"intro":"Reddedilmenin psikolojisini ve bir 'hayır'ı zamanla 'evet'e dönüştürmeyi, deneyimli bir girişimcinin incelikli diliyle anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"If selling has taught me anything, it's that a 'no' is seldom a verdict on the product.","tr":"Satış bana bir şey öğrettiyse, o da bir 'hayır'ın nadiren ürün hakkında bir hüküm olduğudur."},{"who":"Me","en":"Nine times out of ten, it boils down to one of three things: trust, understanding or timing.","tr":"On vakadan dokuzunda mesele özünde üç şeyden birine dayanır: güven, anlama ya da zamanlama."},{"who":"Me","en":"Trust, for its part, is rarely won in the boardroom; it accrues quietly, through a clean website, a prompt reply, a customer prepared to vouch for you.","tr":"Güven ise nadiren toplantı odasında kazanılır; derli toplu bir web sitesiyle, hızlı bir cevapla, size kefil olmaya hazır bir müşteriyle sessizce birikir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Understanding is a matter of clarity, and here the rule is brutally simple: if a buyer needs an engineer to decode your pitch, you've lost them before you've begun.","tr":"Anlaşılmak bir netlik meselesidir ve kural acımasızca basittir: bir alıcı sunumunuzu çözmek için mühendise ihtiyaç duyuyorsa, daha başlamadan onu kaybetmişsinizdir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Timing is the slipperiest of the three, since what moves people, by and large, isn't a better option but a worse status quo.","tr":"Zamanlama üçü arasında en kaygan olanıdır, çünkü insanları harekete geçiren genellikle daha iyi bir seçenek değil, kötüleşen mevcut durumdur."},{"who":"Me","en":"Put bluntly, nobody abandons a familiar process until living with it hurts more than replacing it.","tr":"Açıkçası, kimse alışık olduğu bir süreci, onunla yaşamak onu değiştirmekten daha çok can yakana kadar bırakmaz."},{"who":"Me","en":"So before every meeting I put three questions to myself: why on earth should they trust me, could they grasp this in a minute, and where exactly does it hurt?","tr":"Bu yüzden her toplantıdan önce kendime üç soru sorarım: bana neden güvensinler ki, bunu bir dakikada kavrayabilirler mi ve tam olarak neresi acıyor?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Last year, a clinic that had seemed genuinely keen turned us down, which, I'll admit, stung.","tr":"Geçen yıl, gerçekten istekli görünen bir klinik bizi geri çevirdi ve itiraf edeyim, bu canımı sıktı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Rather than chase them, we simply stayed in touch, and when we asked again three months later, their waiting list had spiralled to the point where saying no had become the riskier option.","tr":"Peşlerine düşmek yerine sadece iletişimde kaldık; üç ay sonra tekrar sorduğumuzda bekleme listeleri öyle kontrolden çıkmıştı ki hayır demek daha riskli seçenek haline gelmişti."},{"who":"Me","en":"Tellingly, our offer hadn't changed in the slightest; their pain had.","tr":"Manidar olan şu ki teklifimiz zerre kadar değişmemişti; değişen onların sıkıntısıydı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, I try not to read every refusal as a hidden yes, since some prospects are simply not a fit.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, her reddi gizli bir 'evet' olarak okumamaya çalışırım, çünkü bazı potansiyel müşteriler bize gerçekten uygun değildir."},{"who":"Me","en":"More often than not, though, a 'no' today is merely a 'not yet' in disguise.","tr":"Yine de çoğu zaman bugünkü bir 'hayır', kılık değiştirmiş bir 'henüz değil'den ibarettir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"boil down to","tr":"özünde ...e dayanmak","ex":"Most refusals boil down to trust, understanding or timing.","def":"to have something as its most basic cause"},{"en":"accrue","tr":"birikmek","ex":"Trust accrues quietly through small signals.","def":"to grow gradually over time"},{"en":"vouch for","tr":"kefil olmak","ex":"A customer prepared to vouch for you is worth a dozen adverts.","def":"to say publicly that someone is reliable"},{"en":"status quo","tr":"mevcut durum","ex":"People move when the status quo gets worse.","def":"the existing state of affairs"},{"en":"put bluntly","tr":"açık konuşmak gerekirse","ex":"Put bluntly, nobody likes change.","def":"said in a very direct and honest way"},{"en":"sting","tr":"canını yakmak, koymak","ex":"It can sting when a keen prospect says no.","def":"to hurt someone's feelings for a short time"},{"en":"spiral","tr":"kontrolden çıkmak, hızla artmak","ex":"Their waiting list had spiralled.","def":"to increase quickly and get out of control"},{"en":"tellingly","tr":"manidar biçimde","ex":"Tellingly, our offer hadn't changed at all.","def":"in a way that reveals something important"},{"en":"prospect","tr":"potansiyel müşteri","ex":"Some prospects are simply not a fit.","def":"a person or company that might become a customer"},{"en":"in disguise","tr":"kılık değiştirmiş","ex":"A 'no' is often a 'not yet' in disguise.","def":"looking like something else, so its true nature is hidden"}],"grammar":{"title":"Hedging with frequency and concession","tr":"C2 düzeyinde kesin genellemelerden kaçınılır: 'nine times out of ten', 'by and large', 'more often than not' gibi ifadeler iddiayı yumuşatır. 'That said' ve 'I'll admit' ise karşı görüşü kabul ederek dengeli bir ton kurar.","examples":["Nine times out of ten, it boils down to trust, understanding or timing.","What moves people, by and large, isn't a better option but a worse status quo.","That said, I try not to read every refusal as a hidden yes."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the speaker, what is a 'no' seldom about?","options":["Timing","The product itself","Trust","Clarity"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'a worse status quo'?","options":["A competitor's cheaper offer","A drop in product quality","A current situation that has become painful"],"a":2},{"q":"What does 'Tellingly' imply about the clinic's change of mind?","options":["It was driven by their pain, not by a better product","The team was too lazy to improve the offer","The clinic had been misled"],"a":0},{"q":"How would you describe the tone of 'which, I'll admit, stung'?","options":["Bitter and resentful","Sarcastic towards the clinic","Detached and clinical","Candid and slightly self-deprecating"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the sentence beginning 'That said' add to the argument?","options":["A caveat that not every refusal is temporary","A claim that every 'no' becomes a 'yes'","A complaint about difficult customers"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Nine times out of ten, a refusal ___ down to trust, understanding or timing.","a":"boils","hint":"özünde ...e dayanır"},{"s":"Trust ___ quietly, through a clean website and a prompt reply.","a":"accrues","hint":"birikir"},{"s":"What moves people isn't a better option but a worse ___.","a":"status quo","hint":"mevcut durum"},{"s":"A 'no' today is often a 'not yet' in ___.","a":"disguise","hint":"kılık değiştirmiş"}],"order":[{"a":"Our offer had not changed but their pain had."},{"a":"Trust is rarely won in the boardroom."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Açıkçası, kimse alışık olduğu bir süreci kolay kolay bırakmaz.","en":"Put bluntly, nobody abandons a familiar process easily.","keys":["put bluntly","familiar process"]},{"tr":"Bununla birlikte, her reddi gizli bir 'evet' olarak okumamaya çalışıyorum.","en":"That said, I try not to read every refusal as a hidden yes.","keys":["that said","refusal","hidden yes"]},{"tr":"Teklifimiz hiç değişmemişti; değişen onların sıkıntısıydı.","en":"Our offer hadn't changed at all; what had changed was their pain.","keys":["hadn't changed","their pain"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hesitant clinic owner","personaTr":"Kararsız klinik sahibi","scene":"Deneyimli ve temkinli bir klinik sahibi, cihazı beğense de değişime direniyor. Asıl sıkıntıyı ortaya çıkarmalı, riski ortadan kaldırmalı ve ilişkiyi zarafetle sürdürmelisin.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll be frank: the device is impressive, but I'm not convinced now is the moment to rock the boat.","aiTr":"Açık konuşacağım: cihaz etkileyici ama şu an ortalığı karıştırmanın doğru zaman olduğuna ikna olmuş değilim.","hint":"I appreciate the candour. If you don't mind my asking, what's keeping you up at night at the moment?","keys":["appreciate","keeping you up at night","if you don't mind"]},{"ai":"If I'm honest, it's the six-week wait for hearing tests, but tearing up a workflow that broadly works hardly feels like the answer.","aiTr":"Dürüst olmak gerekirse, işitme testleri için altı haftalık bekleme; ama genel olarak işleyen bir iş akışını yıkıp atmak da pek çözüm gibi gelmiyor.","hint":"Nor would I suggest it. Why not run it free for a month alongside your current set-up and let the waiting list do the talking?","keys":["free for a month","alongside","waiting list"]},{"ai":"And if my audiologists turn their noses up at it?","aiTr":"Ya odyologlarım burun kıvırırsa?","hint":"Then you walk away with nothing lost, though in my experience they warm to it once it frees them up for the trickier cases.","keys":["walk away","nothing lost","warm to it","trickier cases"]},{"ai":"Let me mull it over with the team and get back to you.","aiTr":"Ekiple bir düşüneyim, size dönerim.","hint":"By all means, there's no rush. I'll send over a one-page summary for the team and check in next week, if that suits you.","keys":["by all means","no rush","summary","check in"]}]}},"fu-02":{"intro":"Deneyimli bir gazeteciyle sağlık verilerinin etiği üzerine; hasta özerkliği, onam ve gizlilik ile yapay zekâ arasındaki gerilimi incelikli bir dille tartışıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Journalist","en":"It's become something of a cliché to call health data the new oil, but if it is, who exactly holds the drilling rights?","tr":"Sağlık verilerine yeni petrol demek neredeyse klişe oldu; ama öyleyse sondaj hakları tam olarak kimde?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The patient, unequivocally, and I'd go further: ownership is a hollow notion unless it comes with meaningful control over who uses the data, and to what end.","tr":"Kesinlikle hastada; hatta daha da ileri giderim: veriyi kimin, ne amaçla kullandığı üzerinde anlamlı bir kontrol yoksa sahiplik içi boş bir kavramdır."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's what informed consent is supposed to guarantee, though all too often it's reduced to a checkbox nobody reads.","tr":"Bilgilendirilmiş onamın güvence altına alması gereken şey budur; ama çoğu zaman kimsenin okumadığı bir kutucuğa indirgenir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Consent worth the name is specific, intelligible and, above all, revocable; anything less is a legal fig leaf.","tr":"Adına layık bir onam belirli, anlaşılır ve her şeyden önce geri alınabilir olmalıdır; bunun altındaki her şey hukuki bir göstermelik örtüdür."},{"who":"Me","en":"Anonymisation is the other safeguard, although stripping out names is, frankly, the bare minimum, since a postcode and a date of birth can be enough to re-identify someone.","tr":"Anonimleştirme diğer güvencedir; ama açıkçası isimleri silmek asgari düzeydir, çünkü bir posta kodu ve doğum tarihi birinin kimliğini yeniden belirlemeye yetebilir."},{"who":"Me","en":"In Europe, GDPR rightly treats health data as a special category, which raises the bar considerably for anyone wishing to process it.","tr":"Avrupa'da GDPR haklı olarak sağlık verilerini özel nitelikli kategori sayar; bu da onları işlemek isteyen herkes için çıtayı epey yükseltir."},{"who":"Me","en":"We took the view that privacy shouldn't be bolted on after the fact, so our AI runs on the device and test data never leaves the clinic.","tr":"Gizliliğin sonradan iliştirilmemesi gerektiği görüşündeydik; bu yüzden yapay zekâmız cihazın üzerinde çalışıyor ve test verileri klinikten hiç çıkmıyor."},{"who":"Journalist","en":"Isn't that a rather expensive principle, given that your competitors' models presumably grow smarter with every record they hoard?","tr":"Rakiplerinizin modelleri muhtemelen istifledikleri her kayıtla daha da akıllanırken, bu oldukça pahalı bir ilke değil mi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I won't pretend otherwise: more data does make for better models, and every dataset you keep is, by the same token, one more thing that can leak.","tr":"Aksini iddia etmeyeceğim: daha fazla veri gerçekten daha iyi modeller sağlar ve aynı mantıkla, tuttuğunuz her veri seti sızabilecek bir şey daha demektir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our compromise is to improve the model solely with anonymised data from clinical studies whose participants gave explicit consent, and to accept that progress will be somewhat slower.","tr":"Bizim uzlaşmamız, modeli yalnızca katılımcılarının açık onay verdiği klinik çalışmalardan gelen anonim verilerle geliştirmek ve ilerlemenin biraz daha yavaş olacağını kabul etmek."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, I'd argue it's less a sacrifice than an investment, since in healthcare trust takes years to earn and a single breach to squander.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, bunun bir fedakârlıktan çok bir yatırım olduğunu savunurum, çünkü sağlıkta güveni kazanmak yıllar alır, heba etmek ise tek bir ihlal."}],"vocab":[{"en":"unequivocally","tr":"kesinlikle, tereddütsüz","ex":"The data belongs, unequivocally, to the patient.","def":"in a way that leaves no doubt"},{"en":"a hollow notion","tr":"içi boş bir kavram","ex":"Ownership is a hollow notion without control.","def":"an idea that sounds good but has no real meaning"},{"en":"to what end","tr":"ne amaçla","ex":"Patients should know who uses their data and to what end.","def":"for what purpose"},{"en":"fig leaf","tr":"göstermelik örtü","ex":"Weak consent is just a legal fig leaf.","def":"something used to hide an embarrassing truth"},{"en":"the bare minimum","tr":"asgari düzey","ex":"Removing names is the bare minimum.","def":"the smallest amount that is acceptable"},{"en":"re-identify","tr":"kimliğini yeniden belirlemek","ex":"A postcode can be enough to re-identify someone.","def":"to work out who a person is from anonymous data"},{"en":"bolt on","tr":"sonradan iliştirmek","ex":"Privacy shouldn't be bolted on after the fact.","def":"to add something as an extra rather than as part of the original design"},{"en":"hoard","tr":"istiflemek","ex":"Some companies hoard every record they can.","def":"to collect and keep large amounts of something"},{"en":"make for","tr":"sağlamak, ...e yol açmak","ex":"More data does make for better models.","def":"to result in or help to create"},{"en":"squander","tr":"heba etmek","ex":"A single breach can squander years of trust.","def":"to waste something valuable"}],"grammar":{"title":"Concession and emphatic 'do'","tr":"Karşı tarafın haklı olduğu noktayı kabul etmek için 'I won't pretend otherwise', 'frankly', 'that said' gibi ifadeler; vurgu için yardımcı fiil 'do/does' kullanılır: 'more data does make for better models'. 'Less a X than a Y' yapısı bir kavramı zarifçe yeniden çerçeveler.","examples":["I won't pretend otherwise: more data does make for better models.","That said, I'd argue it's less a sacrifice than an investment.","Stripping out names is, frankly, the bare minimum."]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the speaker answer the question of ownership?","options":["Hesitantly, saying it depends","Unequivocally: the patient owns it","By saying it belongs to the clinic","By avoiding the question"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker call stripping out names 'the bare minimum'?","options":["Because GDPR forbids it","Because names are not personal data","Because a postcode and a date of birth can still identify someone"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the tone of the journalist's question about 'drilling rights'?","options":["Playfully ironic, extending the 'new oil' metaphor","Angry and accusatory","Purely technical","Sympathetic"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'a legal fig leaf' imply about weak consent?","options":["It gives patients too much power","It is too expensive","It is required by GDPR","It covers the company legally while hiding the lack of real choice"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the final sentence suggest about the company's choice?","options":["It is a long-term bet that trust will pay off","It was forced on them by regulators","It will be reversed soon"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"The patient, ___, and I'd go further.","a":"unequivocally","hint":"kesinlikle"},{"s":"Anything less is a legal fig ___.","a":"leaf","hint":"yaprak (deyim: göstermelik örtü)"},{"s":"Privacy shouldn't be ___ on after the fact.","a":"bolted","hint":"sonradan iliştirilmek"},{"s":"Trust takes years to earn and a single breach to ___.","a":"squander","hint":"heba etmek"}],"order":[{"a":"Test data never leaves the clinic."},{"a":"Trust takes years to earn."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kontrol olmadan sahiplik içi boş bir kavramdır.","en":"Ownership is a hollow notion without control.","keys":["hollow notion","ownership"]},{"tr":"Aksini iddia etmeyeceğim: daha fazla veri gerçekten daha iyi modeller sağlar.","en":"I won't pretend otherwise: more data does make for better models.","keys":["won't pretend otherwise","make for better models"]},{"tr":"Bunu bir fedakârlıktan çok bir yatırım olarak görüyorum.","en":"I see it less as a sacrifice than as an investment.","keys":["less as a sacrifice","investment"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Journalist","personaTr":"Gazeteci","scene":"Keskin dilli, deneyimli bir gazeteci seni ilkelerinle iş modelin arasında sıkıştırmaya çalışıyor. Zarif, dürüst ve kararlı yanıtlar veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Everyone calls health data the new oil; so who, in your view, holds the drilling rights?","aiTr":"Herkes sağlık verisine yeni petrol diyor; sizce sondaj hakları kimde?","hint":"The patient, unequivocally, and ownership is a hollow notion unless it comes with real control over who uses the data and to what end.","keys":["unequivocally","hollow notion","to what end"]},{"ai":"Be honest: isn't informed consent mostly a checkbox that protects companies rather than patients?","aiTr":"Dürüst olun: bilgilendirilmiş onam çoğunlukla hastaları değil şirketleri koruyan bir kutucuk değil mi?","hint":"All too often, yes; consent worth the name is specific, intelligible and revocable, and anything less is a legal fig leaf.","keys":["revocable","fig leaf","worth the name"]},{"ai":"And what makes your company any different?","aiTr":"Peki sizin şirketinizi farklı kılan ne?","hint":"We didn't bolt privacy on after the fact: our AI runs on the device, so test data never leaves the clinic.","keys":["bolt","runs on the device","never leaves the clinic"]},{"ai":"Isn't that an expensive principle when your rivals hoard every record they can?","aiTr":"Rakipleriniz ellerine geçen her kaydı istiflerken bu pahalı bir ilke değil mi?","hint":"I won't pretend otherwise, but trust takes years to earn and a single breach to squander, so I see it as an investment.","keys":["won't pretend otherwise","single breach","investment"]}]}},"in-04":{"intro":"Bir yatırımcının sert ve iğneleyici sorularına soğukkanlı, zarif ve ikna edici yanıtlar veriyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Investor","en":"Forgive the cynicism, but I've seen a dozen 'AI-powered' health startups this year, and most turned out to be a pretty interface on someone else's hardware.","tr":"Kinizmimi bağışlayın ama bu yıl bir düzine 'yapay zekâ destekli' sağlık girişimi gördüm ve çoğu, başkasının donanımına giydirilmiş şık bir arayüzden ibaret çıktı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a fair suspicion, and I'd probably share it if I were in your seat.","tr":"Bu yerinde bir şüphe; sizin yerinizde olsam muhtemelen ben de aynısını düşünürdüm."},{"who":"Me","en":"The incumbents build very good audiometers, but they all presuppose an audiologist in the room, which is precisely the scarce resource.","tr":"Yerleşik şirketler çok iyi odyometreler üretiyor ama hepsi odada bir odyolog olduğunu varsayıyor; oysa kıt olan kaynak tam da bu."},{"who":"Me","en":"The consumer apps, meanwhile, are clever enough, but not one of them is certified, so no clinician can stake a diagnosis on them.","tr":"Tüketici uygulamaları ise yeterince akıllıca ama hiçbiri sertifikalı değil, dolayısıyla hiçbir klinisyen teşhisini onlara dayandıramaz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Granted, but what's to stop a large manufacturer from reverse-engineering the whole thing within a year?","tr":"Kabul, ama büyük bir üreticinin bir yıl içinde her şeyi tersine mühendislikle çözmesini ne engelleyecek?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The interface, they could copy in a month; the model, trained on thousands of real clinical tests, is another matter entirely.","tr":"Arayüzü bir ayda kopyalayabilirler; ama binlerce gerçek klinik testle eğitilmiş model bambaşka bir konu."},{"who":"Me","en":"That data isn't for sale, and by the time anyone has assembled a comparable dataset, we intend to be a few iterations further down the road.","tr":"O veri satılık değil ve biri benzer bir veri seti toplayana kadar biz birkaç sürüm daha ileride olmayı hedefliyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Size cuts both ways, too: a team of six can turn a decision around in a week that would sit in a committee elsewhere for a quarter.","tr":"Büyüklük de iki yönlü keser: altı kişilik bir ekip, başka yerde bir komitede üç ay bekleyecek bir kararı bir haftada sonuçlandırabilir."},{"who":"Investor","en":"So what's the risk you'd rather I didn't ask about?","tr":"Peki sormamamı tercih edeceğiniz risk hangisi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Certification, without question, because Class IIa approvals have an unhappy habit of running over, however meticulously one plans.","tr":"Hiç şüphesiz sertifikasyon, çünkü Sınıf IIa onaylarının, ne kadar titiz planlanırsa planlansın, uzama gibi can sıkıcı bir alışkanlığı var."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, we started well ahead of time and brought in a seasoned regulatory consultant, so a delay would hurt us but not sink us.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, işe çok erken başladık ve deneyimli bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışıyoruz; yani bir gecikme bize zarar verir ama bizi batırmaz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Well, it makes a pleasant change to hear a founder name the risk before I do.","tr":"Eh, bir kurucunun riski benden önce dile getirdiğini duymak hoş bir değişiklik."}],"vocab":[{"en":"turn out to be","tr":"...olduğu ortaya çıkmak","ex":"Most of them turned out to be just a pretty interface.","def":"to be discovered to be something in the end"},{"en":"presuppose","tr":"önceden varsaymak, gerektirmek","ex":"Classic audiometers presuppose an audiologist in the room.","def":"to depend on something already being true or available"},{"en":"stake something on","tr":"bir şeyi ... üzerine bağlamak","ex":"No clinician can stake a diagnosis on an uncertified app.","def":"to risk something important by relying on something else"},{"en":"reverse-engineer","tr":"tersine mühendislikle çözmek","ex":"A large manufacturer could try to reverse-engineer the device.","def":"to take a product apart to understand and copy how it works"},{"en":"another matter entirely","tr":"bambaşka bir konu","ex":"The interface is easy to copy; the model is another matter entirely.","def":"a completely different and usually harder case"},{"en":"further down the road","tr":"daha ileride","ex":"By then we'll be a few iterations further down the road.","def":"at a more advanced stage of progress"},{"en":"cut both ways","tr":"iki yönlü kesmek, iki tarafı da etkilemek","ex":"Size cuts both ways.","def":"to have both good and bad effects"},{"en":"turn a decision around","tr":"bir kararı hızla sonuçlandırmak","ex":"We can turn a decision around in a week.","def":"to complete and deliver a decision quickly"},{"en":"seasoned","tr":"deneyimli, işin kurdu","ex":"We brought in a seasoned regulatory consultant.","def":"having a lot of experience in a particular area"},{"en":"make a pleasant change","tr":"hoş bir değişiklik olmak","ex":"It makes a pleasant change to hear a founder admit a risk.","def":"to be nicely different from what usually happens"}],"grammar":{"title":"Fronting for contrast","tr":"Vurgu veya karşıtlık için nesne cümlenin başına alınabilir: 'The interface, they could copy in a month.' Konuşmada iki şeyi keskin biçimde karşılaştırmak için kullanılır ve çok doğal, kendinden emin bir ton verir.","examples":["The interface, they could copy in a month.","The model is another matter entirely.","That risk, I'd rather name myself."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the tone of the investor's opening remark?","options":["Openly hostile","Cynical but not unfriendly","Enthusiastic","Indifferent"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the founder say 'I'd probably share it if I were in your seat'?","options":["To admit the product is weak","To change the subject","To acknowledge the doubt before answering it"],"a":2},{"q":"According to the founder, what is the real barrier to copying?","options":["The clinical dataset behind the model","The interface design","A patent on the hardware"],"a":0},{"q":"What is implied by 'Size cuts both ways'?","options":["Small companies always lose","Being small has advantages as well as disadvantages","The team plans to grow quickly"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the investor's last line suggest?","options":["They are annoyed by the answer","They think certification is not a real risk","They are pleasantly surprised by the founder's candour"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"That's a fair ___, and I'd probably share it if I were in your seat.","a":"suspicion","hint":"şüphe"},{"s":"The model, trained on thousands of real clinical tests, is another matter ___.","a":"entirely","hint":"tamamen"},{"s":"Size cuts both ___, too.","a":"ways","hint":"iki yönlü kesmek"},{"s":"We brought in a ___ regulatory consultant.","a":"seasoned","hint":"deneyimli"}],"order":[{"a":"They could copy the interface in a month."},{"a":"That data isn't for sale."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sizin yerinizde olsam ben de bu şüpheyi taşırdım.","en":"I'd share that suspicion if I were in your seat.","keys":["share that suspicion","in your seat"]},{"tr":"Büyüklük iki yönlü keser.","en":"Size cuts both ways.","keys":["cuts both ways"]},{"tr":"Bir gecikme bize zarar verir ama bizi batırmaz.","en":"A delay would hurt us, but it wouldn't sink us.","keys":["hurt us","sink us"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Veteran investor","personaTr":"Kıdemli yatırımcı","scene":"Çok şey görmüş bir yatırımcı iğneleyici sorular soruyor; soğukkanlı ve zarif cevaplar ver.","turns":[{"ai":"Forgive the cynicism, but isn't this just another 'AI-powered' gadget?","aiTr":"Kinizmimi bağışlayın ama bu da 'yapay zekâ destekli' bir başka oyuncak değil mi?","hint":"That's a fair suspicion, but the incumbents all presuppose an audiologist in the room, and that's precisely the scarce resource we replace.","keys":["fair suspicion","presuppose","audiologist","scarce"]},{"ai":"Surely a large manufacturer could reverse-engineer this within a year?","aiTr":"Büyük bir üretici bunu bir yıl içinde tersine mühendislikle çözemez mi sanki?","hint":"The interface, perhaps; the model, trained on thousands of real clinical tests, is another matter entirely.","keys":["another matter","trained","clinical tests"]},{"ai":"And being so small, isn't that a weakness?","aiTr":"Peki bu kadar küçük olmak bir zayıflık değil mi?","hint":"Size cuts both ways: a team of six can turn a decision around in a week.","keys":["cuts both ways","team of six","turn a decision around"]},{"ai":"So what's the risk you'd rather I didn't ask about?","aiTr":"Peki sormamamı tercih edeceğiniz risk hangisi?","hint":"Certification, without question, which is why we started early and brought in a seasoned regulatory consultant.","keys":["certification","seasoned","started early"]}]}},"sc-02":{"intro":"Hibe deneyimini deneyimli bir kurucu gibi anlatıyorsun: ince ironi, ölçülü vurgu ve doğal deyimler.","text":[{"en":"There's a tendency to equate startup funding with venture capital, which rather overlooks the quiet power of a well-chosen grant.","tr":"Girişim finansmanını girişim sermayesiyle bir tutma eğilimi var; bu da iyi seçilmiş bir hibenin sessiz gücünü epey göz ardı ediyor."},{"en":"The appeal is obvious enough: nothing has to be repaid, and not a single share changes hands.","tr":"Cazibesi yeterince açık: hiçbir şeyin geri ödenmesi gerekmiyor ve tek bir hisse bile el değiştirmiyor."},{"en":"Last year, we threw our hat into the ring for a European innovation grant earmarked for health technology.","tr":"Geçen yıl sağlık teknolojisine ayrılmış bir Avrupa inovasyon hibesi için biz de yarışa girdik."},{"en":"The application was nothing if not exhaustive, demanding a forensic account of the problem, our solution, the team and every line of the budget.","tr":"Başvuru son derece kapsamlıydı; sorunun, çözümümüzün, ekibin ve bütçenin her kaleminin en ince ayrıntısına kadar açıklanmasını istiyordu."},{"en":"The impact section, which can sink otherwise strong bids, was arguably our easiest, since roughly one in five people lives with some degree of hearing loss.","tr":"Aslında güçlü başvuruları bile batırabilen etki bölümü belki de en kolayımızdı, çünkü yaklaşık her beş kişiden biri bir derece işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor."},{"en":"What followed was a four-month review, which tested our patience rather more than we let on.","tr":"Ardından dört aylık bir değerlendirme geldi; bu süreç sabrımızı belli ettiğimizden çok daha fazla sınadı."},{"en":"We were then invited to defend the proposal before a jury that was courteous but by no means a soft touch.","tr":"Sonra teklifimizi nazik ama kesinlikle kolay ikna edilmeyen bir jüri önünde savunmaya davet edildik."},{"en":"In the end, we secured 250,000 euros, ring-fenced for research and clinical validation, which is precisely where the risk lay.","tr":"Sonunda araştırma ve klinik doğrulamaya ayrılmış 250.000 euroyu aldık; zaten risk de tam olarak oradaydı."},{"en":"Had we raised that sum from investors at such an early stage, the dilution would have been painful, to put it mildly.","tr":"O tutarı bu kadar erken bir aşamada yatırımcılardan toplasaydık, hisse sulanması en hafif deyimiyle acı verici olurdu."},{"en":"Grants are, admittedly, a slog; by the same token, few instruments de-risk early science on such generous terms.","tr":"Hibeler kabul etmek gerek ki meşakkatlidir; ama aynı mantıkla, erken aşama bilimin riskini bu kadar cömert koşullarla azaltan araç azdır."}],"vocab":[{"en":"equate X with Y","tr":"X'i Y ile bir tutmak","ex":"People often equate startup funding with venture capital.","def":"to think that one thing is the same as another"},{"en":"throw your hat into the ring","tr":"yarışa girmek, aday olmak","ex":"We threw our hat into the ring for a European grant.","def":"to enter a competition or announce you want to be considered"},{"en":"nothing if not","tr":"son derece, tam anlamıyla","ex":"The application was nothing if not exhaustive.","def":"used to emphasise that someone or something has a quality to a great degree"},{"en":"a forensic account","tr":"en ince ayrıntısına kadar açıklama","ex":"The jury wanted a forensic account of the budget.","def":"an extremely detailed and careful explanation"},{"en":"sink a bid","tr":"bir başvuruyu batırmak","ex":"A weak impact section can sink a bid.","def":"to cause an application or offer to fail"},{"en":"more than we let on","tr":"belli ettiğimizden daha fazla","ex":"The wait worried us more than we let on.","def":"to a greater degree than we showed to other people"},{"en":"no soft touch","tr":"kolay ikna edilir biri değil","ex":"The jury was polite but by no means a soft touch.","def":"not someone who is easily persuaded or who gives things easily"},{"en":"to put it mildly","tr":"en hafif deyimiyle","ex":"The dilution would have been painful, to put it mildly.","def":"used to say the reality is much worse than your words suggest"},{"en":"dilution","tr":"hisse sulanması","ex":"Early dilution can be very costly for founders.","def":"the reduction in the owners' share when new shares are given to investors"},{"en":"by the same token","tr":"aynı mantıkla","ex":"By the same token, few instruments are so generous.","def":"for the same reason; in the same way"}],"grammar":{"title":"Understatement and emphasis","tr":"C2 düzeyinde vurgu çoğu zaman tersinden yapılır: 'nothing if not' (son derece), 'by no means' (asla), 'to put it mildly' (en hafif deyimiyle), 'rather more than' (çok daha fazla). Abartmadan güçlü bir izlenim bırakır.","examples":["The application was nothing if not exhaustive.","The jury was by no means a soft touch.","The dilution would have been painful, to put it mildly."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the writer suggest people tend to overlook?","options":["The value of grants as a funding source","The risks of venture capital","The cost of audiologists"],"a":0},{"q":"Why was the impact section \"arguably our easiest\"?","options":["The jury already knew the product","The scale of hearing loss made the case compelling","They reused another team's bid"],"a":1},{"q":"What does \"tested our patience rather more than we let on\" imply?","options":["The team complained loudly","The team forgot about the application","The team was more anxious than it showed"],"a":2},{"q":"How does the writer characterise the jury?","options":["Hostile and rude","Friendly and easy to persuade","Disorganised","Polite but demanding"],"a":3},{"q":"What is the tone of \"painful, to put it mildly\"?","options":["Enthusiastic about investors","Understated, implying the cost would have been severe","Purely technical"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"We threw our hat into the ___ for a European innovation grant.","a":"ring","hint":"yarış (ringe şapka atmak)"},{"s":"The application was nothing ___ not exhaustive.","a":"if","hint":"son derece (kalıp)"},{"s":"The jury was by no means a soft ___.","a":"touch","hint":"kolay lokma"},{"s":"The dilution would have been painful, to put it ___.","a":"mildly","hint":"en hafif deyimiyle"}],"order":[{"a":"Not a single share changes hands."},{"a":"The application was nothing if not exhaustive."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Hiçbir şeyin geri ödenmesi gerekmiyor.","en":"Nothing has to be repaid.","keys":["nothing","repaid"]},{"tr":"Jüri nazikti ama kesinlikle kolay ikna edilecek biri değildi.","en":"The jury was courteous but by no means a soft touch.","keys":["courteous","by no means","soft touch"]},{"tr":"Hisse sulanması, en hafif deyimiyle, acı verici olurdu.","en":"The dilution would have been painful, to put it mildly.","keys":["dilution","to put it mildly"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Grant jury member","personaTr":"Hibe jürisi üyesi","scene":"Şüpheci bir jüri üyesi teklifinin yenilikçiliğini ve gerekliliğini sorguluyor. Zarif ama sağlam cevaplar ver.","turns":[{"ai":"Hearing screening is hardly a new idea. What, precisely, is innovative here?","aiTr":"İşitme taraması pek yeni bir fikir sayılmaz. Burada tam olarak yenilikçi olan ne?","hint":"The idea isn't new, granted, but an autonomous test that needs no expert in the room and runs its AI entirely on the device very much is.","keys":["granted","no expert","on the device"]},{"ai":"Your impact claims are bold. Aren't you overstating the need?","aiTr":"Etki iddialarınız cüretkâr. İhtiyacı abartmıyor musunuz?","hint":"If anything, we're understating it: roughly one in five people has some hearing loss, and in small towns the wait for an audiologist runs to months.","keys":["if anything","one in five","months"]},{"ai":"Two hundred and fifty thousand euros is no small sum. Why should it come from the public purse?","aiTr":"İki yüz elli bin euro küçük bir para değil. Neden kamu kaynağından gelsin?","hint":"Because it would de-risk the science at precisely the stage where private investors are most reluctant to step in.","keys":["de-risk","precisely","reluctant"]},{"ai":"And if we said no, would the project survive?","aiTr":"Peki hayır dersek proje ayakta kalır mı?","hint":"It would survive, but more slowly and at the cost of considerable dilution, which, frankly, is a poor trade for something this close to the clinic.","keys":["survive","dilution","frankly"]}]}},"st-05":{"intro":"Zor bir müşteri şikayetini nasıl güvene dönüştürdüğünü, ince bir dil ve hafif ironiyle anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Yesterday's call from a hospital in Izmir, one of our paying customers, was, to put it mildly, not a social one.","tr":"Ücret ödeyen müşterilerimizden biri olan İzmir'deki bir hastaneden dün gelen telefon, en hafif deyimiyle, bir hal hatır sohbeti değildi."},{"en":"Their audiometer had frozen halfway through a test, leaving a blank screen, a bemused patient in headphones and a doctor with a waiting room full of people.","tr":"Odyometreleri bir testin ortasında donmuştu; ortada boş bir ekran, kulaklıklarıyla şaşkın bir hasta ve bekleme salonu dolu bir doktor vardı."},{"en":"Her frustration was entirely justified, and the last thing she needed was a supplier getting defensive.","tr":"Hayal kırıklığı tamamen haklıydı ve ihtiyacı olan son şey savunmaya geçen bir tedarikçiydi."},{"en":"So I apologised without caveats and thanked her for telling us straight away, which is far more than many customers bother to do.","tr":"Bu yüzden hiçbir 'ama' eklemeden özür diledim ve bize hemen haber verdiği için teşekkür ettim; birçok müşteri bu zahmete bile girmez."},{"en":"That said, an apology only buys you so much goodwill, and what she really wanted was her device back.","tr":"Yine de bir özür ancak bir yere kadar iyi niyet kazandırır; onun asıl istediği cihazına yeniden kavuşmaktı."},{"en":"A handful of pointed questions was enough to establish that the culprit was a software bug rather than anything physical.","tr":"Birkaç yerinde soru, sorunun kaynağının fiziksel bir şey değil, bir yazılım hatası olduğunu saptamaya yetti."},{"en":"Our engineer pushed a fix remotely, and within two hours the device was back up and running.","tr":"Mühendisimiz uzaktan bir düzeltme gönderdi ve iki saat içinde cihaz yeniden çalışır hâle geldi."},{"en":"I then called her back myself, partly to confirm everything was in order and partly because a follow-up says more than any apology.","tr":"Sonra onu bizzat geri aradım; kısmen her şeyin yolunda olduğunu teyit etmek, kısmen de bir takip araması her özürden daha çok şey söylediği için."},{"en":"It's tempting to treat a complaint as a verdict on the relationship.","tr":"Bir şikayeti ilişki hakkında verilmiş bir hüküm gibi görmek cazip gelir."},{"en":"In my experience, it is more of a stress test.","tr":"Benim deneyimime göre, daha çok bir stres testidir."},{"en":"Handled with candour and speed, it can leave a customer trusting you rather more than if nothing had gone wrong at all.","tr":"Açık sözlülük ve hızla ele alındığında, müşterinin size hiçbir şey ters gitmemiş olmasından bile daha fazla güvenmesini sağlayabilir."},{"en":"By the same token, a complaint brushed aside rarely stays a single complaint for long.","tr":"Aynı şekilde, geçiştirilen bir şikayet nadiren uzun süre tek bir şikayet olarak kalır."}],"vocab":[{"en":"to put it mildly","tr":"en hafif deyimiyle","ex":"The call was, to put it mildly, not a social one.","def":"used to say that the reality is much stronger or worse than your words"},{"en":"get defensive","tr":"savunmaya geçmek","ex":"The worst thing a supplier can do is get defensive.","def":"to react to criticism by protecting yourself instead of listening"},{"en":"without caveats","tr":"çekince koymadan, 'ama' demeden","ex":"I apologised without caveats.","def":"with no conditions or excuses added"},{"en":"buy goodwill","tr":"iyi niyet kazandırmak","ex":"An apology only buys you so much goodwill.","def":"to create positive feeling and trust"},{"en":"pointed question","tr":"yerinde, nokta atışı soru","ex":"A few pointed questions were enough.","def":"a direct question aimed at a specific point"},{"en":"the culprit","tr":"suçlu, sorunun kaynağı","ex":"The culprit turned out to be a software bug.","def":"the thing responsible for a problem"},{"en":"push a fix","tr":"(uzaktan) düzeltme göndermek","ex":"Our engineer pushed a fix remotely.","def":"to send corrected software to a device from a distance"},{"en":"a verdict on","tr":"...hakkında hüküm","ex":"A complaint is not a verdict on the relationship.","def":"a final judgement about something"},{"en":"with candour","tr":"açık sözlülükle","ex":"Handle complaints with candour and speed.","def":"in an honest and open way"},{"en":"brush aside","tr":"geçiştirmek","ex":"A complaint brushed aside rarely stays small.","def":"to ignore something or treat it as unimportant"}],"grammar":{"title":"Nuanced hedging: that said, in my experience, rather more","tr":"C2'de görüşünü kesin hükümler yerine incelikli ifadelerle verirsin. 'That said' önceki fikri dengeler, 'in my experience' iddiayı kişisel deneyime bağlar, 'rather more' vurguyu ölçülü tutar.","examples":["That said, an apology only buys you so much goodwill.","In my experience, it is more of a stress test.","It can leave a customer trusting you rather more than before."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does 'not a social one' tell us about the call?","options":["It was a sales call","It was very short","It was a complaint, not a friendly chat"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention that many customers don't bother to report problems?","options":["To criticise the doctor","To show that her call was actually valuable","To explain why the bug was missed"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'an apology only buys you so much goodwill' imply?","options":["Words help, but the customer mainly needs the problem fixed","Apologies are useless","The company should offer a discount"],"a":0},{"q":"How was the problem solved?","options":["A new device was delivered","An engineer visited the hospital","A fix was pushed remotely","The doctor restarted it herself"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the speaker's view of complaints?","options":["They are a final verdict on the relationship","They should always go to the engineers","They are rare in medical technology","They are a stress test that can build trust"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"The call was, to put it ___, not a social one.","a":"mildly","hint":"en hafif deyimiyle"},{"s":"I apologised without ___ and thanked her.","a":"caveats","hint":"çekince"},{"s":"The ___ turned out to be a software bug.","a":"culprit","hint":"sorunun kaynağı"},{"s":"A complaint ___ aside rarely stays a single complaint.","a":"brushed","hint":"geçiştirilen"}],"order":[{"a":"An apology only buys you so much goodwill."},{"a":"In my experience it is more of a stress test."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bir özür ancak bir yere kadar iyi niyet kazandırır.","en":"An apology only buys you so much goodwill.","keys":["apology","so much goodwill"]},{"tr":"Sorunun kaynağı bir yazılım hatasıydı.","en":"The culprit was a software bug.","keys":["culprit","software bug"]},{"tr":"Şikayet, ilişki hakkında bir hüküm değildir.","en":"A complaint is not a verdict on the relationship.","keys":["verdict on","relationship"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Angry doctor","personaTr":"Kızgın doktor","scene":"İzmir'deki bir hastanenin deneyimli doktoru, test ortasında donan cihaz yüzünden sert ve alaycı bir dille arıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Frankly, I'm beginning to wonder why we didn't just stick with our old audiometer, because yours has just died on me mid-test.","aiTr":"Açıkçası eski odyometremizle neden devam etmediğimizi sorgulamaya başladım; sizinki test ortasında öylece kapandı.","hint":"That's entirely fair, and I'm sorry, no caveats. I'm grateful you called us straight away rather than quietly giving up on us.","keys":["sorry","grateful","straight away"]},{"ai":"Black screen, won't reboot, patient still sitting there in headphones, so what are we looking at?","aiTr":"Siyah ekran, yeniden açılmıyor, hasta hâlâ kulaklıklarla oturuyor; neyle karşı karşıyayız?","hint":"Let me ask a couple of quick questions, but from what you're describing, the culprit is almost certainly software rather than hardware.","keys":["culprit","software","hardware"]},{"ai":"And that helps me how, exactly, with a waiting room full of people?","aiTr":"Bekleme salonu dolu biriyken bu bana tam olarak nasıl yardımcı oluyor?","hint":"It means we don't need to collect anything: our engineer can push a fix remotely, and you should be back up and running within two hours.","keys":["push a fix","remotely","within two hours"]},{"ai":"I'll hold you to that, but I'd rather not be having this conversation again next month.","aiTr":"Sözünüzü tutmanızı bekleyeceğim; ama bu konuşmayı gelecek ay tekrar yapmak istemem.","hint":"Nor would I. Once we've got to the bottom of it, I'll walk you through what went wrong and what we've changed.","keys":["bottom of it","walk you through","went wrong"]}]}},"li-03":{"intro":"Kuruculuğun en sinsi riski olan tükenmişliği ve enerjiyi stratejik bir kaynak olarak yönetmeyi olgun, incelikli bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"My first year as a founder was, in hindsight, an exercise in self-sabotage: fourteen-hour days, five hours' sleep, and a quiet pride in both.","tr":"Geriye dönüp bakınca, kurucu olarak ilk yılım kendi kendimi baltalamaktan ibaretti: on dört saatlik günler, beş saatlik uyku ve ikisiyle de gizliden gizliye övünmek."},{"who":"Me","en":"The irony, of course, is that the exhaustion I wore as a badge of honour was steadily eroding the very judgement the company depended on.","tr":"İşin ironisi elbette şu: gurur nişanı gibi taşıdığım yorgunluk, şirketin tam da dayandığı muhakememi yavaş yavaş aşındırıyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"A tired brain doesn't simply slow down; it quietly trades the right answer for the easy one, and it rarely tells you it's doing so.","tr":"Yorgun bir beyin sadece yavaşlamaz; doğru cevabı sessizce kolay olanla takas eder ve bunu yaptığını size nadiren belli eder."},{"who":"Me","en":"It took a run of poor decisions for the penny to drop: energy, not time, was the scarce resource.","tr":"Jetonun düşmesi için art arda birkaç kötü karar gerekti: kıt olan kaynak zaman değil, enerjiydi."},{"who":"Me","en":"These days, I live by three rules that I'd be loath to give up.","tr":"Bugünlerde, bırakmaya hiç gönlümün olmayacağı üç kurala göre yaşıyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"Sleep comes first, and I guard at least seven hours of it jealously, which means nothing in my inbox gets a reply after 10 pm.","tr":"Önce uyku gelir ve en az yedi saatini kıskançlıkla korurum; bu da gece 10'dan sonra gelen kutumdaki hiçbir şeye cevap verilmemesi demek."},{"who":"Me","en":"My most important task gets the best of me, first thing in the morning, before meetings have a chance to fragment the day.","tr":"En önemli işim, toplantılar günü paramparça etme fırsatı bulmadan, sabah ilk iş olarak en iyi halimi alır."},{"who":"Me","en":"And every day, come rain or shine, I walk for thirty minutes, which, rather unglamorously, is where many of my best ideas tend to turn up.","tr":"Ve her gün, yağmur çamur demeden otuz dakika yürürüm; pek de göz alıcı olmasa da en iyi fikirlerimin çoğu genellikle orada ortaya çıkar."},{"who":"Me","en":"None of this is revolutionary, admittedly; the hard part is sticking to it when a deadline is breathing down your neck.","tr":"Kabul etmek gerekir ki bunların hiçbiri devrim niteliğinde değil; zor olan, bir teslim tarihi ensenizdeyken bunlara sadık kalmak."},{"who":"Me","en":"That said, I've come to see rest less as an indulgence than as part of the job.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, dinlenmeyi bir keyiften çok işin bir parçası olarak görmeye başladım."},{"who":"Me","en":"A startup is a marathon, not a sprint, and a founder who burns out rarely goes down alone; the company tends to follow.","tr":"Girişim bir sprint değil, maratondur ve tükenen bir kurucu nadiren tek başına batar; şirket de genellikle peşinden gider."}],"vocab":[{"en":"in hindsight","tr":"geriye dönüp bakınca","ex":"In hindsight, I should have slept more.","def":"when looking back at the past with the knowledge you have now"},{"en":"self-sabotage","tr":"kendi kendini baltalama","ex":"Working without sleep was a form of self-sabotage.","def":"behaviour that damages your own success"},{"en":"a badge of honour","tr":"gurur nişanı","ex":"I wore exhaustion as a badge of honour.","def":"something people are proud of, even if it is not good for them"},{"en":"erode","tr":"aşındırmak","ex":"Lack of sleep was eroding my judgement.","def":"to slowly weaken or destroy something"},{"en":"the penny drops","tr":"jeton düşmek","ex":"It took months for the penny to drop.","def":"someone finally understands something"},{"en":"be loath to","tr":"...e hiç gönlü olmamak","ex":"I'd be loath to give up my morning routine.","def":"to be very unwilling to do something"},{"en":"guard jealously","tr":"kıskançlıkla korumak","ex":"I guard my sleep jealously.","def":"to protect something very carefully and not let others take it"},{"en":"fragment","tr":"parçalamak, bölmek","ex":"Too many meetings fragment the day.","def":"to break something into small, separate parts"},{"en":"breathe down your neck","tr":"ensende olmak","ex":"A deadline is breathing down my neck.","def":"to be very close and put you under pressure"},{"en":"indulgence","tr":"keyif, kendini şımartma","ex":"Rest is not an indulgence.","def":"something you allow yourself for pleasure rather than need"}],"grammar":{"title":"Concessive hedging: admittedly, of course, that said","tr":"C2 düzeyinde konuşmacı karşı görüşü kabul ederek ikna eder: 'admittedly', 'of course', 'that said' bir noktayı teslim edip ardından asıl fikri öne çıkarır. 'Less as X than as Y' yapısı ise bir şeyi zarifçe yeniden tanımlar.","examples":["None of this is revolutionary, admittedly.","The irony, of course, is that the exhaustion was eroding my judgement.","That said, I've come to see rest less as an indulgence than as part of the job."]},"questions":[{"q":"How did the founder feel about the long hours at the time?","options":["Secretly ashamed","Quietly proud","Openly angry","Completely indifferent"],"a":1},{"q":"What is 'the irony' the founder refers to?","options":["The exhaustion they were proud of was damaging the judgement the company needed","Working less made the company grow faster","Investors preferred tired founders"],"a":0},{"q":"What does 'for the penny to drop' suggest about the realisation?","options":["It came on the very first day","It was suggested by an investor","It came only after repeated mistakes"],"a":2},{"q":"What is the effect of 'rather unglamorously'?","options":["It criticises other founders","It shows the founder dislikes walking","It suggests the walks are a secret","It adds a self-deprecating touch by admitting the habit is ordinary"],"a":3},{"q":"What does the founder imply with 'the hard part is sticking to it'?","options":["The rules are easy to understand but hard to keep under pressure","The rules are too complicated","Deadlines should be ignored"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"In ___, my first year was an exercise in self-sabotage.","a":"hindsight","hint":"geriye dönüp bakınca"},{"s":"I wore exhaustion as a badge of ___.","a":"honour","hint":"onur"},{"s":"It took a run of poor decisions for the ___ to drop.","a":"penny","hint":"jeton (deyim)"},{"s":"These are rules I'd be ___ to give up.","a":"loath","hint":"gönülsüz"}],"order":[{"a":"Sleep comes first and I guard it jealously."},{"a":"The hard part is sticking to it."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Geriye dönüp bakınca, ilk yılım kendi kendimi baltalamaktan ibaretti.","en":"In hindsight, my first year was an exercise in self-sabotage.","keys":["in hindsight","self-sabotage"]},{"tr":"Bununla birlikte, dinlenmeyi bir keyiften çok işin bir parçası olarak görmeye başladım.","en":"That said, I've come to see rest less as an indulgence than as part of the job.","keys":["that said","indulgence","part of the job"]},{"tr":"Zor olan, bir teslim tarihi ensendeyken buna sadık kalmak.","en":"The hard part is sticking to it when a deadline is breathing down your neck.","keys":["sticking to it","breathing down your neck"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Young founder","personaTr":"Genç kurucu","scene":"Yatırım turu kapatmaya çalışan, tükenmiş ama yavaşlamayı yenilgi sayan genç bir kurucuyla konuşuyorsun. Deneyiminle onu ikna etmelisin.","turns":[{"ai":"I'll be honest, I'm running on empty, but easing off feels like an admission of defeat.","aiTr":"Dürüst olayım, takatim kalmadı ama yavaşlamak yenilgiyi kabul etmek gibi geliyor.","hint":"I wore exhaustion as a badge of honour too, but in hindsight it was quietly eroding my judgement.","keys":["badge of honour","in hindsight","eroding","judgement"]},{"ai":"Fine, but with a round to close, sleep feels like a luxury I can't afford.","aiTr":"Peki, ama kapatmam gereken bir yatırım turu varken uyku, karşılayamayacağım bir lüks gibi geliyor.","hint":"I'd argue it's the opposite: seven hours is precisely what keeps you from making poor calls in the negotiation.","keys":["seven hours","poor calls","the opposite"]},{"ai":"And when the calendar is wall-to-wall meetings?","aiTr":"Peki takvim baştan sona toplantılarla doluyken?","hint":"Then ring-fence the first hours of the morning for whatever matters most, before the meetings fragment the day.","keys":["ring-fence","morning","matters most","fragment"]},{"ai":"Is there any habit you'd be loath to give up?","aiTr":"Bırakmaya hiç gönlün olmayacak bir alışkanlık var mı?","hint":"My thirty-minute walk, come rain or shine; rather unglamorously, that's where many of my best ideas turn up.","keys":["walk","come rain or shine","best ideas"]}]}}};
